\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18They are fed up\u8217\'20\'19: US labor on the march in 2021 after years of decline\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,251 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 December 2021\par 17:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers went on strike and pushed union drives in record numbers after corporations made giant pandemic profits\par \par \uc2 In 2021 workers appear to have had enough.\par \par \uc2 Amid constant claims from some industries of labor shortages as the economy recovers from Covid-19 shutdowns, workers have been pushing employers and elected officials to raise wages, improve working conditions and benefits such as paid sick leave through {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/2021/nov/16/school-bus-drivers-protest-shortages-pay-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walkouts}}}\uc2 , protests, rallies and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/01/us-labor-unrest-unions-strikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  strikes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The last few months of 2021 saw workers quit at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/business/job-labor-quit-october.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record or near record rates}}}\uc2 , while an uptick of strikes occurred around the US in October and November 2021.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been traveling a lot to picket lines all over the country in the last couple of months, been in so many different states and across all industries. But the one thing that\u8217\'20\'19s been really consistent is the sentiment of the working people who are out there taking the risks is that they are absolutely fed up,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Liz Shuler\uc2 , president of the AFL-CIO, the main union federation in the US.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of workers went on strike in 2021 at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2021/07/26/frito-lay-strike-topeka/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Frito-Lay}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/23/nabisco-factory-workers-striking"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nabisco}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/oct/07/kelloggs-workers-strike-offshore-jobs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/14/john-deere-workers-strike-contract-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 John Deere}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/business-strikes-17c318d1250ebfca9f597c5601af820b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Volvo}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.labornotes.org/blogs/2021/10/two-thousand-california-cwa-members-strike-telecoms-corp-frontier-communications"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Frontier Communications}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/30/nyregion/nyu-strike.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York University}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/09/columbia-university-student-worker-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Columbia University}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thecrimson.com/article/2021/11/9/hgsu-threatens-another-strike/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harvard}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seattletimes.com/business/real-estate/washington-carpenters-approve-contract-deal-ending-strike-that-slowed-construction-work/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 carpenters }}}\uc2  in the Pacific north-west, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/jul/30/us-nurses-strike-covid-coronavirus-conditions-understaffing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hospitals}}}\uc2 , airports and at coalmines in Alabama, while workers at several fast-food and retail chains including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Business/wireStory/us-mcdonalds-workers-strike-protest-workplace-harassment-80796624"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.charlotteobserver.com/news/business/article256140907.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Walmart}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yourdailyjournal.com/news/100781/wadesboro-wendys-staff-quits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wendy\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ktvu.com/news/bay-area-fast-food-workers-join-statewide-strike-to-demand-better-conditions-safety-standards"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Burger King}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://portcitydaily.com/eateries/2021/08/14/bo-time-no-time-go-time-monkey-junction-bojangles-staff-walks-out-temporarily-shutters-store/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bojangles}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fox40.com/news/local-news/north-highlands-jack-in-the-box-workers-go-on-strike-claiming-184k-due-in-back-pay/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jack in the Box}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.1011now.com/2021/08/08/employees-family-dollar-off-46th-huntington-quit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Family Dollar}}}\uc2 , held walkouts or short-term strikes.\par \par \uc2 Shuler believes that the hardships of the pandemic \u8211\'20\'13 when so much focus was put on the sacrifices of workers in often manual jobs that were deemed essential \u8211\'20\'13 has sparked a reawakening of labor politics in America, especially as some companies have tried to go back to business as usual.\par \par \uc2 Shuler added: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I was walking the line with those Nabisco workers, and \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  workers, I kept thinking about all of them in the plant, making Oreos and the Ritz crackers, while the rest of us were inside consuming those. Those are the folks that really made the sacrifices and the whole time, they were told that they were essential. Then they go to the bargaining table, and they\u8217\'20\'19re basically disposable because the companies continued to profit through the pandemic and then say, \u8216\'20\'18Thanks, but we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to compensate you, we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to protect you, we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to value and reward you for making those sacrifices.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One of the year\u8217\'20\'19s most important strikes is playing out in the deep south where about 1,100 coalminers at \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  in Alabama have been on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/01/striking-coalminers-alabama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike}}}\uc2  since 1 April, as workers fight for better wages after accepting concessions in their previous union contract.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe past eight months have been some of the hardest times of our lives. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think any of us imagined the strike would be going into its ninth month with no end in sight, but I\u8217\'20\'19m proud of our resolve,\u8221\'20\'1D said James Traweek, a miner who has worked for four years at \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  in Brookwood, Alabama.\par \par \uc2 Other strikes have broken records.\par \par \uc2 At the \uc2 Tenet Healthcare\uc2 -owned St Vincent hospital in Worcester, Massachusetts, about 700 nurses have been on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/jul/30/us-nurses-strike-covid-coronavirus-conditions-understaffing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike}}}\uc2  since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcboston.com/news/local/as-nurses-strike-stretches-on-st-vincent-hospital-moves-to-implement-recent-contract-offer/2518065/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 8 March}}}\uc2  over understaffing and cuts at the hospital before and during the pandemic, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wbur.org/news/2021/08/31/st-vincent-nurse-strike-becomes-longest-in-mass-history#:~:text=Vincent%20Hospital%20in%20Worcester%20is,in%20Fitchburg%20in%20the%201980s."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  longest strike in Massachusetts\u8217\'20\'19 history}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Tenet Healthcare\uc2  has sought to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.masslive.com/politics/2021/08/saint-vincent-hospital-hires-100-permanent-replacement-nurses-as-strike-continues.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 permanently replace }}}\uc2  nurses on strike as the hospital {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.masslive.com/worcester/2021/11/state-threatens-to-fine-saint-vincent-hospital-in-worcester-if-decision-regarding-closed-beds-isnt-reached.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faces fines}}}\uc2  from the state for closing down inpatient behavioral health beds due to the strike. An agreement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.masslive.com/worcester/2021/10/saint-vincent-hospital-exercises-right-to-give-striking-nurses-last-offer-same-deal-presented-in-august-as-mna-files-unfair-labor-practices-charge.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fell through}}}\uc2  in August over \uc2 Tenet Healthcare\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s return to work agreement that would have prevented some nurses from returning to their previous positions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSaint Vincent hospital nurses\u8217\'20\'19 fight has now become all of labor\u8217\'20\'19s fight,\u8221\'20\'1D said Marlena. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a big red flag for all of labor and all of humanity that if you stand up for what you believe in on principle and stand up for patients and you stand up for one another as workers, \uc2 Tenet Healthcare\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s strategy is that you can be replaced and will be punished for that. That\u8217\'20\'19s very dangerous, this strategy trying to diminish our union rights instead of coming to a settlement, trying to intimidate nurses to cross a picket line.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On 18 December, a tentative agreement was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.telegram.com/story/news/2021/12/17/st-vincent-hospital-nurses-reach-tentative-agreement-end-strike-worcester/8946921002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached}}}\uc2  after the US secretary of labor, Marty Walsh, served as mediator in the final negotiating session, which will end the strike if approved by the nurses.\par \par \uc2 The Labor Action tracker at Cornell University Institute of Labor Relations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://striketracker.ilr.cornell.edu/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 documented}}}\uc2  346 strike locations in 2021 as of 10 December. Johnnie Kallas, the project director , attributed an uptick in strikes in October and November to increased leverage of workers in a labor market where workers are in high demand and burnout of workers who have continued working through the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLabor market conditions can provide workers with more leverage, but strikes don\u8217\'20\'19t just automatically happen. They often require deep organizing and always require incredible sacrifice,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kallas.\par \par \uc2 Unionization rates in the US have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2021/02/05/union-enrollment-declined-for-decades-but-union-workers-still-earn-more.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined}}}\uc2  over the past few decades, but several union organizing efforts were launched in 2021 in response to pandemic working conditions, while labor leaders and unions continue pushing for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/pro-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 labor law reforms}}}\uc2  to rein in anti-union employers and facilitate US workers\u8217\'20\'19 ability to organize unions and engage in collective bargaining.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unionelections.org/data/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unionelections.org}}}\uc2 , 890 union elections in the private sector were held in the US in 2021 as of 11 December, with 573 resulting in a new union certification. Union election rates and union density in the US have been in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ericdirnbach.medium.com/decline-and-fall-union-election-trends-and-the-failing-nlrb-strategy-1e2263f3f59b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 downward decline}}}\uc2  over the past several decades, though approval of labor unions in the US is at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/354455/approval-labor-unions-highest-point-1965.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 68%}}}\uc2  according to a September Gallup poll.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we see any changes, it will be next year. Between the tight labor market and the high profile coverage of the strikes and recent elections, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  for example, I\u8217\'20\'19d expect to see some increase,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kevin Reuning, assistant professor of Political Science at \uc2 Miami University in Oxford\uc2 , Ohio, who manages the unionelections.org website.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers in Bessemer, Alabama, attempted to form the \uc2 first union\uc2  at the retail giant in the spring and though the union lost the election, the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/11/29/business/amazon-bessemer-alabama-election.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered}}}\uc2  a new election to be held due to \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s anti-union misconduct. At the same time New York\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ag.ny.gov/press-release/2021/attorney-general-james-seeks-emergency-relief-protect-rights-and-safety-amazon#:~:text=NEW%20YORK%20%E2%80%93%20In%20continuing%20her,warehouses%20that%20are%20threatening%20workers."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pressuring}}}\uc2 Amazon\uc2  to reinstate a fired employee and improve safety protections amid a union organizing drive led by the terminated employee, Chris Smalls, in Staten Island.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers in Buffalo, New York, also won a historic union election on 9 December, forming the \uc2 first union\uc2  at a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  corporate store in the US. A second branch is likely to have won their union election after challenged ballots are resolved and three more stores are set to hold union elections in Buffalo, New York, and another in Arizona. With the union victory {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-12-09/starbucks-workers-vote-to-unionize-in-labor-board-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spurring optimism}}}\uc2 , it could lead to more stores requesting to unionize.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a major victory,\u8221\'20\'1D said Brian Murray, a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  barista in the Buffalo area and one of the organizers with Starbucks Workers United. \u8220\'20\'1CI think our real fight will be now getting a first contract and hopefully having them recognize the right to organize, but with these wins I\u8217\'20\'19m sure we\u8217\'20\'19ll see more workers organizing nationwide in the near future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211221ehcl00105\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
