\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 FBI\uc2  searches for \uc2 Jimmy Hoffa\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s body in New Jersey landfill after deathbed tip\b0\par\par\uc2 Edward Helmore \par \uc2 606 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 November 2021\par 17:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  confirms search for the Teamster boss, who disappeared in July 1975, had begun again after a 2020 deathbed tip from landfill worker\par \par \uc2 A half-century American fixation on the whereabouts of the remains of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/category/teamsters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters}}}\uc2  boss \uc2 Jimmy Hoffa\uc2  has finally led investigators to a landfill in New Jersey.\par \par \uc2 The area of suspicion is on a Little League diamond on the landfill beneath the General Pulaski Skyway, a three-mile bridge that arches over a cinematically criminal evocative expanse of industrial wasteland and marshes west of Manhattan \u8211\'20\'13 one that once featured in marketing for the Sopranos TV show.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  confirmed that its search for the Teamster boss, who disappeared in July 1975 after he showed up for a meeting with two mob bosses in Michigan, had begun anew after a March 2020 deathbed tip from landfill worker Frank Cappola, who had told a friend that his father confessed he\u8217\'20\'19 had been ordered by unidentified men to bury Hoffa\u8217\'20\'19s body in a steel drum.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the FBI told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/11/18/nyregion/jimmy-hoffa-fbi-investigation.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2  that agents from the bureau\u8217\'20\'19s Detroit and Newark offices had carried out a site visit on the Jersey City side of the bridge late last month.\par \par \uc2 The location of the search is freighted with cinematic references: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mJpNmYeooQE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the opening sequences}}}\uc2  of The Sopranos depicts a car ride through the area, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sopranos-locations.com/season-0/episode-0/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including shots}}}\uc2  of the Pulaski; in 2019, Martin Scorsese\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/category/the-irishman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Irishman}}}\uc2 , starring Robert De Niro and Al Pacino, offered a fictionalized account of Hoffa\u8217\'20\'19s disappearance from the perspective of Mafia hitman Frank Sheeran.\par \par \uc2 While the \uc2 FBI\uc2  did not explicitly name Hoffa in its statement, saying only that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cunable to provide any additional information\u8221\'20\'1D, sources at the bureau confirmed to NBC that the effort at the site was tied to Hoffa\u8217\'20\'19s disappearance.\par \par \uc2 The search comes as the authorities attempt to address some of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most enduring crime mysteries and miscarriages of justice.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Cyrus Vance\uc2 , said that decisions made by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and its long-serving director J Edgar Hoover had led to the false convictions of two men for the assassination of civil rights leader Malcolm X.\par \par \uc2 The search for Hoffa\u8217\'20\'19s remains has been long and circuitous. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  interrogated union leaders and Mob bosses and henchmen and began receiving tips that his body was buried in New Jersey landfill hundreds of miles from where he was abducted, found nothing, and filed the tips.\par \par \uc2 Years later, agents searched various locations in Michigan, including a farm, a driveway and beneath a swimming pool. Back in New Jersey, where by reputation Italian-American Mafiosi still hold sway over carting and trucking, criminal folklore has focused on the nearby Giants Stadium, which was under construction at the time of Hoffa\u8217\'20\'19s disappearance.\par \par \uc2 But the theory advanced by The Irishman \u8211\'20\'13 that Hoffa had been murdered and incinerated \u8211\'20\'13 has largely been rejected by Hoffa experts. Dan Moldea, author of several books on Hoffa\u8217\'20\'19s disappearance, told the Times that the New Jersey site is \u8220\'20\'1C100%\u8221\'20\'1D credible.\par \par \uc2 In July, Moldea published an article in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.deadlinedetroit.com/articles/25860/moldea_is_this_enough_evidence_to_obtain_a_search_warrant_for_jimmy_hoffa_s_grave"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Detroit Deadline}}}\uc2  placing Hoffa\u8217\'20\'19s unmarked grave at a 53-acre landfill in Jersey City, New Jersey. He pointed to an \uc2 FBI\uc2  report four months after Hoffa disappeared that cited a visit Teamster boss, convicted murderer and \uc2 FBI{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/1976/01/31/archives/new-jersey-convict-is-called-informer-on-hoffa-suspects.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 informant}}}\uc2  Ralph Picardo had received from Steve Andretta, an alleged Hoffa murder co-conspirator. The tip described Hoffa being stuffed into a 55-gallon drum, loaded onto a truck and shipped to New Jersey.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211120ehbk001rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
