\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A slap in the face\u8217\'20\'19: nurses\u8217\'20\'19 strike signals Kaiser\u8217\'20\'19s end as union haven\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 1,234 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 November 2021\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The management\u8217\'20\'19s initial offer of 1%-a-year raise and 26% cut in salary for new hires seen as a wage squeeze during pandemic\par \par \uc2 Across corporate America, relations between companies and their labor unions range from chilly to ice-cold. Not at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the California-based healthcare giant. Kaiser has long been seen as having the nation\u8217\'20\'19s best labor-management partnership. Now the partnership finds itself in crisis as 34,000 \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  healthcare workers prepare to strike on Monday, in what would be the largest walkout in this {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/23/striketober-unions-strikes-workers-lasting-change"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  fall\u8217\'20\'19s strike wave. }}}\uc2  healthcare workers prepare to strike on Monday, in what would be the largest walkout in this\par \par \uc2 After risking their lives during the pandemic, many Kaiser workers are asking how things could have turned so sour in the much-praised partnership, in which managers and union members team up at hundreds of Kaiser facilities to find innovative ways to improve care and efficiency, saving the company tens of millions of dollars a year.\par \par \uc2 Last week one of Kaiser\u8217\'20\'19s nurses\u8217\'20\'19 unions served notice it would strike on 15 November, and soon after, several other unions also voted to strike. The nurses\u8217\'20\'19 union \u8211\'20\'13 United Nurses Associations of California/Union of Health Care \u8211\'20\'13 complained that management\u8217\'20\'19s latest employment offer would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unacuhcp.org/press_release/21000-nurses-and-health-care-professionals-will-strike-against-kaiser-permanente-beginning-monday-november-15/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdepress wages for current employees and slash wages for incoming workers\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Saying that its labor costs were far above its competitors, Kaiser initially proposed raises of 1% a year for three years and cutting the pay of new hires to 26% below those of its current employees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe partnership has been built on it being a leading payer in the market,\u8221\'20\'1D said Adrienne Eaton, dean of the Rutgers School of Management and Labor Relations, who has written about Kaiser. \u8220\'20\'1CIf they\u8217\'20\'19ve decided not to do that any more, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to cause a strong reaction among the unions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It certainly caused a strong reaction in Semanu Mawugbe, a Kaiser nurse in Los Angeles. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a slap in the face,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, noting that the 1%-a-year offer was well below this year\u8217\'20\'19s 5%-plus inflation rate. \u8220\'20\'1CThey tell us we\u8217\'20\'19re heroes and we\u8217\'20\'19re much appreciated because of everything we did during the pandemic\u8221\'20\'1D, he said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut their offer shows they don\u8217\'20\'19t mean it. We\u8217\'20\'19re the ones who sustained the hospitals and took care of the sick like it\u8217\'20\'19s a war zone.\u8221\'20\'1D The unions say Kaiser is seeking to squeeze wages when the non-profit company is doing well, with $45bn in cash reserves and $6.8bn in operating profits the last three years.\par \par \uc2 Since Kaiser\u8217\'20\'19s labor-management partnership was founded in 1997, none of its 35 union locals has gone on strike. The partnership includes over 100,000 union members. Kaiser overall has $89bn in annual revenues, 12 million health plan members, 39 hospitals and more than 700 other medical facilities spread across eight states and Washington DC.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://about.kaiserpermanente.org/who-we-are/labor-relations/addressing-alliance-strike-notifications"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe challenge we are trying to address }}}\uc2  in partnership with our unions is the increasingly unaffordable cost of healthcare,\u8221\'20\'1D Arlene Peasnall, Kaiser\u8217\'20\'19s senior vice-president of human resources, said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact is wages and benefits account for half of \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s operational costs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Peasnall said Kaiser\u8217\'20\'19s wages have risen to the point where its union members earn \u8220\'20\'1Con average 26% above the market rate\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://about.kaiserpermanente.org/who-we-are/labor-relations/our-proposal-to-alliance-includes-higher-wage-increases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This is unsustainable }}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. Facing a strike, Kaiser management increased its contract offer to a 2% raise in each of four years with a 2% lump sum payment in the contract\u8217\'20\'19s first two years. Under Kaiser\u8217\'20\'19s revised proposal, new hires would be paid 15% less than current workers.\par \par \uc2 Several labor experts said Kaiser made some elementary bargaining mistakes that were bound to inflame its workers. Kaiser offered just 1%-a-year raise while its largest union, a service employees\u8217\'20\'19 local representing 46,000 Kaiser workers, has a contract that calls for raises of 3% a year over the next two years. Other unions felt shortchanged to be offered less than that. \u8220\'20\'1CIt does seem like a provocation,\u8221\'20\'1D Dean Eaton said.\par \par \uc2 Labor experts also said Kaiser\u8217\'20\'19s two-tier proposal to pay new hires significantly less was bound to anger workers and worsen staffing problems. \u8220\'20\'1CIt generally doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make sense having two tiers of staff and it makes even less sense when we\u8217\'20\'19re going through a pandemic.\u8221\'20\'1D said Peter Lazes, former director of the Health Care Transformation Project at \uc2 Cornell University\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI have to blame management for not being sensitive. It seems hard to understand why they\u8217\'20\'19re doing this when there\u8217\'20\'19s a nursing shortage nationally.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They tell us we\u8217\'20\'19re heroes and we\u8217\'20\'19re much appreciated \u8230\'20\'26 But their offer shows they don\u8217\'20\'19t mean it. We sustained the hospitals and took care of the sick like it\u8217\'20\'19s a war zone\par \par \uc2 Semanu Mawugbe\par \par \uc2 Lazes, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ideas.bkconnection.com/solving-systemic-problems-in-hospitals-and-beyond"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who has studied Kaiser\u8217\'20\'19s partnership }}}\uc2 , isn\u8217\'20\'19t so sure that the labor dispute will jeopardize the partnership long-term. \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea that you\u8217\'20\'19re going to have differences between labor and management partners that might result in a strike or a strike vote is part of the labor-management process,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CUnion and management have to know how to dance together and box at the same time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Denise Duncan, president of the United Nurses union, called Kaiser\u8217\'20\'19s offer \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally unacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D. She derided the proposal to pay new workers less: \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t solve a nursing shortage that way.\u8221\'20\'1D She faulted Kaiser\u8217\'20\'19s wage survey, saying it should have been done in cooperation with Kaiser\u8217\'20\'19s unions. She said the survey, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unacuhcp.org/press_release/21000-nurses-and-health-care-professionals-will-strike-against-kaiser-permanente-beginning-monday-november-15/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comparing Kaiser\u8217\'20\'19s pay levels with those at smaller, less sophisticated medical institutions, often in rural areas }}}\uc2 , was apples and oranges.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUltimately, we just had to pull our levers [for a strike]\u8221\'20\'1D, Duncan told the Guardian . \u8220\'20\'1COur members were angry. Everyone worked so hard. We feel Kaiser let our principles of partnership go.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lazes said that Kaiser\u8217\'20\'19s new CEO and leadership team do not seem nearly as committed to making the labor-management partnership succeed and run smoothly as was \uc2 Bernard Tyson\uc2  , a Kaiser CEO who died of a heart attack in November 2019. Duncan wholeheartedly agreed. \u8220\'20\'1CWe believed Bernard to be a purist on social justice and working people and having the utmost respect for the history of the partnership,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Duncan said Tyson\u8217\'20\'19s successor, \uc2 Greg Adams\uc2  , had been doing little to ensure the partnership\u8217\'20\'19s success. \u8220\'20\'1CYou got to invest in it. You have to bring in the next generation of workers and leaders,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you don\u8217\'20\'19t invest in it, it dies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Peasnall said the company was devoted to the partnership. \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t mistake passionate advocacy in bargaining with actual changes in a relationship,\u8221\'20\'1D she told the Guardian . \u8220\'20\'1COur labor-management partnership remains strong and is a significant source of our strength as an organization.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Peasnall added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe absolutely believe that as we conclude bargaining this cycle, and get through the disastrous pandemic, we will emerge stronger and more united than ever before.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile nurses like Semanu Mawugbe are angry and ready to walk out. \u8220\'20\'1CNone of us want a strike, but there are times it has to be done,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re hoping for a last-minute, 11th-hour turnaround.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211113ehbd001bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
