\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Workers are very afraid\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 HelloFresh\uc2  employees aim to unionize amid claims of abuse\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,364 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 November 2021\par 17:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers for the largest meal-kit delivery service in the world say attempts to unionize have been met with retaliation and bullying\par \par \uc2 Workers at \uc2 HelloFresh\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inc.com/magazine/201808/burt-helm/hellofresh.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largest }}}\uc2  meal-kit delivery service in the world, say they are facing an aggressive anti-union campaign led by the company after they tried to organize amid claims of safety issues and poor treatment of workers.\par \par \uc2 HelloFresh\uc2  has operations in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hellofresh.co.nz/careers/locations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 14 other countries}}}\uc2  including the US, UK and Australia and employs over 11,800 people worldwide preparing ingredients for delivery for home cooked meals including brown sugar bourbon apple pork chops and kale, cranberry and walnut stuffed squash.\par \par \uc2 During the pandemic its profits soared and now workers at its production facilities in Richmond, California, and Aurora, Colorado, are trying to form unions amid claims they have faced intimidation and abuse.\par \par \uc2 At the Richmond, California facility, the \uc2 union Unite Here\uc2  Local 2850 has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/search/case/grocery%20delivery%20e-services%20USA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  several unfair labor practice charges with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) against \uc2 HelloFresh\uc2 , alleging the company has retaliated, intimidated, and bullied union supporting workers over the last several months.\par \par \uc2 Evelin Escobar, a production worker at the Richmond, California, facility, alleged two \uc2 HelloFresh\uc2  security guards approached her and requested she turn in her employee badge to them, claiming she was distributing pro-union leaflets in the workplace during work hours, after she and other co-workers handed out leaflets during their lunch break outside the facility.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do that during lunch and that\u8217\'20\'19s my right, so, I felt very intimidated,\u8221\'20\'1D said Escobar.\par \par \uc2 She said co-workers came to her defense and forced the security guards to stop insisting she turn over her badge.\par \par \uc2 Escobar said the union campaign was started in response to safety issues, treatment of workers by management, and working conditions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne day I was running the production line, and my team lead was yelling at me, telling me to do so many things at once I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t do and while yelling at me called me \u8216\'20\'18a Mexican shit\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D said Escobar. \u8220\'20\'1CShe doesn\u8217\'20\'19t respect any of us. I heard her call someone else stupid. She yells at us. And so that\u8217\'20\'19s why the most important thing for me above all else is that we can win respect on the job. We work eight hours a day and we don\u8217\'20\'19t feel happy going to work, so we\u8217\'20\'19re ready for a change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Like \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and other businesses now facing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/21/amazon-workers-union-election-nlrb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 union drives}}}\uc2  from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/23/striketober-unions-strikes-workers-lasting-change"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unhappy workers, HelloFresh}}}\uc2  experienced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://progressivegrocer.com/hellofresh-had-record-breaking-year"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record sales and profits}}}\uc2  during the Covid-19 pandemic, with the company\u8217\'20\'19s revenue more than doubling in 2020. As demand soared, workers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/m7ey5b/hellofresh-workers-are-unionizing-the-booming-meal-kit-industry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  unsafe working conditions, which contributed to workers deciding to organize to form a union.\par \par \uc2 Some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/27-RC-282916"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 386 workers}}}\uc2  at the Aurora, Colorado, facility are currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/27-RC-282916"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 casting}}}\uc2  ballots by mail, with votes scheduled to be counted on 22 November.\par \par \uc2 Around 850 workers in Richmond are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/32-RC-283407"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scheduled}}}\uc2  to receive ballots by 18 November, with their union election votes scheduled to be tallied on 15 December.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of their union election, \uc2 HelloFresh\uc2  workers have claimed management retaliated against them for engaging in union activity.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after Denis Guzman and Aindra Hernandez, two workers in the quality assurance department at \uc2 HelloFresh\uc2 , were distributing union leaflets outside during their lunch break, the workers were approached by managers and told they were not permitted to do so.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s very unjust that all of this treatment gets so normalized\par \par \uc2 Aindra Hernandez\par \par \uc2 Later the same day, Guzman was brought into an office room with other managers who informed him he was being demoted from quality assurance back to production.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI asked them, \u8216\'20\'18what is the real reason that you\u8217\'20\'19re doing this?\u8217\'20\'19 And they said, the real reason is because I don\u8217\'20\'19t speak English well enough,\u8221\'20\'1D said Guzman, who claimed other workers in the department have similar English proficiency and it was never mentioned as an issue before or during his training. \u8220\'20\'1CI felt like they were trying to camouflage the demotion because I had been exercising my rights on my break, and I felt discriminated against when they told me that I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t good enough to be in a department because I didn\u8217\'20\'19t speak English.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When Hernandez found out that afternoon Guzman was demoted, she defended Guzman to one of her managers and asked why the decision was made. Hernandez said she received no answer and the manager told her to clock out and go home without pay, two hours before her shift ended, following her until she clocked out and left.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere have been so many problems with disrespect, with not being given the material we need to work, and injuries happening in the workplace. It\u8217\'20\'19s very unjust that all of this treatment gets so normalized,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hernandez. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are so many people who fear getting sent home early or the managers being upset with them, like I was sent home, and that makes workers very afraid. We need to change that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers at \uc2 HelloFresh\uc2  said they were also consistently forced into meetings during work hours with paid union avoidance consultants from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://inthesetimes.com/article/kulture-consulting-union-busting-qanon-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kulture Consulting}}}\uc2 . The company is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/hellofresh-is-paying-thousands-of-dollars-a-day-to-anti-union-consultants_n_616043d1e4b0196444241908"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spending}}}\uc2  thousands of dollars a day for the consultants to try to dissuade workers from voting in favor of the union.\par \par \uc2 Alec Woodard, a shipping department worker at the Richmondfacility explained how \uc2 HelloFresh\uc2  has responded to the union organizing campaign over the past several weeks, which has included hiring union avoidance consultants who have held several captive audience meetings with workers in an attempt to dissuade workers from voting for the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey outright said you might lose money by doing this in the first meeting,\u8221\'20\'1D said Woodard. \u8220\'20\'1CAn executive said they were proud the facility had the largest number of Covid-19 cases in Contra Costa county because that demonstrated the success of their Covid testing program.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said consultants and management have tried to characterize the union as a business, comparing union organizers to sales representatives who will \u8220\'20\'1Ctrick\u8221\'20\'1D workers into joining a union.\par \par \uc2 New {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HelloFresh?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @HelloFresh}}}\uc2  anti-union content just dropped. ??\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll go ahead and let y\u8217\'20\'19all react.\par \par \uc2 (PS the man in the photo works for Kulture Consulting, an anti-union firm that received $2,625/day for work in 2019) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FZIyCvc7K2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FZIyCvc7K2}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 UNITE HERE\uc2  (@unitehere) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/unitehere/status/1445496096734605312?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 ?? URGENT: Seen today at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HelloFresh?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @HelloFresh}}}\uc2  factory where workers have filed for a union election.\par \par \uc2 ?? Playing off the famous organizing fish, eh? Well,\par \par \uc2 ?? Union Busting is Disgusting!\par \par \uc2 ?? Tell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/HelloFresh?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #HelloFresh}}}\uc2  TODAY to not interfere with workers right to vote!\par \par \uc2 ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dC1ogpCY1n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/dC1ogpCY1n}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SljtrMdX06"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SljtrMdX06}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 UNITE HERE\uc2  (@unitehere) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/unitehere/status/1443623970008408064?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 30, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 In the shipping department, Woodard said the department manager has been present a lot more during the union campaign, often making promises that high workloads, understaffing and issues in the department with workers having to stack multiple pallets at a time due to organize them around different shipping carriers would be resolved.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRichmond used to be a strong industrial center and this could be a good job, this facility doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need to run this way,\u8221\'20\'1D added Woodard. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we win, I think it would be a significant step for the city as a whole, not just for the workers at \uc2 HelloFresh\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for HelloFresh said in an email: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 HelloFresh\uc2  believes that the decision of whether or not to be represented by a union is an important one and we respect each employee\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose or refuse union membership.\u8221\'20\'1D They did not provide information on how much the company is spending on union avoidance consultants.\par \par \uc2 In regards to the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  charges, the spokesperson added; \u8220\'20\'1CWe take these allegations very seriously, and all such complaints are vigorously investigated and addressed. We have comprehensive anti-discrimination and anti-harassment policies and training programs, and numerous avenues for employees to raise concerns, including a 24/7 hotline for employees to report complaints anonymously. We look forward to refuting these charges with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , however because this is an ongoing investigation, we have no further information to share at this time about these specific claims.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211111ehbb001pc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
