\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 New York City taxi drivers end hunger strike after reaching deal on debt relief\b0\par\par\uc2 Erum Salam in New York \par \uc2 800 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 November 2021\par 13:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Taxi and Limousine Commission agrees to city-backed guarantee to lower monthly payments of taxi medallion owners\par \par \uc2 After weeks of camping outside City Hall in New York, taxi drivers can finally head home after striking a deal with officials to rescue thousands of workers from crushing loans that had caused misery for their families.\par \par \uc2 The news arrived on the 15th day of a hunger strike led by the drivers and their advocates.\par \par \uc2 New York City\u8217\'20\'19s Taxi and Limousine Commission (TLC) agreed to a city-backed guarantee to lower the monthly payments of taxi medallion owners, or \u8220\'20\'1Cowner drivers\u8221\'20\'1D to a maximum $170,000 \u8211\'20\'13 far less than the average medallion debt of around $600,000, according to the New York Taxi Workers Alliance (NYTWA).\par \par \uc2 The agreement was made with Marblegate, the largest medallion loan-holder, with more lenders expecting to follow suit. Soon, the most a driver can expect to pay back in loanswill be just over $1,100 per month.\par \par \uc2 For driver Erhan Tuncel, 61, who has a total medallion debt of $690,000 with monthly payments of $3,800, the news was a great relief.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe lower monthly payment is a huge break for every single one us,\u8221\'20\'1D Tuncel said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt means we can put in a full day\u8217\'20\'19s work and be happy with the money we take home because owning and operating a medallion in New York City is an expensive business. On top of the medallion payments, we take on all the expenses like insurance, maintaining the vehicle, the TLC fees, inspection fees \u8211\'20\'13 they all add up. I\u8217\'20\'19m ecstatic and happy for all the owner-drivers who are going to get a huge break from this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The crisis in the city\u8217\'20\'19s famed yellow cab industry began with the tin plate required to operate a yellow cab, otherwise known as a taxi medallion. The reasons for the large debt owed by taxi drivers are a lack of regulation by New York City, which allowed the price of the medallion to be artificially inflated (once to the point of $1m), and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/19/nyregion/nyc-taxis-medallions-suicides.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predatory lenders}}}\uc2  that targeted the taxi workforce, which is made up of many people of color in a sector long seen as a path to the middle class for immigrants.\par \par \uc2 The city was complicit in marketing the medallion as \u8220\'20\'1Cbetter than a stock\u8221\'20\'1D and a pathway to the American dream, leading taxi drivers to believe a medallion was an investment worthy of risking all they hold dear. The substantial debt eventually drove some drivers to suicide.\par \par \uc2 The drivers\u8217\'20\'19 case had won support from progressive elected officials at national, state, and local levels \u8211\'20\'13 including Senator \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , Congresswoman Alexandria Ocasio Cortez, and New York\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Letitia James.\par \par \uc2 Big news: My office, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NYTWA?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NYTWA}}}\uc2 , & {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NYCMayor?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NYCMayor}}}\uc2  reached a deal that includes city backstop to ensure DESPERATELY needed debt relief for our taxi workers\par \par \uc2 This is a real victory\u8212\'20\'14Thank you to the brave hunger strikers and extraordinary movement of NYers for coming together for our cabbies\u8212\'20\'14 Chuck Schumer (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1455987481019625481?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 3, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www1.nyc.gov/office-of-the-mayor/news/739-21/mayor-senator-schumer-ny-taxi-workers-alliance-marblegate-asset-management-announce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  Schumer, who brokered the deal with Mayor \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe medallion debt crisis has gone on for years, taking lives and livelihoods. I commend Mayor \uc2 de Blasio\uc2  for his leadership, the New York Taxi Workers Alliance for their steadfast advocacy, and Marblegate for their good-faith effort to forge a workable solution. Together, we will bring this ongoing situation to a just resolution for the thousands of cabbies who work every day to serve this city.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One of the NYTWA\u8217\'20\'19s most vocal advocates is Zohran Mamdani, a state assemblyman from Queens. After 15 days of hunger striking and consuming nothing but water, Gatorade and eventually chicken broth, the activist-politician broke his fast upon hearing the news with just two slices of avocado and a date.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI woke up on Monday of this week and I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t sure if I could go on. It had been 12 days at that point and I just wasn\u8217\'20\'19t sure where we were and how long it was going to go. I was just so tired and I was so tired of being hungry,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Mamdani said he viewed the hunger strike as a much-needed escalatory tactic that made the consequences of policy public.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy going on a hunger strike in front of City Hall, there was no way you could ignore what we were doing to our bodies in the service of this fight. It\u8217\'20\'19s infectious \u8211\'20\'13 the courage, the belief. Then it all culminated in today and I just haven\u8217\'20\'19t felt the emotions that I felt today in a long time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211104ehb4001mf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
