\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 Child labor laws in some states may be weakened as US industries look to hire teens\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,064 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 November 2021\par 15:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Experts fear increased stress and loss of sleep among students as some Republicans want to allow teenagers to work longer hours\par \par \uc2 US employers are recruiting teenaged workers to solve their difficulties in hiring and retaining workers, and some Republicans and industry groups are pushing for looser child labor laws to allow those industries to put teens to work for longer hours.\par \par \uc2 Businesses around the United States that have advertised hiring 14- and 15-year-olds through the pandemic\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Clabor shortage\u8221\'20\'1D include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://triblive.com/local/valley-news-dispatch/some-a-k-valley-businesses-are-hiring-14-and-15-year-olds-to-address-staffing-shortages/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 several restaurants in Pennsylvania}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kshb.com/news/local-news/liberty-pumpkin-patch-adjusts-hiring-requirements-to-widen-employment-pool"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Pumpkin Patch in Liberty, Missouri}}}\uc2 , a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailydot.com/irl/burger-king-teen-worker-sign/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Burger King in Ohio}}}\uc2 , and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/mcdonalds-trying-to-hire-teens-with-labor-shortage-2021-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s in Oregon}}}\uc2 . Employers such as Chipotle have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.restaurant.org/articles/news/tapping-the-teen-market?mkt_tok=MDc4LVpMQS00NjEAAAF-AmpfPRXIfzfipfYNUDBzk6vhHTS0IWqo0vrMA-TE5MDDm_yebnbB7KaF7UBmu223-yqIhhEUPMROp6t7O0KKhQPqZlgRdyi1JTRkqtBj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expanded }}}\uc2  recruiting efforts this year to target younger workers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://markets.businessinsider.com/news/stocks/fast-food-retail-labor-shortage-teenagers-managers-wage-laynes-texas-2021-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Other restaurants }}}\uc2  and employers such as amusement parks and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wgme.com/news/local/maine-teens-cash-in-on-summer-labor-shortage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seasonal businesses}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.convenience.org/Media/Daily/2021/Jun/8/1-Businesses-Recruit-Teens-Labor-Shortage_HR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 around the US }}}\uc2  have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/nj-state-wire-co-state-wire-health-coronavirus-pandemic-travel-2f02bf564e726f4c4f6916790bda7a2a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 touted}}}\uc2  their reliance on teenage workers under 18 as a labor shortage solution. A restaurant in Arkansas, noting it had struggled to hire and retain workers, recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.yahoo.com/restaurant-owner-paying-teen-workers-090842434.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offered}}}\uc2  to pay its teen workers for one hour to do homework before their shift.\par \par \uc2 Teenage employment in the US surged to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/business/business-news/teen-workers-fill-job-shortage-what-happens-when-summer-fades-n1272915"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 32% }}}\uc2  in summer 2021, the highest level since 2008, and for the first time in history the unemployment rate for 16- to 19-year-olds fell below the rate for 20- to 24-year-olds.\par \par \uc2 In a recent op-ed for a local Pennsylvania newspaper, Darcy Leight, a junior in high school, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.buckscountycouriertimes.com/story/lifestyle/2021/10/15/worker-shortage-teens-juggling-school-jobs/5990727001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  the claims of labor shortages and staffing issues in the food service, recreation and tourism industry had driven teenagers to work more and longer hours past summer employment periods.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA job I intended to work strictly during the summer has somehow found its way into my fall schedule and has become almost equivalent to academics on my priority list. And I don\u8217\'20\'19t even know how it happened,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CThe coupling of a job anywhere from five to 35 hours a week along with being a student is extremely stressful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/no-end-sight-labor-shortages-us-companies-fight-high-costs-2021-10-26/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  labor shortage concerns }}}\uc2  have galvanized an effort by some elected officials \u8211\'20\'13 mostly Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 to scale back some child labor regulations.\par \par \uc2 Three Republicans and one Democrat in the Ohio state senate have recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://legiscan.com/OH/bill/SB251/2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced a bill }}}\uc2  to expand the hours minors under the age of 16 are permitted to work in the state, from 7pm to 9pm during the school year with a parent or guardian\u8217\'20\'19s permission.\par \par \uc2 In Wisconsin, Republican state senators recently approved a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/2021/proposals/sb332"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill}}}\uc2 , SB332, and sent it to the Wisconsin state assembly. The bill would expand permissible work hours for minors under the age of 16.\par \par \uc2 Supporters of the bill, which include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.thewheelerreport.com/wheeler_docs/files/102021felzkowski.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Republican legislators}}}\uc2 , the Wisconsin Restaurant Association and other industry groups, have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/sports-business-wisconsin-bills-afl-cio-2a23a54173dca96c13233ae5c5d6f239"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  argued }}}\uc2  the bill could help small businesses that are experiencing hiring and staff retention issues amid some industries experiencing labor shortages throughout 2021.\par \par \uc2 Under current law, minors are permitted to work from 7am to 7pm from labor day to 31 May and 7am to 9pm from 1 June to labor day.\par \par \uc2 The bill would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/2021/related/proposals/sb332"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expand}}}\uc2  those times and dates from 6am to 9.30pm on a day preceding a school day and 6am to 11pm on a day preceding a non-school day, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://patch.com/wisconsin/milwaukee/wi-senate-bill-would-extend-workday-minors-5-things-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expand}}}\uc2  weekly hours from three hours during a school week to 18 hours.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin Republicans have successfully passed several bills in the last decade to weaken child labor laws, including in 2011 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://stopchildlabor.org/new-child-labor-laws-expand-work-hours/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminating}}}\uc2  limits on the number of hours and days minors, ages 16 and 17, could work, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/wisconsin-bills-legislature-madison-lena-taylor-7e7c241bb18049f898a03a9b8fecf451"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminating work permits}}}\uc2  for 16 and 17-year-olds, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/2017/related/lcactmemo/act011.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 replacing}}}\uc2  all uses of the term \u8220\'20\'1Cchild labor\u8221\'20\'1D in state employment statutes with the term \u8220\'20\'1Cemployment of minors\u8221\'20\'1D in 2017.\par \par \uc2 They also kids that need time to study, to sleep and to prepare their minds for their future\par \par \uc2 Stephanie Bloomingdale\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe passage of this bill would be a slippery slope for eliminating child labor practices in Wisconsin and in the United States in general,\u8221\'20\'1D said Stephanie Bloomingdale, president of the Wisconsin AFL-CIO, which opposes SB332. \u8220\'20\'1CYoung teenagers need to have good work experiences that help them to learn work ethics and valuable skills, but at the same time, recognizing they also are kids that need time to study, to sleep and to prepare their minds for their future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reports of labor shortages have received significant coverage throughout 2021, with employers and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uschamber.com/workforce/us-chamber-calls-ending-300-weekly-supplemental-unemployment-benefits-address-labor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 industry groups}}}\uc2  often {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2021/08/04/early-end-to-federal-unemployment-pay-in-26-states-not-getting-people-to-work.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blaming}}}\uc2  unemployment benefits for difficulties in finding enough workers, though ending unemployment benefits {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2021/09/24/little-evidence-that-end-of-extra-unemployment-sent-people-back-to-work.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not result}}}\uc2  in a mass influx of Americans returning to work. Several solutions that employers have turned to amid labor shortage concerns through 2021 include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/20/companies-claim-theres-a-labor-shortage-their-solution-prisoners"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prison labor}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/americans-with-criminal-records-could-be-a-solution-to-the-labor-shortage-212251293.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently released prisoners}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/business-and-finance/2021/10/26/22733082/labor-shortage-inflation-immigration-foreign-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigrant visa programs}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Labor groups and workers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/u-s-labor-shortage-unlikely-heres-why/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 characterized }}}\uc2  the labor issues as a result of low wages, Covid-19 safety concerns, rampant poor working conditions and a lack of childcare and paid sick leave throughout the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe notion that we would be solving some economic turmoil by allowing the expansion of child labor hours, is at best, ridiculous, and at worst, very detrimental to young people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Debra Cronmiller, executive director of the League of Women Voters of Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Scientific research has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washington.edu/news/2011/02/09/working-more-than-20-hours-a-week-in-high-school-can-harm-grades-uw-researcher-finds/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shown}}}\uc2  working long hours while attending high school can have negative academic and behavioral impacts on teenagers.\par \par \uc2 Dr Kathryn C Monahan, a psychologist who researched the impact of work on adolescents while at the \uc2 University of Washington\uc2 , explained much of the research on adolescent employment has focused on formal types of employment that generally occurs at age 16 and above.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat this bill does, I think, is it opens up and it encourages young teens to enter into that workforce,\u8221\'20\'1D said Monahan.\par \par \uc2 She noted a lack of scientific research on how work affects teens this young, and what impact earning income at such a young age may have on other negative behaviors, such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/wonk/wp/2015/04/16/an-alarming-number-of-teenagers-are-quitting-school-to-work-heres-how-to-help-them/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropping out of high school}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4593323/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 substance abuse}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe second thing that concerns me about this is the sleep issue,\u8221\'20\'1D Monahan added. \u8220\'20\'1C I can imagine the kid getting home later on a school night \u8230\'20\'26 because that\u8217\'20\'19s when that child uses that time for homework, for catching up with friends, and so you\u8217\'20\'19re going to get an even further delay out in terms of sleep, while school is going to stay constant in terms of those really early wake up times.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211102ehb20018i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
