\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 New York: 9,000 public workers put on unpaid leave for refusing Covid vaccine\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang and agencies \par \uc2 564 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 November 2021\par 11:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mayor says thousands of firefighters have called out sick in apparent protest, with 18 of 350 units out of service\par \par \uc2 About 9,000 New York City municipal workers were put on unpaid leave for refusing to comply with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2021/nov/01/flu-cancer-hiv-after-covid-success-what-next-for-mrna-vaccines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Covid-19 vaccine}}}\uc2  mandate that took effect on Monday, Mayor \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2  said, adding that thousands of firefighters had called out sick in apparent protest.\par \par \uc2 Firehouses remained open but 18 of 350 units were out of service and \u8220\'20\'1Cmany units are understaffed\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Daniel Nigro\uc2 , the fire commissioner, said.\par \par \uc2 Officials have been battling fierce resistance among a minority of workers in some critical public safety jobs, including police officers and firefighters, with a pending legal challenge to the mandate from the largest police union.\par \par \uc2 As of Sunday, one in four of uniformed New York firefighters had not had a first dose of the vaccine, as required. About one in six police personnel and one in six sanitation workers were still unvaccinated.\par \par \uc2 About 2,300 firefighters were out sick, up from a norm of around 1,000 a day, in what Nigro said appeared to be a protest against the vaccine mandate. The fire department medical office normally saw about 200 people a day, Nigro said. Over the past week, it had been 700 a day, most of them unvaccinated.\par \par \uc2 As officials prepared for staffing shortfalls, calling in vaccinated employees for overtime shifts, Nigro called on firefighters to stop misusing sick leave.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are understaffed units,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat understaffing could end immediately if members stopped going sick when they weren\u8217\'20\'19t sick. Once the members come to their senses and stop using medical leave improperly, they can help out not just the citizens of the city but their brothers and sisters staffing the units.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 De Blasio\uc2  said the city was watching to see if the firefighters union was coordinating the sick-outs and would take it to court if there was evidence of an illegal strike. He said firefighters found to be faking illness would be \u8220\'20\'1Cawol effectively\u8221\'20\'1D and would face internal discipline.\par \par \uc2 The head of the union that represents New York City firefighters, which has fought the vaccine mandate, warned that public safety could be at risk. The fire department has said it is prepared to take up to 20% of companies out of service and have 20% fewer ambulances on the road.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re here today because of a mandate that was put not only on our members, but also all New York City employees, given nine days to make a life-changing decision on their career or whether or not they\u8217\'20\'19re going to take a vaccine,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Uniformed Firefighters Association president, Andrew Ansbro.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, six firefighters were suspended for four weeks without pay after they drove a fire engine to the Brooklyn office of a New York state senator, Zellnor Myrie, to protest the vaccine mandate.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2021/11/01/us/nyc-fdny-firefighters-suspended-vaccine-mandate/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to}}}\uc2  Myrie\u8217\'20\'19s spokesman, Matt Baer, the firefighters asked to discuss the mandate. They asked where the senator lived and said the city would have blood on its hands due to the mandate.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, numerous FDNY members also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeeroyPress/status/1453777288009502727?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protested}}}\uc2  outside Gracie Mansion, the mayor\u8217\'20\'19s residence. Signs read \u8220\'20\'1CEssential Workers aren\u8217\'20\'19t Disposable Heroes\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1CMy Body My Choice\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1C#NaturalImmunity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211102ehb2001ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
