\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s clear capitalism isn\u8217\'20\'19t working when US politicians try to bring back child labor\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,064 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2021\par 13:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 There is something very, very wrong with a system that would rather recruit more kids instead of paying better wages and providing more benefits to adults\par \par \uc2 Build Back Better (with child labour)\par \par \uc2 Back in the good old days American children didn\u8217\'20\'19t sit around playing video games, making TikToks, and bingeing \uc2 Netflix\uc2 . They worked long hours in factories and sweatshops; they knew the value of hard graft. They didn\u8217\'20\'19t take sick days either, they just died of diphtheria. It was a simpler time.\par \par \uc2 Some US politicians, it would seem, are trying their best to return the country to a golden era of loose labour laws. The Wisconsin senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/changing-america/enrichment/arts-culture/577754-wisconsin-moves-to-let-14-year-olds-work-till-11-pm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently approved}}}\uc2  a bill that expands the working day for minors, allowing 14- and 15-year-olds to work until 11 pm on non-school nights. Must be fun being a child in Wisconsin! Not only do adults want to take away your free time, they also want to take away your free food. Over the summer school board members in the Waukesha school district made headlines after they voted to leave a federal free meals program because they worried it made it easy for families to \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.salon.com/2021/08/27/wisconsin-school-board-pilloried-for-halting-free-meals-program-citing-concern-of-spoiled-children/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 become spoiled}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D or develop an \u8220\'20\'1Caddiction\u8221\'20\'1D to the service. Imagine if kids became addicted to the government ensuring they didn\u8217\'20\'19t starve, eh? They might not be so keen to work for peanuts until 11 at night. Then you might have to start paying adults a living wage and the whole system would fall apart!\par \par \uc2 As I\u8217\'20\'19m sure you are aware, the United States \u8211\'20\'13 along with much of the world \u8211\'20\'13 is facing a dramatic labour shortage amid what has been termed the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/money/2021/jul/13/we-quit-the-great-resignation-era-has-begun-at-a-boiling-hot-branch-of-burger-king"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Great Resignation}}}\uc2 . Earlier this month the \uc2 US Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  reported that an unprecedented 2.9% of the workforce, about 4.3 million people, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-09-21/high-quits-rates-poaching-u-s-firms-are-plagued-by-turnover"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quit their jobs}}}\uc2  in August. Republicans have been doing their best to starve people back into the low-paid jobs that keep the economy running by cutting off {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/21/us-unemployment-benefits-pandemic-cut-republican-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pandemic unemployment benefits}}}\uc2 , but that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t immediately solved the issue. So some bright sparks have been turning to child labour instead. Over the summer New Jersey passed legislation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nj1015.com/now-law-nj-teens-can-work-50-hours-per-week/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily increasing}}}\uc2  the number of hours that kids aged 16-18 are able to work. Meanwhile, fast-food chains across the US have ramped up their efforts to recruit kids. Last month a \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  in Oregon sparked headlines after it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/news/business-58414597"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 put out a banner}}}\uc2  urging 14- and 15-year-olds to apply.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s obviously nothing wrong with teenagers getting summer jobs. But there is something very, very wrong with a system that would rather recruit more kids into the workforce instead of paying better wages and providing more benefits to adults. There\u8217\'20\'19s something very wrong with a system where billionaires have seen their net worth balloon during the worst public health crisis in recent memory \u8211\'20\'13 and politicians seemingly have no desire to make them pay their fair share in taxes. There\u8217\'20\'19s something very wrong with a system where minimum wage isn\u8217\'20\'19t enough to afford a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/aug/12/housing-renter-affordable-data-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two-bedroom rental anywhere in the US}}}\uc2 . And, increasingly, people aren\u8217\'20\'19t putting up with all this any more. They\u8217\'20\'19re not swallowing the lie that if they just buckle down and work hard, they can achieve the American dream. They\u8217\'20\'19re not quietly getting on with it, they\u8217\'20\'19re organising: the past year has seen a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/oct/19/america-strike-wave-john-deere-iatse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wave of labour uprisings}}}\uc2  across America. Meanwhile, socialism (once an incredibly dirty word in the US) has been gaining popularity {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/americas-continued-move-toward-socialism-84a0dda7-4b8d-483a-8c4e-0c2e562c4e67.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 among young Americans}}}\uc2 . And that last bit should surprise no one. If politicians are trying to bring back child labour to plug labour shortages then I think it\u8217\'20\'19s pretty clear that capitalism isn\u8217\'20\'19t working.\par \par \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s to give staff in the UK fertility, menopause and miscarriage leave\par \par \uc2 The company has said it is aiming to help staff feel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/news/uk-england-manchester-59089645"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cpsychologically safe\u8221\'20\'1D at work}}}\uc2 . Not sure if that ethos extends to its employees in the US: 1,400 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commondreams.org/news/2021/10/06/kelloggs-strrr-ike-1400-workers-walk-job-protect-benefits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently went on strike}}}\uc2  to protest against poor working conditions.\par \par \uc2 Women are better investors than men\par \par \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s investment returns were 0.4% higher than men\u8217\'20\'19s, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fidelity.com/bin-public/060_www_fidelity_com/documents/about-fidelity/FidelityInvestmentsWomen&InvestingStudy2021.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fidelity\u8217\'20\'19s 2021 Women and Investing Study}}}\uc2 . While that\u8217\'20\'19s not a huge difference, it\u8217\'20\'19s just the latest study to show that women tend to be better with money than men. Women tend to hold their investments for longer and are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://inews.co.uk/inews-lifestyle/money/investing/think-like-female-investor-how-women-less-prone-panic-selling-men-1270113"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less prone to panic selling}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Men are increasingly worried about their biological clocks\par \par \uc2 Sirin Kale {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2021/oct/28/scared-late-kids-men-biological-clocks-ageing-procreation-anxieties?mc_cid=740af84e36&mc_eid=8ce16ced76"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 profiles the men}}}\uc2  who are afraid they\u8217\'20\'19ve left it too late to have kids.\par \par \uc2 US tech investor Joe Lonsdale thinks men who take paternity leave are losers\par \par \uc2 The multimillionaire venture capitalist tweeted that men with important jobs shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be taking extended time off to spend with their newborns. \u8220\'20\'1CIn the old days men had babies and worked harder to provide for their future \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s the correct masculine response,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JTLonsdale/status/1453399478254379008?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1453399478254379008%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fmoney%2F2021%2Foct%2F28%2Fus-tech-investor-joe-lonsdale-refuses-to-apologise-for-loser-paternity-tweet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he tweeted}}}\uc2 . The father-of-three has refused to apologize {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/money/2021/oct/28/us-tech-investor-joe-lonsdale-refuses-to-apologise-for-loser-paternity-tweet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for his comments}}}\uc2 . Real men don\u8217\'20\'19t apologize, doubling down on looking like an idiot is the correct masculine response!\par \par \uc2 Sexual misconduct complaint filed against \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\par \par \uc2 The former New York governor continues his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/28/andrew-cuomo-new-york-governor-misdemeanor-complaint"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dramatic fall from grace}}}\uc2 . Still, things aren\u8217\'20\'19t too bad for him: at least he has that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/andrew-cuomo-pandemic-book-deal-08136b1149764bd2a630a08ab50b6703"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $5.1m payout}}}\uc2  from his book on leadership to fall back on.\par \par \uc2 Polish parliament debates bill banning LGBTQ pride parades\par \par \uc2 Poland has become an increasingly hostile place for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dw.com/en/poland-parliament-debates-bill-banning-lgbtq-pride-parades/a-59655348"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LGBTQ people in recent years}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 US issues its first passport with \u8216\'20\'18X\u8217\'20\'19 gender designation\par \par \uc2 X-citing news for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/oct/27/us-passport-x-gender-designation-first"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 non-binary people!}}}\par \par \uc2 Study finds California condors can have \u8216\'20\'18virgin births\u8217\'20\'19\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Technology/wireStory/study-finds-california-condors-virgin-births-80847358"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Researchers believe}}}\uc2  it is the first case of asexual reproduction in any avian species where the female had access to a mate.\par \par \uc2 The week in phonecall-archy\par \par \uc2 Like every sensible millennial, I do not pick up my phone to unknown numbers under any circumstance. Nor, it seems, does a hiker who got lost in Colorado recently and repeatedly ignored phone calls from a search and rescue team because he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/26/hiker-lost-on-us-mountain-ignored-calls-from-rescuers-because-he-didnt-recognise-the-number"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 didn\u8217\'20\'19t recognize the number}}}\uc2 . I appreciate the dedication to avoiding spammers, but that was a very bad call.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arwa Mahdawi\u8217\'20\'19s new book, Strong Female Lead, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://linktr.ee/ARWAMAHDAWI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 available for pre-order}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211030ehau001gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
