\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18You can\u8217\'20\'19t pay bills on $12 an hour\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 Walmart\uc2  employees left out of raises\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,344 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 October 2021\par 16:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Company announced it would raise minimum wage at Sam\u8217\'20\'19s Club to $15, but \uc2 Walmart\uc2  workers were only bumped up to $12\par \par \uc2 Mendy Hughes, 46, has worked as a cashier for Walmart in Malvern, Arkansas, for 11 years.\par \par \uc2 Her hourly wage, after a recent increase, is $12.85 an hour, a mere 85 cents more than the hourly starting wage for new hires despite her 11 years with the company.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t pay your bills, rent and buy groceries on $12 an hour. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think anywhere in the United States, you can do that. No way,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hughes, who is a member of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://united4respect.org/about-us/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign group}}}\uc2  United for Respect. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t understand how they think $12 an hour is enough to live on, because it\u8217\'20\'19s not at all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the largest employer in the US with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://corporate.walmart.com/newsroom/company-facts#:~:text=Walmart%20employs%20more%20than%202.3,million%20in%20the%20U.S.%20alone."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly 1.6 million workers}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Walmart\uc2  has faced criticism for years over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2020/11/19/walmart-and-mcdonalds-among-top-employers-of-medicaid-and-food-stamp-beneficiaries.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 low wages}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2020/sep/24/walmart-workers-hours-pay-great-workplace"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 working conditions}}}\uc2 , a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-walmart-workers/half-of-walmarts-workforce-are-part-time-workers-labor-group-idUSKCN1IQ295"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reliance }}}\uc2  on keeping workers on part-time schedules and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://violationtracker.goodjobsfirst.org/parent/walmart"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wage theft}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Walmart{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2021/09/02/walmart-hikes-hourly-pay-by-1-for-over-550000-workers.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  in September the company would raise the minimum wage at Sam\u8217\'20\'19s Club locations from $11 to $15 an hour, but \uc2 Walmart\uc2  employees were left out as the parent company raised the minimum wage from $11 to just $12 an hour for \uc2 Walmart\uc2  workers. Earlier this year, \uc2 Walmart{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/02/18/investing/walmart-minimum-wage-retail/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  it would raise wages for 425,000 employees to $13 an hour, emphasizing it would increase the company\u8217\'20\'19s average hourly wage to more than $15 an hour.\par \par \uc2 But thousands of \uc2 Walmart\uc2  employees are still struggling to make ends meet with low pay and many are now speaking up to agitate and campaign for a wage increase. \uc2 Walmart\uc2  workers who are members of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://inthesetimes.com/article/our-walmart-ufcw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 United for Respect for Walmart}}}\uc2  are pushing for a $15 minimum wage at the company.\par \par \uc2 A diabetic with four children, Hughes continued working throughout the pandemic.She said working conditions had worsened due to lack of Covid protections and customers who took out their frustrations on staff around missing products, understaffing, and Covid protocols.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe never have enough people,\u8221\'20\'1D Hughes said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have long lines, people are backed up all the way to the clothes and sometimes wrapped around, because there are maybe two or three, sometimes only one cashier, and the self-checkouts are card only so people who can\u8217\'20\'19t use those are mad and it\u8217\'20\'19s hard to deal with people now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In recent years, \uc2 Walmart\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s competitors have raised their hourly minimum wage to $15 an hour, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marketplace.org/2020/06/17/why-target-is-raising-its-minimum-wage-to-15/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Target}}}\uc2  in 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2018/10/02/amazon-raises-minimum-wage-to-15-for-all-us-employees.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon}}}\uc2  in 2018 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.yahoo.com/costco-raising-starting-wages-17-220948533.html#:~:text=Costco%20just%20raised%20starting%20wages,it%20had%20been%20since%202019.."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Costco}}}\uc2  to $17 an hour in 2021.\par \par \uc2 In the 2021 fiscal year, \uc2 Walmart{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marketwatch.com/investing/stock/wmt/financials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  a profit of more than $13.5bn. In February, \uc2 Walmart\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s board of directors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://d18rn0p25nwr6d.cloudfront.net/CIK-0000104169/598c8825-536a-4371-ab8a-98b9ee761c43.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved}}}\uc2  another $20bn stock buyback program. From November 2020 to the end of January 2021, \uc2 Walmart{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://d18rn0p25nwr6d.cloudfront.net/CIK-0000104169/598c8825-536a-4371-ab8a-98b9ee761c43.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repurchased}}}\uc2  more than 10m shares in the company at over $140 a share, spending more than $1.4bn.\par \par \uc2 Walmart\uc2  is owned by the Walton family, the wealthiest family in the world, with an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/features/worlds-richest-families-2021/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated}}}\uc2  net worth of about $238bn. During the pandemic, Alice, Jim and Rob Walton saw their net worths climb by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ips-dc.org/u-s-billionaire-wealth-surged-by-70-percent-or-2-1-trillion-during-pandemic-theyre-now-worth-a-combined-5-trillion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over $10bn each}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Anna Turner worked at \uc2 Walmart\uc2  in Stockton, California, for more than eight years as a door greeter and customer service associate before she was fired in January, after she had spent months complaining to \uc2 Walmart\uc2  corporate, her store management and California Osha about \uc2 Walmart\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s poor Covid responses.\par \par \uc2 Through her time working at \uc2 Walmart\uc2 , Turner noted she made less than $15 an hour and she was never hired for full-time hours, though she said her department was chronically understaffed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter eight and a half years working the most difficult area of my store I was making just under $15 an hour at part-time. They would always cut our hours so we couldn\u8217\'20\'19t get full-time and health benefits,\u8221\'20\'1D said Turner, who relied on Medi-Cal for health insurance through her employment at \uc2 Walmart\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was fired for not lying on my Covid-19 health and temperature assessments. It was the last thing I said to management the day things started and eventually led to me being fired,\u8221\'20\'1D said Turner, who said she was terminated after an incident where she had to take a break after experiencing an anxiety attack when a customer threatened to assault her over trying to return an item. \u8220\'20\'1CThat place gave me such bad panic attacks and I was mistreated on a regular basis because of the situation \uc2 Walmart\uc2  created by not staffing that department.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the first nine months of the pandemic, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  provided only a fraction of their Covid profits to workers in the form of hazard pay and additional compensation, according to an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/blog/the-avenue/2020/12/22/amazon-and-walmart-have-raked-in-billions-in-additional-profits-during-the-pandemic-and-shared-almost-none-of-it-with-their-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Brookings Institution\uc2 . The Waltons\u8217\'20\'19 net worth increased 26 times more than the cost of Covid compensation for \uc2 Walmart\uc2  workers, estimated at 71 cents an hour in additional wages for workers, compared with a $6.2m-an-hour wealth increase for the Waltons.\par \par \uc2 A research brief by Human Impact Partners {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://humanimpact.org/hipprojects/a-five-dollar-raise-could-transform-walmart-associates-health-and-well-being/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published}}}\uc2  in October found a $5-an-hour minimum wage increase for \uc2 Walmart\uc2  workers would improve mental and physical health for workers, including an increased lifespan of nearly two years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Walmart\uc2  is the largest private employer in the country, they employ more women and people of color than any other employer in the country. So they have a large stake in terms of setting the tone for racial equity in our country and financial security as well,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sukhdip Purewal Boparai, research project director at Human Impact Partners and author of the brief. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Walmart\uc2  really can set the stage and in shifting into transforming the lives of the people that work for them, especially during the pandemic, as they\u8217\'20\'19re putting their lives at risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Peter Naughton, a cashier and self-checkout host at \uc2 Walmart\uc2  in Baton Rouge, Louisiana, for two years, recently saw his hourly wage increase from $11.55 an hour to $12.55 an hour with the new company-wide wage increases. But Naughton said the increase did not go far enough, and he criticized \uc2 Walmart\uc2  for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pymnts.com/news/retail/2021/walmart-ends-quarterly-bonuses-for-store-workers/#:~:text=Hundreds%20of%20thousands%20of%20Walmart,by%20The%20Wall%20Street%20Journal."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminating}}}\uc2  quarterly MyShare bonuses for all employees, which often provided workers with an extra few hundred dollars every three months.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA $1-an-hour increase does not help. We have less money now with a $1 raise than we did before,\u8221\'20\'1D said Naughton. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Walmart\uc2  could raise our wages to $15, $18, even $20 an hour, but they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to, out of greed. \uc2 Walmart\uc2  is the most subsidized company in America by the government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said many of his co-workers have additional jobs and rely on Snap, rental subsidies and other government relief programs in order to make ends meet. In many states, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2020/11/19/walmart-and-mcdonalds-among-top-employers-of-medicaid-and-food-stamp-beneficiaries.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 top employer }}}\uc2  of Medicaid and Snap beneficiaries.\par \par \uc2 In April 2021, Naughton had to vacate his apartment and move in with his parents because he couldn\u8217\'20\'19t afford the rent and other bills on his salary at \uc2 Walmart\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI couldn\u8217\'20\'19t afford the rent, the utilities. I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t afford food or to pay my car note and insurance at the same time,\u8221\'20\'1D added Naughton. \u8220\'20\'1CIf they would raise our wages to even $15 an hour, that would help us have more money to spend. They could actually afford to do that. But they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to do that. It\u8217\'20\'19s really all about the money.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A Walmart spokesperson said in an email: \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we are not going to provide details about individual personnel matters, the claims being made are simply not accurate. We are proud of the industry leading health screening protocols and emergency leave policies we\u8217\'20\'19ve developed and maintained throughout this pandemic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They added the MyShare bonuses were eliminated and rolled into workers\u8217\'20\'19 wages and claimed thousands of people are not on public assistance programs because they work or are insured through \uc2 Walmart\uc2 . They characterized the Human Impact Partners\u8217\'20\'19 study developed with United for Respect as \u8220\'20\'1Cmisleading\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cflawed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211028ehas001e4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
