\par\par \uc2 Film\par \b \uc2 Halyna Hutchins mourned amid anger at Hollywood \u8216\'20\'18cutting corners\u8217\'20\'19 on sets\b0\par\par\uc2 Soo Youn in Los Angeles \par \uc2 1,013 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 October 2021\par 21:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Somber vigil charged with subdued rage over conditions that many lower-paid crew believe were linked to cinematographer\u8217\'20\'19s death\par \par \uc2 A public vigil for the slain cinematographer Halyna Hutchins in Los Angeles on Sunday evening served both as an unofficial memorial event and an outlet for anger over working conditions in Hollywood that many lower-paid crew believe were linked to the 42-year old {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/22/alec-baldwin-fired-prop-gun-woman-death-movie-rust-sheriff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mother\u8217\'20\'19s death}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Several hundred colleagues gathered outside the local union office for the International Alliance of Theatrical Stage Employees (IATSE) which represents workers on film and TV sets, who had been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/15/hollywood-workers-pay-conditions-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poised to go on strike}}}\uc2  to protest about pay, long hours and dangers on sets just days before Hutchins was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2021/oct/22/alec-baldwin-voices-shock-and-sadness-over-shooting-of-halyna-hutchins-on-film-set"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fatally shot}}}\uc2  by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2021/oct/23/alec-baldwin-taking-back-control-until-tragedy-struck"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alec Baldwin}}}\uc2  on the New Mexico set of the desert western film Rust last week.\par \par \uc2 The mood at the vigil was somber yet charged with subdued rage, referenced by IATSE\u8217\'20\'19s international vice-president, Michael Miller, as he addressed the crowd.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re here to mourn. But I\u8217\'20\'19m afraid we are also gathered with some frustration and a little bit of anger. Anger that too often the rush to complete productions and the cutting of corners puts safety on the back burner and puts crew members at risk,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Miller spoke next to a projected image of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2021/oct/22/from-ussr-to-hollywood-how-halyna-hutchins-succeeded-as-a-top-cinematographer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hutchins}}}\uc2  and flanked by standing wreaths of white flowers. A black cloth-covered table, piled high with bouquets and framed photos of Hutchins, became a makeshift altar, illuminated by an array of candles on the ground.\par \par \uc2 Rust\u8217\'20\'19s director, Joel Souza, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2021/oct/24/alec-baldwin-film-halyna-hutchins-vigil"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was injured}}}\uc2  in the shooting last Thursday and the incident is being investigated by the Santa Fe sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s department in New Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Baldwin was rehearsing a scene that involved him pointing a gun \u8220\'20\'1Ctowards the camera lens\u8221\'20\'1D when it accidentally went off, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2021/oct/25/alec-baldwin-was-rehearsing-scene-when-gun-went-off-rust-director-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Souza noted}}}\uc2  in a statement to the sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 Most of those who attended the vigil belong to one of the Hollywood trade unions. Nearly every attendee was masked against the spread of Covid-19, although the event was outdoors, in a crowd that is used to strict set protocols as they work through the ongoing pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Most held a lit candle and many had pinned a white ribbon to their jackets. Some wore their union jackets. One person held up a sign that said \u8220\'20\'1CVote No\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This referred to an upcoming vote to ratify a tentative agreement reached by the union and Hollywood producers earlier this month when members were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/15/hollywood-workers-pay-conditions-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on the verge}}}\uc2  of a strike that would have halted TV and movie-making, with workers protesting against low pay, grueling days without breaks and safety hazards.\par \par \uc2 A mentor to Hutchins from the \uc2 American Film Institute (AFI)\uc2 , Stephen Lighthill, who is also president of the American Society of Cinematographers, implored those gathered \u8220\'20\'1Cto start a conversation about functional guns on sets. There is no place for weapons that can kill on a motion picture.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Most firearms that appear in Hollywood movies or TV shows are real, but have been modified to shoot blanks.\par \par \uc2 The Rust crew had protested about long hours and low pay on the set, and half a dozen had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2021/oct/23/crew-on-baldwin-film-raised-prop-gun-concerns-before-fatal-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walked off the set}}}\uc2  just hours before Hutchins was killed, according to reports on Friday that were corroborated by affidavits released by the Santa Fe sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s department on Sunday night.\par \par \uc2 Serge Svetnoy, who worked as the gaffer, or head electrician on the set, wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/sergey.svetnoy/posts/7126586147366790"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public Facebook post}}}\uc2  on Sunday, that he had been standing \u8220\'20\'1Cshoulder-to-shoulder\u8221\'20\'1D with Hutchins {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2021/oct/22/alec-baldwin-voices-shock-and-sadness-over-shooting-of-halyna-hutchins-on-film-set"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when she was shot}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was holding her in my arms while she was dying. Her blood was on my hands,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to tell my opinion on why this has happened. It\u8217\'20\'19s the fault of negligence and unprofessionalism,\u8221\'20\'1D Svetnoy said.\par \par \uc2 In tying the tragedy on set last week to an industry tendency towards production cost-cutting, Svetnoy\u8217\'20\'19s post added: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is true that the professionals can cost a little more and sometimes can be a little bit more demanding, but it is worth it. No saved penny is worth the LIFE of the person!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ezra Riley, a friend of Hutchins who called her \u8220\'20\'1Cjust amazing\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ca loving person\u8221\'20\'1D said on Sunday he was offered a job on Rust but turned it down because of what he deemed \u8220\'20\'1Csuper low pay\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A request made to Rust Movie Productions to respond on numerous points did not receive an immediate reply.\par \par \uc2 Tom Kang, a friend of Hutchins from AFI, said he last spoke with her about one month ago, when she called to ask a technical question about the camera she would use on Rust. He said that there had been some industry criticism directed at Hutchins since her death for not walking off set and this upset him as she would have regarded the crew members as family.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou spend months. You spent so much time prepping. It\u8217\'20\'19s unpaid. You spend so much of your heart and soul into the images that you\u8217\'20\'19re crafting. You work with the director. And sacrificing time with her son to do this,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s not the type to quit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another friend of Hutchins and fellow cinematographer Antonio Cisneros said she was probably \u8220\'20\'1Ctrying to be the negotiator\u8221\'20\'1D. But her death underscored what he saw as worsening conditions in the industry as a result of digital streaming services forcing productions to be made more cheaply and on tighter schedules. He said he would vote against the settlement with producers, and favors a strike.\par \par \uc2 Kang also decried the conditions often tolerated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou default to the same thing that everyone has been always doing in the subculture of this business: long hours are acceptable. They just assume that people are going to do it, because they have been. And so you have all this stuff contributing \u8211\'20\'13 from the top, the systemic issues, down to the very detailed things that directly happened, they all contributed,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211025ehap00338\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
