\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Buttigieg\u8217\'20\'19s paternity leave is a reminder that the US prioritizes work over family\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,331 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 October 2021\par 13:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The transportation secretary is \u8216\'20\'18at work\u8217\'20\'19 like the heroic workaholic he is \u8211\'20\'13 but that undermines the whole point of parental leave\par \par \uc2 What Pete Buttigieg reveals about paternity leave in America\par \par \uc2 Brace yourself, because what I\u8217\'20\'19m going to say next may shock you. Here we go: an American man adopted newborn twins and then had the audacity to take some time off work to look after them! No, I can\u8217\'20\'19t believe it either. No self-respecting, red-blooded man should be spending time with his tiny babies. He should be in the office, missing those early months, so he can focus on what\u8217\'20\'19s really important. Forget bonding with your vulnerable newborns, there are urgent emails to be sent.\par \par \uc2 The man in question, of course, is the US secretary of transportation, Pete Buttigieg, who recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/aug/17/pete-buttigieg-chasten-parents-adopting-child"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 adopted twins}}}\uc2  with his husband. Conservatives have, predictably, been having homophobic hysterics about the loving family but were tipped over the edge when it emerged that Buttigieg had taken parental leave. The Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , the patron saint of family values, ridiculed Buttigieg\u8217\'20\'19s parenting last week. \u8220\'20\'1CPaternity leave, they call it,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/16/pete-buttigieg-tucker-carlson-fox-news-paternity-leave"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carlson sneered}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CTrying to figure out how to breastfeed. No word on how that went.\u8221\'20\'1D Carlson, by the way, has four children. No word on how much time he spent with them when they were born. No doubt he was a Real Man\u8482\'21\'22 and left his wife, or the nannies, to do all the parenting.\par \par \uc2 Buttigieg\u8217\'20\'19s paternity leave was criticized again on Tuesday when a reporter from the conservative outlet Newsmax asked the White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , whether it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t wise for Buttigieg to come back to work. Psaki {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://people.com/parents/white-house-jen-psaki-responds-reporter-questions-pete-buttigieg-paternity-leave/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 responded by saying}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CHe is at work. I was on a conference call with him this morning.\u8221\'20\'1D She then went on to talk about how important parental leave is.\par \par \uc2 Psaki\u8217\'20\'19s response to the Newsmax has been widely celebrated on social media and by the more liberal news outlets. There have been a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/us-politics/psaki-buttigieg-paternity-leave-newsmax-b1941433.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 number of headlines like}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CPsaki shuts down Newsmax\u8217\'20\'19s reporter\u8217\'20\'19s attack.\u8221\'20\'1D I wonder whether the people praising Psaki actually listened to what she said. Because her very first instinct, let me remind you, was to insist that Buttigieg is still working. (Buttigieg, by the way, had a similar response to Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s attack \u8211\'20\'13 he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/transportation/2021/10/15/pete-buttigieg-time-off-parental-leave/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went on MSNBC}}}\uc2  shortly after to stress that he has \u8220\'20\'1Cbeen available 24/7 on issues that can\u8217\'20\'19t wait\u8221\'20\'1D.)\par \par \uc2 Contrary to all the gushing headlines, Psaki didn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Cshut down\u8221\'20\'1D the Newsmax reporter at all. Rather, she reassured her that Buttigieg may be on leave but he\u8217\'20\'19s still juggling all of his responsibilities like the heroic workaholic he is. And that\u8217\'20\'19s an absolutely terrible response. It undermines everything Psaki later says about the importance of parental leave. Because, last time I checked, parental leave is supposed to be leave. You\u8217\'20\'19re not supposed to work at the same time. I get it: Buttigieg has a very important job. But if the transportation department can\u8217\'20\'19t function without him for a couple of months, then we should all be very worried indeed. A commitment to parental leave is more than just noble words, it means putting into place processes that let people actually take that leave.\par \par \uc2 You expect conservatives to have stone age views about paternity leave but let\u8217\'20\'19s face it, the Democrats have a hell of a long way to go in this department also. Buttigieg\u8217\'20\'19s paternity leave was an amazing opportunity for the Biden administration to communicate just how important paid family leave is. They should have shouted about Buttigieg\u8217\'20\'19s paternity leave from the rooftops from the very beginning. They should have used him as an opportunity to talk about the importance of men taking time off \u8211\'20\'13 and how we will never achieve gender equality until men start taking their caregiving responsibilities seriously. Instead it looks suspiciously like they tried to keep Buttigieg\u8217\'20\'19s leave under wraps. The transportation department didn\u8217\'20\'19t announce that Buttigieg would be taking leave when it began in mid-August. The only reason it made headlines is because Politico broke the news last week with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/west-wing-playbook/2021/10/14/can-pete-buttigieg-have-it-all-494710"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletter}}}\uc2  describing Buttigieg as being \u8220\'20\'1CMIA\u8221\'20\'1D and asking whether Buttigieg can \u8220\'20\'1Chave it all\u8221\'20\'1D. Having it leak out the way it did makes it look like it was some kind of dirty secret. The defensiveness since (he is working, promise!) only reinforces that.\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to be too downbeat. Buttigieg\u8217\'20\'19s paternity leave is a big deal and an example of how social norms are slowly changing for the better. Still, the fact that Psaki is getting wild praise for what was ultimately a pretty dreadful response is depressing. It shows just how much the US \u8211\'20\'13 the only rich country in the world without a law on paid leave for new parents \u8211\'20\'13 prioritizes work over families. It shows just how little the American people seem to expect from their own government. And it shows how even liberals in the US still seem to have a hard time with the idea of a man putting his kids before his job.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a hotline to help men cool down\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re a man in Bogot\u225\'00\'E1, Colombia, dealing with anger issues you can now call the Calm Line to get help. The service was set up to fight violence against women by addressing the root cause: machismo. As the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/10/18/world/americas/colombia-machismo-hotline-masculinity.html?tpcc=nlbroadsheet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times explains}}}\uc2 , the central idea is that \u8220\'20\'1Cmachismo hurts not only women, but men, too, by confining them to a narrow set of emotions and roles \u8211\'20\'13 men must be strong, men cannot fail, men cannot cry \u8211\'20\'13 that leaves them prone to isolation, violence and social conflict\u8221\'20\'1D. The Calm Line was started by the government of Claudia L\u243\'00\'F3pez, who became the first woman and the first openly gay mayor of Bogot\u225\'00\'E1 last year and is just one part of a broader initiative to confront machismo.\par \par \uc2 Ghana\u8217\'20\'19s president calls for \u8216\'20\'18tolerance\u8217\'20\'19 as parliament considers anti-LGBTQ+ law\par \par \uc2 Gay sex is already punishable with up to three years in jail in Ghana. The new bill, which is (of course!) called the family values bill, would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/nbc-out/out-news/ghana-s-president-calls-tolerance-parliament-considers-anti-lgbtq-law-n1282154"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminalize being LGBTQ+ further}}}\uc2 . Ghana\u8217\'20\'19s president, who has said same-sex marriage will never happen under his watch, is calling for civil debate and tolerance as he tries to take away people\u8217\'20\'19s rights.\par \par \uc2 Most rapes in New York went unsolved in 2020\par \par \uc2 Remind me again how we need to keep paying billions of dollars to fund the police if we want to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gothamist.com/news/your-case-is-closed-dont-call-here-any-more-most-rapes-in-new-york-city-went-unsolved-in-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protect women}}}\uc2  ? Because I\u8217\'20\'19m not seeing a particularly good ROI here.\par \par \uc2 Vienna museums open adult-only OnlyFans account to display nudes\par \par \uc2 A Vienna tourist board spokesperson said the city and its cultural institutions had been finding it \u8220\'20\'1Calmost impossible\u8221\'20\'1D to use nude artworks in promotional materials on social media {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2021/oct/16/vienna-museums-open-adult-only-onlyfans-account-to-display-nudes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 because of censorship}}}\uc2 . Perhaps big tech should more on censoring neo-Nazis than nudes.\par \par \uc2 Teen girls are developing tics and TikTok could be a factor\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal has a fascinating story about a surge of teenage girls around the world seeking medical attention for tics, which they link to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/some-doctors-across-us-are-blaming-social-media-app-tiktok-for-surge-in-reported-tics-in-teenage-girls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social contagion and TikTok}}}\uc2 . A rather less sensational explanation, of course, is that the pandemic has screwed everyone\u8217\'20\'19s mental health up.\par \par \uc2 The week in Wizardarchy\par \par \uc2 New Zealand has terminated the contract with its official wizard after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/oct/15/new-zealand-council-ends-contract-with-wizard-after-two-decades-of-service?tpcc=nlbroadsheet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 23 years of service}}}\uc2 . The 88-year-old (who has made some dubious comments about women) is not happy about it. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just they don\u8217\'20\'19t like me because they are boring old bureaucrats and everyone likes me and no one likes them,\u8217\'20\'19\u8217\'20\'19 he complained. Perhaps he should just be thankful for two decades of wizarding: it was a very long spell.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arwa Mahdawi\u8217\'20\'19s new book, Strong Female Lead, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://linktr.ee/ARWAMAHDAWI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 available for pre-order}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211023ehan001jl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
