\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Over 10,000 John Deere workers strike over \u8216\'20\'18years\u8217\'20\'19 of poor treatment\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 868 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 October 2021\par 15:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers wage biggest private-sector strike in the US for two years, saying they were forced to do overtime consistently while company made record profits\par \par \uc2 More than 10,000 production and warehouse workers at 14 John Deere plants in Iowa, Illinois, Kansas, Colorado and Georgia walked off the job at midnight, in the latest in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/01/us-labor-unrest-unions-strikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wave of industrial unrest}}}\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 The workers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.deere.ca/en/our-company/news-and-announcements/news-releases/2021/corporate/2021aug17-uaw-negotiations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 represented}}}\uc2  by nine locals with the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://qctimes.com/business/local/deere-uaw-workers-pass-strike-authorization/article_5996008b-a331-5cd5-91de-fceef0c4a6d6.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted}}}\uc2  99% in favor of a strike authorization in September after receiving the initial six-year contract proposal from John Deere.\par \par \uc2 It is the biggest private sector strike in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/10/14/business/john-deere-strike-uaw/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US for two years}}}\uc2 , since the \uc2 UAW\uc2  led an action against \uc2 General Motors\uc2 . It also comes amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/01/us-labor-unrest-unions-strikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threats of other strikes}}}\uc2  in the US and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/oct/13/american-workers-general-strike-robert-reich"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 widespread labor problems}}}\uc2  in an economy still recovering form the battering inflicted by the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 On 10 October, workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcchicago.com/news/local/most-john-deere-workers-reject-contract-offer-from-illinois-based-tractor-maker/2633979/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted}}}\uc2  overwhelmingly by 90% to reject the tentative contract agreement offered by John Deere, with a strike deadline set for 11.59pm CT on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 David Schmelzer, a quality control inspector at John Deere in Milan, Illinois for 24 years and former chairman of UAW Local 79, said that in 1997 workers took {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wcfcourier.com/union-oks-deere-pact-pay-and-benefits-for-new-hires-halved-under-six-year-contract/article_1cceaf8f-2151-524f-b92a-4fc778b9f85c.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 several concessions}}}\uc2  from John Deere in contract negotiations at the time, which included creating a two-tier system of employees, with workers hired after 1997 receiving fewer benefits.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe sacrificed, and we want that back now,\u8221\'20\'1D said Schmelzer. \u8220\'20\'1CWorkers in this country need to understand that we have a considerable amount of power in this country, if we choose to utilize it, and there\u8217\'20\'19s no reason why we should stand back and let these companies just completely exploit our labor for billions of dollars and fight tooth and nail not to give us anything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said John Deere spent months sending out texts, mailers, and using supervisors to push workers in support of current benefits for employees leading up to the new union contract negotiations, and the company has currently prepared salaried employees to come in to replace workers on strike.\par \par \uc2 During the pandemic, Schmelzer said workers have been forced to work overtime consistently, with 10- to 12-hour days through the week and Saturdays.\par \par \uc2 Through that time, John Deere has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/money/agriculture/2021/08/20/deere-annual-profits-record-broken-three-months-left-go/8209000002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  record profits in 2021, with a $4.7bn profit in the first three quarters of this year, compared to their previous record profit year of $3.5bn in 2013. The company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s22.q4cdn.com/253594569/files/doc_downloads/2021/08/Deere-Company-Q3-2021-10-Q.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent}}}\uc2  over $1.7bn on stock buybacks in the first nine months and paid out $761m in dividends to shareholders.\par \par \uc2 This goes beyond numbers. It\u8217\'20\'19s just as much about how people are treated\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of what\u8217\'20\'19s been going on in the country over the last couple of years has definitely made people more aware of the disparity between corporate and income inequality. Just massive amounts of corporate greed,\u8221\'20\'1D added Schmelzer. \u8220\'20\'1CThe majority of people want a bigger share of the success of this company, the success that we\u8217\'20\'19ve been a major part of.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Prior to the pandemic, John Deere {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/dec/20/iowa-midwest-manufacturing-trump-trade-wars"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laid off}}}\uc2  dozens of workers across several plants and reorganized their workforce, demoting several salaried workers to lower-level positions with less pay, citing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariff wars with China and its impact on demand.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis goes beyond numbers. It\u8217\'20\'19s just as much about how people are treated,\u8221\'20\'1D said a John Deere employee in Illinois who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation. \u8220\'20\'1CRespect from management no longer exists. You can feel the tension in the air. Everybody has been on edge for quite some time. Nearly every day, I would lift my weld hood up to hear employees and managers screaming at each other. They have put highly paid managers on certain operators to watch them and just bird dog them all day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During the last union contract negotiations in 2015, John Deere workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wqad.com/article/life/people/john-deere-and-company-strike-timeline/526-83d1325f-7ca0-45d2-be19-e8671c6a0f77"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved}}}\uc2  the contract by fewer than 200 votes after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/money/agriculture/2015/01/23/john-deere-iowa-layoffs/22210349/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rounds of layoffs}}}\uc2  where hundreds of jobs were cut. The last time John Deere workers went on strike was in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/1986/12/12/business/company-briefs-867686.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1986}}}\uc2 , which lasted 163 days and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.upi.com/Archives/1986/12/11/UAW-strike-Deeres-longest/8511534661200/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 included}}}\uc2  a lockout by the company at other plants in retaliation. The current strike is the largest in the private sector since thousands of \uc2 General Motors\uc2  workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2019/10/25/business/gm-strike-uaw-vote/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walked off the job}}}\uc2  in September 2019.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt goes way deeper than just not liking a contract,\u8221\'20\'1D said another John Deere employee in Illinois. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the summation of years of negative wage movement and probably would\u8217\'20\'19ve happened last contract had the layoff situation not happened.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The worker cited proposed cuts to post-retirement healthcare, inadequate wage increases and inadequate pension benefits that don\u8217\'20\'19t nearly match what pre-1997 John Deere employees receive as reasons why workers overwhelmingly voted against the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/59754-UAW.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest proposed contract}}}\uc2 . For new hires, the retirement pension plans would be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/money/business/2021/10/10/uaw-united-auto-workers-members-overwhelmingly-reject-john-deere-contract-sunday/6020190001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 replaced}}}\uc2  by a 401k.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for John Deere said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.deere.com/en/our-company/news-and-announcements/news-releases/2021/corporate/deere-employees-reject-tentative-agreements/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on the contract rejection by workers: \u8220\'20\'1CJohn Deere remains fully committed to continuing the collective bargaining process in an effort to better understand our employees\u8217\'20\'19 viewpoints. In the meantime, our operations will continue as normal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211014ehae001pc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
