\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US wages are going up, and those who don\u8217\'20\'19t adapt to the new reality will fail\b0\par\par\uc2 Gene Marks \par \uc2 742 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 October 2021\par 14:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Labor is in short supply, so it\u8217\'20\'19s more expensive. It\u8217\'20\'19s simple economics and hankering for pre-pandemic times won\u8217\'20\'19t help\par \par \uc2 There is a significant shortage of labor across the United States. Yes, federal unemployment Covid payments ran out after Labor Day. But still, many workers are reluctant to return to work, wary of their health and safety as the Delta variant continues to rage. Many are looking to switch jobs amid reports of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/jul/03/us-jobs-report-june-trend"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat resignation\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  and employers are desperate to do whatever they can to retain workers as demand continues to remain strong.\par \par \uc2 As a result, job openings are at a historic high and small businesses across the country are begging for workers. So what happens when the demand for a critical commodity is high and the supply of that commodity is in short supply? It\u8217\'20\'19s simple economics: prices go up. Wages are going up.\par \par \uc2 According to data from the \uc2 US Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/CES0500000003"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 average hourly earnings}}}\uc2  of all employees in the US working for private companies rose to $30.85 in September, following large increases in the prior five months. It\u8217\'20\'19s a fair bet that wages will increase even more in the very near future if people are going to eat and heat their homes.\par \par \uc2 Many small business owners across the country \u8211\'20\'13 and across industries \u8211\'20\'13 get this.\par \par \uc2 For example, there\u8217\'20\'19s Amanda Cohen, who owns a vegetarian restaurant in New York City and who raised her starting wages to $25 an hour. She says she hasn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Chad a single problem\u8221\'20\'1D attracting workers to her business. \u8220\'20\'1CWe put the focus on \u8216\'20\'18staff comes first and everything comes second\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D she told a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/labor-shortage-restaurant-owner-wages-pay-hiring-dirt-candy-manhattan-2021-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Business Insider}}}\uc2  reporter. \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t succeed without a staff.\u8221\'20\'1D Cohen has raised her prices 30% to cover these costs.\par \par \uc2 Hourly wages are up at restaurants and retailers elsewhere. And wage increases aren\u8217\'20\'19t just happening in the restaurant and retail sector.\par \par \uc2 The furniture manufacturer Ethan Allen recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globenewswire.com/en/news-release/2021/09/27/2303986/31475/en/Ethan-Allen-Plans-to-Expand-Manufacturing-Production-in-Vermont-Announces-New-Job-Openings-and-Increases-Wages.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  an expansion into Vermont along with an increase in its starting wage to $16 an hour as well as wage increases for more experienced associates. A manufacturer of trailers in Wisconsin is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbc15.com/2021/09/21/stoughton-manufacturer-cites-labor-shortage-wage-increase-decision/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raising wages}}}\uc2  for the second time in a year in response to the labor shortage there. Another manufacturer in Dayton, Ohio, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bizjournals.com/dayton/news/2021/09/28/malt-products-corporation-dayton-entry-level-wages.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 giving}}}\uc2  every employee a $10-an-hour raise. The National \uc2 Association of Manufacturers{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cfodive.com/news/manufacturers-plan-boost-wages-record-rate-nam/606479/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2  that its members plan to increase wages 3.5% over the next year and I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure that\u8217\'20\'19s even enough.\par \par \uc2 The founder of a construction company in Los Angeles is having a hard time finding workers and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.constructiondive.com/news/the-war-for-talent-how-contractors-battle-for-workers/605880/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 admits}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe easiest way, which is the hardest way\u8221\'20\'1D to get and keep workers on his job sites is \u8220\'20\'1Cto pay them more\u8221\'20\'1D. A company that builds roads in Tennessee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newschannel9.com/news/local/jobs-still-open-construction-company-raises-wages-benefits-to-solve-hiring-difficulties"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bumped up}}}\uc2  their starting wages to $14 an hour (this is Tennessee, not San Francisco). A New York construction firm {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/construction-labor-shortage-raises-wages-and-benefits-2021-7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised}}}\uc2  hourly raises to $25 and is now paying hiring bonuses. Paper hangers, pile driver operators and roofers have seen their wages {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox41yakima.com/construction-jobs-with-the-fastest-growing-wages/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increase}}}\uc2  more than 15% over just the past five years.\par \par \uc2 Wage increases are affecting small businesses everywhere \u8211\'20\'13 from the Hudson, New Hampshire, landscaper that is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wmur.com/article/facing-hiring-shortage-a-hudson-nh-landscaping-company-offers-a-paid-trial-for-interested-workers/37120039"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paying}}}\uc2  workers $25 an hour to just \u8220\'20\'1Csee if they want to pursue a position\u8221\'20\'1D to the trucking companies in Wisconsin that are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://spectrumnews1.com/wi/milwaukee/news/2021/09/23/as-truck-driver-shortage-continues--new-drivers-met-with-opportunities-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offering}}}\uc2  hiring bonuses between $5,000 to $15,000. Service industry wages overall {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pymnts.com/smbs/2021/main-street-services-smbs-wages-higher-than-last-year/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are up}}}\uc2  about 10% this year.\par \par \uc2 This is not temporary. Once you increase an employee\u8217\'20\'19s wage you\u8217\'20\'19re not going to ever take it away from them in the future. Which means there\u8217\'20\'19s an enormous shift in overhead structures at small and large firms happening across the country, a shift that will continue for the foreseeable future.\par \par \uc2 I have some clients that are still operating as if it\u8217\'20\'19s pre-Covid. When they\u8217\'20\'19re looking for employees they\u8217\'20\'19re offering compensation similar to the rates they paid before. It hasn\u8217\'20\'19t dawned on them that times have changed and the basic principles of economics are playing out in front of them: when demand exceeds supply, prices go up. Those businesses that accept this reality will adapt and continue to profit. They will hire good people and succeed. Those business owners that refuse to understand this simple concept simply won\u8217\'20\'19t.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211010ehaa00106\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
