\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Death of 1,000 cuts\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  workers on why they\u8217\'20\'19re striking\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 769 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2021\par 06:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Union took issue with company\u8217\'20\'19s threats to outsource jobs from the US to Mexico if workers refuse to accept their proposals\par \par \uc2 About 1,400 \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  workers at four US plants have gone on strike after their current union contracts expired and amid accusations that the cereal giant is offshoring jobs.\par \par \uc2 The workers, represented by the \uc2 Bakery, Confectionery, Tobacco Workers and Grain Millers International Union\uc2  (\uc2 BCTGM\uc2 ), produce cereals for brands, including Rice Krispies, Fruit Loops, Frosted Flakes and Raisin Bran, at plants in Michigan, Tennessee, Nebraska and Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Trevor Bidelman, president of BCTGM Local3G and a fourth-generation employee at the \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  plant in Battle Creek, Michigan, explained workers are on strike against a proposed two-tier system for current and new employees proposed by \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 . Bidelman said \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  wants to not offer pensions to new employees, remove cost of living provisions, and make changes in holiday pay and vacations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re fighting for our future,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bidelman. \u8220\'20\'1CWe made it very clear from the onset of negotiations that this was not something we\u8217\'20\'19ll be able to accept.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shortly before the strike, \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wwmt.com/news/local/kellogg-co-cuts-jobs-in-battle-creek"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced plans}}}\uc2  to cut 212 jobs at the Battle Creek, Michigan, plant over the next two years, including 174 positions represented by the union. The plant currently employs about 390 workers. \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  cited plans to streamline efforts and relocate cereal production to other facilities in North America as reasons for the job cuts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is after just one year ago, we were hailed as heroes, as we worked through the pandemic, seven days a week, 16 hours a day. Now apparently, we are no longer heroes. Very quickly you can go from hero to zero,\u8221\'20\'1D added Bidelman. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t have weekends, really. We just work seven days a week, sometimes 100 to 130 days in a row. For 28 days the machines run then rest three days for cleaning. They don\u8217\'20\'19t even treat us as well as they do their machinery.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bctgm.org/2021/10/05/workers-at-kelloggs-cereal-production-plants-are-on-strike/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 union}}}\uc2  took issue with \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  threatening to outsource jobs from the US to Mexico if workers refuse to accept their proposals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe company continues to threaten to send additional jobs to Mexico if workers do not accept outrageous proposals that take away protections that workers have had for decades,\u8221\'20\'1D said the BCTGM president, Anthony Shelton, in a statement announcing the strikes.\par \par \uc2 In 2018, 187 workers were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.doleta.gov/tradeact/taa/taadecisions/93594.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laid off}}}\uc2  at the Battle Creek plant, with work being shifted to Canada and other US plants. About two years earlier, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.doleta.gov/tradeact/taa/taadecisions/90277.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over 30 workers }}}\uc2  were laid off from the plant, with work outsourced to India, according to approved Trade Adjustment Assistance petitions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like a death of 1,000 cuts. They\u8217\'20\'19re slowly eliminating jobs out of the Lancaster plant,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kerry Williams, who works in processing maintenance at the Lancaster, Pennsylvania, facility. \u8220\'20\'1CWe had to work through this Covid for the last two years and they\u8217\'20\'19ve just shown disrespect for the union name. They even want to remove our union logo from the cardboard cereal box.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 From October 2013 to November 2014, \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bctgm.org/2015/05/14/nlrb-reaffirms-lockout-of-memphis-tenn-kellogg-workers-was-illegal-orders-workers-to-be-made-whole/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 locked out}}}\uc2  about 220 workers from their Memphis, Tennessee, plant while trying to reclassify some workers as \u8220\'20\'1Ccasual\u8221\'20\'1D workers to reduce wages and benefits.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  ultimately ruled the lockout was illegal and ordered the locked-out employees to be reinstated with compensation for the wages and benefits they lost as a result of the lockout, but in 2016 a federal appeals court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://archive.commercialappeal.com/topstories/Appeals-court-overturns-pro-union-order-on-Kellogg-lockout-390848622.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  overturned }}}\uc2  that ruling.\par \par \uc2 Food production workers represented by \uc2 BCTGM\uc2  also went on strike at Frito Lay and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/23/nabisco-factory-workers-striking"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nabisco}}}\uc2  earlier this year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fooddive.com/news/strike-at-mondelez-factories-ends-as-nabisco-workers-agree-to-new-contract/605555/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 winning}}}\uc2  new union contracts a few weeks after walking off the job.\par \par \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s1.q4cdn.com/243145854/files/doc_downloads/2020/K_FY2020_Annual-Report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2  a profit of $1.25bn in 2020. Cereal sales grew {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s1.q4cdn.com/243145854/files/doc_downloads/2020/K_FY2020_Annual-Report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 8%}}}\uc2  in 2020 due to increased demand during the pandemic. The company approved a stock buyback program in February 2020 through December 2022 of $1.5bn. The CEO of Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s, \uc2 Steven Cahillane\uc2 , received {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/paywatch/K"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 around $11.6m}}}\uc2  in total compensation in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  has noted contingency plans are in place to bring in replacement workers, internally and through third parties, to avoid production disruptions.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s said in a statement: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are disappointed by the union\u8217\'20\'19s decision to strike. Kellogg provides compensation and benefits for our US RTEC employees that are among the industry\u8217\'20\'19s best. Our offer includes increases to pay and benefits for our employees, while helping us meet the challenges of the changing cereal business.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211007eha7000un\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
