\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Wave of US labor unrest could see tens of thousands on strike within weeks\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,350 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2021\par 08:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 From healthcare to Hollywood, workers are demanding higher wages, fighting cuts and seeking better safety and conditions\par \par \uc2 Tens of thousands of workers around the US could go on strike in the coming weeks in what would be the largest wave of labor unrest since a series of teacher strikes in 2018 and 2019, which won major victories and gave the American labor movement a significant boost.\par \par \uc2 The unrest spans a huge range of industries from healthcare to Hollywood and academia, and is largely focused on higher wages, fighting cuts and better working and safety conditions, especially in light of Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 It also plays out against a backdrop of an economy bouncing back from the torrid experience of widespread economic shutdowns during the coronavirus pandemic, but one that is still marked by profound inequality.\par \par \uc2 However, the pandemic is also seen as potentially providing a shot in the arm for US labor unions by increasing bargaining power amid increased union drives and labor shortages in some industries.\par \par \uc2 About 24,000 nurses and other healthcare workers at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  in California represented by the United Nurses Associations of California/Union of Health Care Professionals will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unacuhcp.org/press_release/rns-put-the-brakes-on-20-year-labor-management-partnership-say-kaiser-permanente-walked-away-first/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vote}}}\uc2  on a strike authorization {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.beckershospitalreview.com/hr/24-000-kaiser-workers-could-be-heading-for-a-strike-union-says.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from}}}\uc2  1 to 10 October. The union took issue with \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 1% wage increase for workers, cuts to wages for new staff, and benefit cuts in the company\u8217\'20\'19s most recent offer.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have people burned out, complaining of mental health issues and PTSD. We\u8217\'20\'19re in a situation as a union where we\u8217\'20\'19re concerned about the future of nursing, [and] how we recruit and retain nurses and other healthcare professionals,\u8221\'20\'1D said Denise Duncan, president of UNAC/UHCP and a registered nurse.\par \par \uc2 About {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o-hH5IsO5vM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 700 building engineers }}}\uc2  at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  in the San Francisco area are already on strike.\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://ofnhp.aft.org/news/kaiser-workers-voting-strike-authorization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 additional 3,400 health workers }}}\uc2  in Oregon and 7,400 health workers with USW at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/usw-local-7600-will-seek-strike-authorization-from-7-400-kaiser-permanente-workers-301383413.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced }}}\uc2  strike authorization votes. Other unions representing thousands of workers at the company with expiring union contracts are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://usw7600.org/local-national-bargaining-updates-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  considering }}}\uc2  strike authorization votes.\par \par \uc2 In an emailed statement, Kaiser Permanente\u8217\'20\'19s senior vice-president of human resources, Arlene Peasnall, said: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Labor Management Partnership was created 24 years ago, and has a great track record of serving as the framework through which we can solve sometimes very difficult problems. Instead of abandoning it, in the spirit of the partnership we ask union leaders to continue to work constructively toward an agreement, rather than call on nurses and other employees to walk away from patients who need them during this pandemic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After four months of negotiations with the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  (AMPTP), the International Alliance of Theatrical Stage Employees (IATSE) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/business/story/2021-09-20/iatse-calls-for-historic-strike-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced }}}\uc2  a strike authorization vote for 60,000 workers across the film and television industry in the US. If the union moves forward with the strike, it would be the first among Hollywood production workers since the second world war.\par \par \uc2 Hollywood workers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/07/hollywood-film-industry-union-wages-conditions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  long workdays and unsafe schedules that have worsened during the pandemic. Pay rates for many workers have remained low, at just above the minimum wage in the Los Angeles area, while streaming services and shorter television series have also depressed wages.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have much to film if we weren\u8217\'20\'19t here building everything for them,\u8221\'20\'1D said Joe Martinez, a IATSE Local 44 member and special effects technician. \u8220\'20\'1CThey need to start looking at it from a perspective of what would happen if we weren\u8217\'20\'19t there. And then it changes the whole dynamics, because there\u8217\'20\'19s no way they would ever have a central product if we weren\u8217\'20\'19t there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2021/09/iatse-everything-you-need-to-know-about-the-union-planning-a-historic-hollywood-walkout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voting}}}\uc2  starts 1 October, with 75% of each local union\u8217\'20\'19s delegates required to vote in favor of the strike authorization. The AMPTP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/2021/film/news/iatse-strike-authorization-vote-1235069694/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  IATSE left a \u8220\'20\'1Cgenerous, comprehensive package\u8221\'20\'1D on the bargaining table for a strike authorization vote.\par \par \uc2 Several other large groups of workers have voted to authorize strikes around the US while continuing new union contract negotiations, such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://speedmatters.org/news/frontier-workers-california-vote-authorize-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2,000 Frontier Communications workers}}}\uc2  in California, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.12newsnow.com/article/news/local/beaumont-transit-workers-hold-picket-for-better-work-conditions-ahead-of-possible-strike/502-7fe3b220-16d1-4fda-9c23-626747c62f04"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 transit workers }}}\uc2  in Beaumont, Texas, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.beaconjournal.com/story/news/2021/09/21/akron-metro-rta-transport-workers-resume-union-contract-talks/8419200002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Akron, Ohio}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.startribune.com/minneapolis-public-works-employees-reject-contract-offer-authorize-future-strike-if-necessary/600099733/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 450 public works employees}}}\uc2  in Minneapolis, Minnesota, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dailynorthwestern.com/2021/09/23/campus/northwestern-dining-workers-vote-to-authorize-strike-from-compass-group/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dining workers}}}\uc2  at \uc2 Northwestern University\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courant.com/politics/hc-pol-group-home-strike-20210921-mvx5xwdm3vbdti6dlmoofkshdi-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  hundreds of group home workers}}}\uc2  in Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 Graduate workers at Harvard and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://patch.com/new-york/upper-west-side-nyc/bargaining-resuming-reformed-student-worker-union-opens-new-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Columbia University}}}\uc2  are currently holding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hgsuuaw/status/1440837607127089154"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike authorization votes}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Illinois State University\uc2  graduate workers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pantagraph.com/news/local/education/watch-now-illinois-state-university-graduate-workers-union-says-yes-in-strike-authorization-vote/article_0ebb0717-4d8f-5093-9a66-8ac4ece33d11.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 authorized}}}\uc2  the bargaining team to call for a strike vote.\par \par \uc2 About 1,100 coalminers in Alabama have been on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/01/striking-coalminers-alabama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike }}}\uc2  for the past six months and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/business-seattle-washington-strikes-f0b61d72e97f58171224fbebb4c8848f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2,000 carpenters}}}\uc2  in Washington have been on strike since 16 September.\par \par \uc2 On 12 September, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.deere.ca/en/our-company/news-and-announcements/news-releases/2021/corporate/2021aug17-uaw-negotiations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10,100 John Deere production and warehouse workers }}}\uc2  in Iowa, Illinois and Kansas, represented by nine locals with the \uc2 United Auto Workers{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://qctimes.com/business/local/deere-uaw-workers-pass-strike-authorization/article_5996008b-a331-5cd5-91de-fceef0c4a6d6.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted }}}\uc2  99% in favor of a strike authorization if a new six-year union contract isn\u8217\'20\'19t attained through negotiations with the company.\par \par \uc2 After the strike vote, some union members {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kwqc.com/2021/09/14/union-members-picket-outside-john-deere-headquarters/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held a protest}}}\uc2  outside John Deere headquarters in Moline, Illinois, over the company\u8217\'20\'19s first contract offer.\par \par \uc2 According to workers at the strike authorization meetings, John Deere\u8217\'20\'19s first contract offer included increases in healthcare costs, including premiums and deductibles, the end of a no plant closure commitment in the union contract agreement, and reducing eligibility for overtime after eight hours a day to only after exceeding 40 hours in a week. The current union contract {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.deere.ca/en/our-company/news-and-announcements/news-releases/2021/corporate/2021aug17-uaw-negotiations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expires}}}\uc2  on 1 October.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe initial offer is really a slap in the face,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chris Larsen, a member of \uc2 UAW\uc2  Local 74 in Ottumwa, Iowa, who has worked at John Deere for 19 years. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are a lot of dissatisfied people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 John Deere has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/money/agriculture/2021/08/20/deere-annual-profits-record-broken-three-months-left-go/8209000002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2  record profits in 2021, breaking their annual profit record in the first nine months of this year with new earnings records set each quarter in 2021 so far. The company reported a net income of $4.7bn on 2 August, compared with their previous record profit year in 2013 where the annual net income was reported at $3.5bn.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for John Deere declined to comment on the initial offer.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere 2,500 nurses and other hospital staff represented by the \uc2 Communications Workers of America\uc2  are fighting for a new union contract with \uc2 Catholic Health\uc2  at three hospitals in the Buffalo, New York, area. At \uc2 Catholic Health\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Mercy hospital 2,000 workers voted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wgrz.com/article/news/local/catholic-health-no-common-ground-found-union-negotiations/71-9657cfb3-abdd-4255-9779-2bb63a47a113"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 97% }}}\uc2  in favor of authorizing a strike to start on 1 October, when their current contract expires.\par \par \uc2 Tina Knop, a nurse at Mercy hospital, argued unsafe staffing ratios, lack of support staff and supply shortages have worsened working conditions through the pandemic, and made it more difficult to adequately care for patients.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19re fighting for is to have better staffing and \uc2 Catholic Health\uc2  to come forward and work harder to actually staff their facilities,\u8221\'20\'1D said Knop. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re not providing us with support, emotionally or physically, and all they want to do is cut our pay, take away the pension targets, and charge more for our health insurance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cheryl Darling, an immediate treatment assistant at Mercy hospital, recently tested positive for Covid-19 though she is vaccinated, but only found out from a rapid test she took before visiting her mother at a local nursing home. She described chaotic working conditions at the hospital due to staffing shortages from housekeepers to nurses, leaving workers struggling to keep up with the workloads.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m afraid to go into work, because I don\u8217\'20\'19t know what my day is going to be like,\u8221\'20\'1D said Darling. \u8220\'20\'1CI go to bed the night before work and I\u8217\'20\'19m a bundle of nerves, because I don\u8217\'20\'19t know where they\u8217\'20\'19re going to put me or what my work conditions are going to be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blog.chsbuffalo.org/mercy-hospital-open-cwa-strike/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 , Catholic Health\u8217\'20\'19s president, Eddie Bratko, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI want to assure our community that our top priority is the welfare and safety of our patients, and our hospital will remain open and operational during a strike to continue providing safe, high quality care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211001eha100105\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
