\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 LA officers sue over vaccine mandate as police across California threaten to resign\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin in Los Angeles \par \uc2 1,125 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 September 2021\par 01:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Police department employees claim \u8216\'20\'18hostile work environment\u8217\'20\'19 for the unvaccinated and say mandate violates civil rights\par \par \uc2 Los Angeles police department\uc2  (LAPD) employees have sued over requirements they get vaccinated for Covid-19, alleging that the department has created a \u8220\'20\'1Chostile work environment\u8221\'20\'1D for the unvaccinated and that the mandate violates employees\u8217\'20\'19 privacy and civil rights.\par \par \uc2 The suit is one of several aggressive challenges to vaccine mandates by police unions and officers across California, some of whom have threatened mass resignations in response to new rules. It comes as staff at law enforcement agencies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/16/california-police-prison-guards-vaccination-rates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remain unvaccinated at disproportionately high rates}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 LA\u8217\'20\'19s vaccine mandate requires city employees to be vaccinated by 20 October unless they are approved for a specific religious or medical exemption.\par \par \uc2 Six LAPD employees over the weekend asserted in a federal complaint that that policy and its implementation infringed on their rights to \u8220\'20\'1Cbodily integrity\u8221\'20\'1D and constituted \u8220\'20\'1Ccoerced medical treatment\u8221\'20\'1D. The complaint says that officials have threatened to lay off thousands of officers who refuse to get the jab.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit comes amid increasingly fraught debates over employer vaccination mandates in America, which escalated last week after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced the government would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/09/joe-biden-coronavirus-covid-pandemic-white-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily mandate}}}\uc2  that employers with more than 100 employees require workers to get vaccinated or be tested weekly.\par \par \uc2 The federal government and California have had public sector mandates in place for months, but some cities have adopted stricter requirements \u8211\'20\'13 that employees must be vaccinated and cannot submit to regular testing as an alternative.\par \par \uc2 The LA suit, which was brought against the city, the police chief and several other government officials, claims that weekly testing is \u8220\'20\'1Chighly intrusive\u8221\'20\'1D. It alleges that officers have not been given enough time to apply for exemptions, after a Monday deadline.\par \par \uc2 It suggests that police should be able to submit antibody tests showing their immunity given high infection rates in the department and that masks and other \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-pharmaceutical\u8221\'20\'1D interventions allow unvaccinated officers to safely do their job. However in past months, officers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/16/california-police-prison-guards-vaccination-rates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeatedly been documented}}}\uc2  not wearing masks on duty, including while indoors and in close proximity to civilians under arrest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a city that overall believes in vaccinations and believes in wearing masks, and we have first responders that don\u8217\'20\'19t,\u8221\'20\'1D said William Gude, an LA activist who has filmed police without masks and filed complaints. \u8220\'20\'1CThe lawsuit reflects the culture of the department.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An LAPD spokesperson declined to comment on the suit on Monday, but said that as of 3 September, 47% of LAPD staff were fully vaccinated, and 54% had received at least one dose. Those figures are significantly lower than the rates among the general population in LA county, where 76% of eligible residents have had at least one dose. Covid has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2021-09-12/lapd-employees-sue-city-over-vaccination-mandate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed 10 LAPD employees}}}\uc2 , including an officer who died last month amid Delta outbreaks within the agency.\par \par \uc2 Last month, a Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/16/california-police-prison-guards-vaccination-rates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation}}}\uc2  found that police and correctional staff across the state had significantly lower vaccination rates than their surrounding communities. Since then, the California highway patrol (CHP), the largest state police agency in the US, has shared records with \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  showing that, as of mid-August, only 47% of employees had confirmed they were vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 LA is not the only California city where law enforcement unions are fighting vaccine requirements. In San Jose, police and firefighter unions are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sanjosespotlight.com/san-jose-firefighters-police-covid-vaccine-mandate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fighting a vaccine mandate}}}\uc2  similar to the LA policy, warning that the rule could lead to worker shortages. A city spokeswoman said Monday that 82% of sworn police staff were vaccinated, roughly in line with community rates, and that the city had consulted with union leaders in crafting the policy.\par \par \uc2 The police union in San Diego said last week that its internal survey found that 45% of employees would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://timesofsandiego.com/politics/2021/09/10/sdpd-police-union-poll-many-officers-would-consider-resigning-in-face-of-vaccination-mandate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rather be fired}}}\uc2  than comply with the vaccination requirement the city is pursuing. The resistance comes weeks after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2021-08-17/anti-covid-19-vaccine-mask-post-on-sdpd-union-website-prompts-calls-for-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post}}}\uc2  on an online forum allegedly written by a San Diego officer made headlines in the state. \u8220\'20\'1CMyself and another God-fearing Patriot on this Department are building up a coalition of cops who will stand up for our God-given freedoms and are willing to risk it all,\u8221\'20\'1D the author wrote, adding that they refused to get vaccinated or be tested.\par \par \uc2 San Diego spokespeople said on Monday that roughly 50% of police officers had confirmed they were vaccinated as of last week, and that the city was investigating whether that officer\u8217\'20\'19s post violated policy.\par \par \uc2 California prison guards \u8211\'20\'13 which have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ktla.com/news/california/some-california-prison-workers-now-required-to-get-vaccinated-against-covid-19/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some of the lowest law enforcement vaccination rates}}}\uc2  in the state, despite their close contact with vulnerable residents \u8211\'20\'13 are also now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ktla.com/news/california/some-california-prison-workers-now-required-to-get-vaccinated-against-covid-19/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fighting}}}\uc2  new strict vaccination requirements.\par \par \uc2 Christina Ramirez, a \uc2 University of California, Los Angeles\uc2  (UCLA) biostatistics professor and public health expert, said she was not surprised to learn of low vaccination rates among police. Other first responders, including some nurses, had argued against mandates by pointing at high levels of infections last year, she explained. Research had shown that infections have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.science.org/content/article/having-sars-cov-2-once-confers-much-greater-immunity-vaccine-vaccination-remains-vital"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 led to strong immunity}}}\uc2 , she noted, though the CDC recommends people get vaccinated regardless. Last month, LAPD said there were nearly 1,600 employees who were not vaccinated but had \u8220\'20\'1Cnatural immunity\u8221\'20\'1D from infections.\par \par \uc2 Legal experts have said vaccine mandates are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/are-employee-covid-19-vaccine-mandates-legal-what-to-know-11627506537"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 generally lawful}}}\uc2  as long as there are religious and medical exemptions, and the courts have recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2021/09/08/vaccine-mandate-strong-supreme-court-precedent-510280"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upheld policies}}}\uc2 . Health officials have also noted that vaccine mandates have long been in place for other infectious diseases.\par \par \uc2 Mike Feuer\uc2 , the LA city attorney, said he was confident the city would win the legal battle, adding in a statement: \u8220\'20\'1CIt cannot be the case that the health of anyone\u8217\'20\'19s child, anyone\u8217\'20\'19s grandma, anybody in our city could be put at risk because they come into contact with a first responder who hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been vaccinated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vickie Mays, a UCLA professor of psychology and health policy and management, said that mandates could help increase vaccination rates and that she suspected physicians would resist signing off on medical exemptions that were not justified.\par \par \uc2 The low rates among police would probably fuel additional mistrust in police in communities of color, she said. \u8220\'20\'1CNow, when having encounters with police, it\u8217\'20\'19s not just a matter of, will they shoot you? It\u8217\'20\'19s a matter of, if they\u8217\'20\'19re unvaccinated, is there now an additional risk of infection? We know a Black male can be walking down the street and next thing you know is in a scuffle with the police.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CAre you really dedicated to protecting and serving, if science says [vaccination] would be a great way to serve \u8230\'20\'26 but you\u8217\'20\'19re determining you don\u8217\'20\'19t want to do it?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210914eh9e0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
