\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US drone strike mistakenly targeted Afghan aid worker, investigation finds\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 743 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 September 2021\par 15:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Zemari Ahmadi, who died alongside nine others had no connection to terrorism, a \uc2 New York Times\uc2  investigation suggested\par \par \uc2 The US mistakenly targeted and killed an innocent aid worker for an American company in a drone strike in Afghanistan, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/10/world/asia/us-air-strike-drone-kabul-afghanistan-isis.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times suggested}}}\uc2  in an investigation into the country\u8217\'20\'19s final military action of the recently concluded 20-year war.\par \par \uc2 The victim, the newspaper said, was 43-year-old Zemari Ahmadi, who died with nine members of his family, including seven children, when a missile from a US air force Reaper drone struck his car as he arrived home from work in a residential neighborhood of Kabul.\par \par \uc2 US military officials have insisted the targets of the 29 August operation were Islamic State suicide bombers plotting an attack on Kabul airport similar to that which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/26/isis-affiliate-iskp-is-prime-suspect-for-kabul-airport-suicide-bomb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed 13 American troops}}}\uc2  helping with evacuations, and more than 170 others three days earlier.\par \par \uc2 The action, Gen Mark Milley, chair of the US joint chiefs of staff, insisted, was a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7H9KEWOpcRg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 righteous strike}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D against Isis-K members who had been observed at points during the day loading what a surveillance team thought to be explosives into the vehicle and visiting a known safe house of the terrorist group.\par \par \uc2 But the Times\u8217\'20\'19 reporting, compiled from extensive video analysis, interviews with Ahmadi\u8217\'20\'19s colleagues and family, and visits to the scene, casts considerable and potentially devastating doubt on that US official version of events.\par \par \uc2 What the US military observers figured was Ahmadi acting suspiciously, the newspaper said, was him going about his normal business as a worker for the California-based aid group Nutrition and \uc2 Education International\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 His duties that day included dropping off colleagues at various places in Kabul, according to the director of NEI in Afghanistan interviewed by a Times reporter, and the \u8220\'20\'1Cexplosives\u8221\'20\'1D in the vehicle were water cartons that Ahmadi filled from a hose at his office and was taking home to his family.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have nothing to do with terrorism or Isis. We love America. We want to go there,\u8221\'20\'1D said the director, who was quoted anonymously because of the danger of being associated with a US company doing business in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 The Washington Post also published {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/interactive/2021/kabul-drone-strike-questions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its own investigation}}}\uc2  into the deadly US strike, which reached similar conclusions, including that there was no indication of a second, larger explosion at the residential compound that Milley suggested was evidence of explosives in the back of the Ahmadi\u8217\'20\'19s car.\par \par \uc2 The Post quoted several experts who concluded that the damage captured in images of the aftermath of the strike were consistent only with the explosion of a single Hellfire missile from the drone and subsequent rupture of the car\u8217\'20\'19s fuel tank.\par \par \uc2 Ahmadi, who had worked for NEI since 2006, lived at the compound with two of his brothers and their families. The 10 victims, the Times said, were all related to him, including three of his own children, aged between 10 and 20, and five other relatives aged two to seven.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll of them were innocent,\u8221\'20\'1D Emal, Ahmadi\u8217\'20\'19s brother, told the Times. \u8220\'20\'1CYou say he was Isis, but he worked for the Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The relative said Ahmadi and a cousin both had open resettlement applications for the US for themselves and their families.\par \par \uc2 The Times also spoke to neighbors and an Afghan health official who confirmed that children\u8217\'20\'19s bodies were removed from the site. A reporter who visited the following day saw blood splattered on interior walls and ceilings, and photographs provided by Ahmadi\u8217\'20\'19s relatives of the burned bodies of the children.\par \par \uc2 In remarks following the strike, Milley conceded the US was aware of at least three deaths. \u8220\'20\'1CWere there others killed? Yes, there are others killed. Who they are, we don\u8217\'20\'19t know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Department of Defense is conducting its own investigation into the strike, which the Post reported was not yet conclusive. An anonymous senior military official who spoke to the newspaper said the area where Ahmadi\u8217\'20\'19s car was hit, about four miles west of Kabul airport, was not previously known to military or intelligence analysts.\par \par \uc2 US Central Command, the defense department wing reviewing the incident, did not provide comment to either newspaper.\par \par \uc2 The US military already has a deadly record of errors in drone strike operations in Afghanistan. In 2008, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2008/jul/11/afghanistan.usa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 47 civilians, including 39 women and children, were killed}}}\uc2  as they travelled to a wedding.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210911eh9b001gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
