\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Oregon declares emergency as another \u8216\'20\'18extreme heatwave\u8217\'20\'19 looms\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,308 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 August 2021\par 10:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 People in Pacific north-west flock to cooling centers, plus 17 questions to ask yourself before quitting your job\par \par \uc2 Good morning,\par \par \uc2 Oregon has declared a state of emergency as the Pacific north-west prepares for triple-digit temperatures just weeks after a deadly heatwavestruck the region. People streamed into cooling centers and misting stations on Wednesday evening in an effort to escape the sweltering heat.\par \par \uc2 The governor, \uc2 Kate Brown\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1COregon is facing yet another extreme heatwave, and it is critical that every level of government has the resources they need to help keep Oregonians safe and healthy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The declaration went into effect as concerns grew over the safety of residents, some of whom do not have air conditioning. The order is expected to remain in place until 20 August, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/11/oregon-heatwave-pacific-northwest-state-emergency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes}}}\uc2  Hallie Golden.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How hot is it in Oregon? Temperatures in Portland soared to 97F (36.1C) by Wednesday eveningand they are likely to rise to 100F or above for three consecutive days, peaking at around 105F on Thursday. In a \u8220\'20\'1Cworst-case scenario\u8221\'20\'1D, the temperature could reach 111F (44C) in some parts of western Oregon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Are any other areas affected? Exceptionally hot weather was also expected in other parts of the country. The National Weather Service said advisories and warnings would be in effect from the midwest to the north-east and mid-Atlantic until Friday at least.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Oregon\u8217\'20\'19s Bootleg fire has offered new evidence that Indigenous techniques {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/12/the-fire-moved-around-it-success-story-in-oregon-fuels-calls-for-prescribed-burns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 can change how megafires behave}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  vows to change \u8216\'20\'18toxic\u8217\'20\'19 culture as she waits to become New York governor\par \par \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , who is expected to become New York\u8217\'20\'19s first female governor after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/andrew-cuomo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Cuomo}}}\uc2  resigned over sexual harassment allegations, has said she will work to change the \u8220\'20\'1Ctoxic\u8221\'20\'1D work culture in the state\u8217\'20\'19s top office, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/11/kathy-hochul-new-york-governor-in-waiting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Maya Yang}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe promise I make to all New Yorkers, right here and right now: I will fight like hell for you every single day, like I\u8217\'20\'19ve always done and always will,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Democrat, who has served as lieutenant governor since 2015 but remains an unfamiliar face to many in the city.\par \par \uc2 Hochul, 62, said there would be no place in her administration for any Cuomo aides who were implicated by the state attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into his behavior toward women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the end of my term, whenever it ends, no one will ever describe my administration as a toxic work environment,\u8221\'20\'1D Hochul said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Cuomo, 63, announced on Tuesday that he would quit rather than face a likely impeachment trial after the state attorney general, Letitia James, released a report concluding he sexually harassed 11 women, including one who accused him of groping her breast. He denies that he touched anyone inappropriately.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hochul will become the state\u8217\'20\'19s first\par \par \uc2 female governor in 13 days, when Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s resignation takes effect.\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2  employees who work from home could lose money\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2  staff could have their pay cut if they switch to working from home permanently in the wake of the pandemic, according to a company pay calculator seen by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 It is an experiment taking place across Silicon Valley, which often sets trends for other large employers. \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Twitter\uc2  cut pay for remote employees who moved to less expensive areas. However, \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pay calculator tool \u8211\'20\'13 which allows staff to see the effects of a move \u8211\'20\'13 suggests remote employees, especially long-distance commuters, could experience pay cuts without moving.\par \par \uc2 A Google spokesperson said: \u8220\'20\'1COur compensation packages have always been determined by location, and we always pay at the top of the local market based on where an employee works from,\u8221\'20\'1D adding that pay would differ from city to city and state to state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Smaller companies including Reddit and Zillow have shifted to location-agnostic pay models, citing advantages when it comes to hiring, retention and diversity.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US officials have\par \par \uc2 said Afghanistan\u8217\'20\'19s government {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/11/joe-biden-urges-afghans-to-fight-for-their-nation-as-taliban-advance-continues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could fall}}}\uc2  in 90 days and that Kabul could be isolated in as little as a month as the \uc2 Taliban{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/12/afghanistan-taliban-lashkar-gah--army-chief-is-replaced"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 captured the strategic city of Ghazni}}}\uc2 , 95 miles (150km) south of the capital. The insurgents have taken control of the entire city, an official confirmed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Brazilian lawmakers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/11/brazil-flordelis-evangelical-superstar-expelled-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to expel}}}\uc2  the gospel star turned congresswoman\par \par \uc2 Flordelis dos Santos de Souza over her alleged involvement in the murder of her husband, in the latest dramatic chapter of a saga that has gripped Brazil. Flordelis has insisted she is innocent.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 South Korean politicians are seeking to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/aug/12/south-korean-politicians-seek-to-criminalise-semen-terrorism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminalise \u8216\'20\'18semen terrorism\u8217\'20\'19}}}\uc2 , after after a string of men who secretly ejaculated on women\u8217\'20\'19s belongings were punished for \u8220\'20\'1Cproperty damage\u8221\'20\'1D, and not for sexually criminal behaviour.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meet Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/12/joe-biden-secret-weapon-louisa-terrell-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 secret weapon}}}\uc2  : the woman who wrangles with Congress. Louisa Terrell, the White House director of legislative affairs, is the tip of the spear of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s team as she fulfils one of the most difficult jobs in a deeply divided political landscape.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Nearly half of American workers\par \par \uc2 are not paid enough to rent a one-bedroom apartment\par \par \uc2 Rents in the US continued to increase through the pandemic, and a worker now needs to be paid about $20.40 an hour to afford a modest one-bedroom rental. The median wage in the US is about $21 an hour. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/aug/12/housing-renter-affordable-data-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Data}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 National Low Income Housing Coalition\uc2  shows that millions of Americans \u8211\'20\'13 from \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse workers to cab drivers to public school teachers \u8211\'20\'13 are struggling to pay rent.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Ready to quit your job? Here are the 17 questions to ask yourself first\par \par \uc2 It has been termed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Great Resignation\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Cturnover tsunami\u8221\'20\'1D, writes Elle Hunt. Whether it is because of a shift in priorities during the pandemic or simply a desire for a change, many people have left their jobs, or are thinking of leaving. A \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  survey of more than 30,000 workers worldwide revealed that 41% were considering quitting or changing professions this year, but how do you know if you are in desperate need of change or just in a pandemic fug? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/money/2021/aug/12/ready-to-quit-your-job-here-are-the-17-questions-to-ask-yourself-first"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here are 17 questions to ask yourself}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Highest recorded temperature\par \par \uc2 in Europe of 48.8C apparently logged in Sicily\par \par \uc2 The highest temperature in European history {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/11/sicily-logs-488c-temperature-possibly-highest-ever-recorded-for-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears to have been recorded}}}\uc2  in Italy during a heatwave sweeping the country, with early reports suggesting a high of 48.8C (119.85F). If this is accepted by the \uc2 World Meteorological Organization\uc2 , it will break the previous European record of 48C (118.4F) set in Athens in 1977. The temperature was measured at a monitoring station in Syracuse, Sicily, and confirmed soon after by the island\u8217\'20\'19s meteorological authorities.\par \par \uc2 Want more environmental stories delivered to your inbox?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2015/oct/19/sign-up-to-the-green-light-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up to our Green Light newsletter}}}\uc2  to get the good, bad and essential news on the climate every week\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Pilot charged after landing helicopter in Canada town centre to buy ice-cream cake\par \par \uc2 A man\u8217\'20\'19s cravings for a sweet treat have landed him in the hot seat with the police after he landed his helicopter in the centre of a small Canadian town to buy an ice-cream cake. Residents in the town of Tisdale, Saskatchewan watched in astonishment on 31 July as a bright red helicopter descended on the parking lot near the Dairy Queen. Initially, some residents thought the chopper was on the scene for a medical emergency. But when the town\u8217\'20\'19s mayor saw the passenger leave the restaurant with an ice-cream cake, he realized {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/11/canada-helicopter-dairy-queen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the aircraft had a different mission \u8230\'20\'26}}}\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in Touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210812eh8c001jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\png