\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Uber and \uc2 Google\uc2  are latest among tech firms to delay reopening as Delta variant spreads\b0\par\par\uc2 Kari Paul and agencies \par \uc2 825 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 August 2021\par 09:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The companies also announced a vaccine mandate for all employees who will eventually return to offices\par \par \uc2 Major tech firms are reversing plans to return to in-office work in coming weeks, as Covid cases in the US rise due to the emergence of a highly transmissible variant of the virus.\par \par \uc2 Uber, \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , \uc2 Google\uc2 , Apple and \uc2 Netflix\uc2  have delayed planned returns to in-person work recently, while other companies have announced employees can continue remote working indefinitely. The changes come amid the spread of the Delta variant, which now accounts for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/20/delta-variant-us-covid-increase-cdc-director"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 80% }}}\uc2  of new coronavirus cases in the US.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, \uc2 Google\uc2  said it would delay reopening from early September to mid-October. The company also announced a policy that would eventually require all workers who return to be vaccinated. Apple similarly has moved its reopening date to at least October.\par \par \uc2 In an email to more than 130,000 \uc2 Google\uc2  employees worldwide, chief executive officer \uc2 Sundar Pichai\uc2  said the company is now aiming to have most of its workforce back to its offices beginning 18 October instead of its previous target date of 1 September.\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s delay also affects tens of thousands of contractors who \uc2 Google\uc2  intends to continue to pay while access to its campuses remains limited.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis extension will allow us time to ramp back into work while providing flexibility for those who need it,\u8221\'20\'1D Pichai wrote. This marks the third time \uc2 Google\uc2  has pushed back the date for fully reopening its offices.\par \par \uc2 Pichai said that once offices are fully reopened, everyone working there will have to be vaccinated. The requirement will first be imposed at \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s headquarters in Mountain View, California, and other US offices, and will later be extended to the more than 40 other countries where \uc2 Google\uc2  operates.\par \par \uc2 Facebook\uc2  announced a similar policy on Wednesday, saying it will make vaccines mandatory for US employees who work in its offices. Apple is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.macrumors.com/2021/07/28/apple-considering-vaccine-requirement-for-employees/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly }}}\uc2  also considering requiring vaccines.\par \par \uc2 Uber announced Friday it would delay its office reopening and require vaccines when workers are allowed back. \uc2 Twitter\uc2  last week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/joewalsh/2021/07/28/twitter-closes-its-headquarters-again-amid-covid-uptick/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also halted }}}\uc2  reopening plans and closed offices due to the Delta variant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the stuff that needs to be done, because otherwise we are endangering workers and their families,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Dr Leana Wen\uc2 , a public health professor at George Washington University and a former health commissioner for the city of Baltimore. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not fair to parents to be expected to come back to work and sit shoulder-to-shoulder with unvaccinated people who could be carrying a potentially deadly virus.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Because children under the age of 12 aren\u8217\'20\'19t currently eligible to be vaccinated, parents can bring the virus home to them from the office if they are around unvaccinated colleagues, Wen said.\par \par \uc2 The delays from these companies could influence other large employers to take similar precautions, given that the technology industry has been at the forefront of the shift to remote work triggered by the spread of Covid-19.Many {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2021/06/09/facebook-says-all-employees-can-request-permanent-remote-work.html#:~:text=Facebook%20says%20employees%20at%20all,permanent%2C%20full%2Dtime%20remote%20work&text=A%20giant%20digital%20sign%20is,%2C%20on%20October%2023%2C%202019."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 others in the tech industry }}}\uc2  have decided to let employees do their jobs from remote locations permanently.\par \par \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2  on Thursday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2021/07/29/linkedin-says-most-employees-can-work-from-home-forever/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reversed a previous decision }}}\uc2  to require a return to the office, saying its 16,000 employees will have the option to work from home indefinitely. It initially said workers would be required to come back to the office at least 50% of the time. However, those who relocate from cities such as San Francisco to cheaper locations in the US will have their pay docked based on local market rates, the company told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Even before the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  declared a pandemic in March 2020, \uc2 Google\uc2 , Apple and many other prominent tech firms had been telling their employees to work from home.\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to require employees working in the office to be vaccinated comes on the heels of similar moves affecting hundreds of thousands government workers in California and New York as part of stepped-up measures to fight the Delta variant. On Thursday \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced a mandate that all federal government workers be vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 The rapid rise in cases during the past month has prompted more public health officials to urge stricter measures to help overcome vaccine scepticism and misinformation.\par \par \uc2 While other major technology companies may follow suit now that \uc2 Google\uc2  and \uc2 Facebook\uc2  have taken stands on vaccines, employers in other industries still may be reluctant, predicted \uc2 Brian Kropp\uc2 , chief of research for the research firm Gartner. Less than 10% of employers have said they intend to require all employees to be vaccinated, based on periodic surveys by \uc2 Gartner\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Google\uc2  is seen as being such a different kind of company that I think it\u8217\'20\'19s going to take one or two more big employers to do something similar in terms of becoming a game changer,\u8221\'20\'1D Kropp said.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contributed to this report\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210802eh820030h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
