\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18My savings were gone\u8217\'20\'19: millions who lost work during Covid faced benefit system chaos\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 843 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 July 2021\par 12:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Americans thrown out of work by the pandemic faced months-long backlogs in receiving benefits, if they arrived at all\par \par \uc2 Unemployed workers are pushing for reforms and changes to America\u8217\'20\'19s unemployment insurance system after millions of workers experienced severe problems in receiving benefits throughout the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Workers across America faced long delays in receiving unemployment benefits as state systems were quickly overwhelmed with the mass influx of applications that caused months-long backlogs. Meanwhile, workers who made errors on their applications, had missing records or had their claims flagged had their benefits stopped \u8211\'20\'13 and often had difficulty restarting them once problems were resolved.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/features/2021-06-25/u-s-unemployment-at-least-9-million-americans-didn-t-receive-any-benefits#:~:text=They're%20three%20of%20at,U.S.%20Department%20of%20Labor%20data."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 About 9 million Americans}}}\uc2  are estimated to have lost work due to the pandemic but received no unemployment benefits.\par \par \uc2 Sharon Corpening, 60, a freelance writer in Roswell, Georgia, lost all her work contracts when the pandemic shutdowns occurred throughout the US in March last year.\par \par \uc2 As a gig worker, Corpening\u8217\'20\'19s initial unemployment application was denied by the \uc2 Georgia department of labor\uc2 , until the Cares Act provided pandemic unemployment assistance for gig workers a few weeks later. She spent weeks trying to process her application and encountered issues with the unemployment website, and would sit on the phone for hours daily failing to reach a service representative.\par \par \uc2 Like thousands of Americans having trouble with their unemployment applications, Corpening joined a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  group and got involved in helping others through the unemployment process, advocating for systemic reforms and countering narratives that try to portray unemployed workers as \u8220\'20\'1Clazy\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cnot wanting to work\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Corpening took offense at these characterizations and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/21/us-unemployment-benefits-pandemic-cut-republican-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 push}}}\uc2  from Republican governors to prematurely cancel federal unemployment benefits while unemployment systems remain broken.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe still have people who applied eight months ago who have not received a dime,\u8221\'20\'1D said Corpening. \u8220\'20\'1CGeorgia is one of the 26 states that cut off federal benefits, and a week out I will tell you all my bank accounts are overdrawn.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The impacts were detrimental to workers around the US, who fell behind on rent or mortgage or car payments, experienced utility shutoffs and relied on food banks and assistance programs to feed themselves and their families.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of the mass unemployment caused by the pandemic, several organizations, including the Economic Policy Institute and National Employment Law Project, created a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/unemployment-insurance-reform/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report }}}\uc2  with unemployed workers outlining reforms needed to fix the widespread issues to unemployment insurance that were exposed by Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFifty-one different unemployment programs don\u8217\'20\'19t work and I think the past 16 months have proven that these different systems are 51 different excuses,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chevon Hussey, who waited several months to receive unemployment benefits when her mental health and public speaking business shut down due to Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 While waiting for unemployment, Hussey and her husband, whose work hours were cut due to the pandemic, were forced to place their special needs daughter in a group home until they could become financially stable enough to care for her at home again.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe couldn\u8217\'20\'19t rely on the state to get it together any more,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hussey. \u8220\'20\'1CThe federal government had acted so fast to make these dollars available. The unemployment applications were there, but nothing was happening, and our state was saying everything\u8217\'20\'19s working.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kelly Johnson, a single mother in Dunedin, Florida, lost both her jobs as a restaurant manager and personal trainer when the pandemic hit.\par \par \uc2 She started organizing protests through social media around Florida over the issues she and other unemployed workers were facing in not being able to receive benefits through Florida\u8217\'20\'19s unemployment system, which the Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/coronavirus-live-updates/2020/08/06/899893368/gov-says-floridas-unemployment-system-was-designed-to-create-pointless-roadblock"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 admitted}}}\uc2  in August 2020, was designed to create pointless roadblocks for the unemployed to limit the number of paid-out claims.\par \par \uc2 Her experience with Florida\u8217\'20\'19s unemployment system, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.firstcoastnews.com/article/news/regional/florida/national-expert-says-floridas-unemployment-system-is-the-worst-in-the-country/77-e0d10f7e-8374-4f0d-9aff-910777981b41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the worst}}}\uc2  in the US, included long delays in receiving benefits, low payouts due to only one of her job incomes being accounted for in determining her benefit, technical difficulties with the website, and the inability to reach any representatives to help[ her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSix weeks went by still in that phase and all of a sudden my savings were gone and I spent my stimulus on my mortgage and to keep my house running. I was getting really scared, because I was not getting any money coming in,\u8221\'20\'1D said Johnson.\par \par \uc2 She returned to work in the restaurant industry a few months ago, but is still working severely reduced hours while caring for her children who are out of school for the summer. Because Florida cancelled federal extended unemployment benefits early, her unemployment benefits dropped significantly, while re-employment services and childcare services are inadequate or non-existent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy state benefit is $71 a week, and I was working 60 hours a week before the pandemic,\u8221\'20\'1D added Johnson. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we learned going through all of this is we cannot trust the system. We\u8217\'20\'19ve been working our butts off just trying to get our unemployment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210722eh7m0015t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
