\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Fauci says regional vaccine disparities could create \u8216\'20\'18two types of America\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Lois Beckett in Los Angeles and Joan E Greve in Washington \par \uc2 7,891 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 July 2021\par 00:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Top expert encourages vaccination amid Delta variant spreadDefense secretary wants to remove decisions from commandersPresident celebrates 3m jobs created since he took officeTrump financial chief Allen Weisselberg and company charged\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Evening Summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re wrapping up our live US politics coverage for the evening, ahead of an Independence Day weekend that has the wildfire-prone west coast of the US on edge, as celebratory fireworks are set off across a parched landscape that is all-too-ready to burn.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Americans plan to gather in large numbers for the holiday, some still leery of the pandemic, and most, hopefully, outside.\par \par \uc2 Key news updates from today, from myself and Joan Greve. Meanwhile, keep safe, and enjoy the holiday weekend.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2  warned that regional disparities in coronavirus vaccination rates could create \u8220\'20\'1Ctwo types of America\u8221\'20\'1D. Asked about whether he is concerned the delta variant of coronavirus could cause outbreaks in the US, Fauci said, \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think you\u8217\'20\'19re going to be seeing anything nationwide. Because fortunately, we have a substantial proportion of the population vaccinated. So it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be regional.... We\u8217\'20\'19re going to see, and I\u8217\'20\'19ve said, almost two types of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The US jobs report showed the economy added 850,000 jobs last month. In remarks celebrating the jobs report this morning, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the latest numbers represented \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric progress\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CPut simply: our economy is on the move, and we have Covid-19 on the run,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 * Biden and the defense secretary, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , announced support for a bill to remove the review of military sexual assault cases from the chain of command. The Democratic senator Kirsten Gillibrand has been pushing the legislation for several years. Biden said in a statement, \u8220\'20\'1CWe need concrete actions that fundamentally change the way we handle military sexual assault and that make it clear that these crimes will not be minimized or dismissed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The US military will complete the withdrawal of troops from Afghanistan by the end of next month, the White House press secretary told reporters. Biden said earlier today that the operation was \u8220\'20\'1Con track\u8221\'20\'1D with his plans to withdraw all troops by 11 September, denying reports that the withdrawal would wrap up in the next few days.\par \par \uc2 * The death toll from the Surfside condo building collapse increased to 22. The seven-year-old daughter of a Miami firefighter was among the victims whose bodies were recovered from the Florida site. As of now, 128 people remain unaccounted for.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 The Trump Organization\uc2  may face even more legal troubles in the months to come, as New York prosecutors have indicated their investigation is continuing. Prosecutors filed tax crime charges against the company and its chief financial officer, Allen Weisselberg, yesterday.\par \par \uc2 * Nonpartisan voter registration groups in Kansas have filed a lawsuit against the state\u8217\'20\'19s new Republican-backed voting restrictions, saying they will have to suspend all voter registration drives for fear of violating the law. Meanwhile, the Arizona Republic had new details about attempted White House interference in the 2020 election, with Republican officials in Arizona describing multiple inappropriate contacts from the White House and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies over the vote counting, similar to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempted interference in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 * Two-thirds of Americans say they feel democracy is under threat, according to a new poll.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 New law prompts \uc2 League of Women Voters\uc2  to suspend voter registration in Kansas\par \par \uc2 A new Republican-backed Kansas voting law has prompted the nonpartisan \uc2 League of Women Voters\uc2  and other get-out-the-vote groups in Kansas to say they are going to suspend voter registration drives for fear of criminal prosecution, two local media outlets report.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are legitimately concerned that our staff and volunteers might face criminal charges if someone at the farmers market subjectively thinks they might be impersonating an election official and reports them,\u8221\'20\'1D said Caleb Smith, a voter engagement campaign director for Kansas Appleseed, told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kansasreflector.com/2021/07/01/kansas-groups-halt-voter-registration-drives-to-avoid-being-jailed-under-new-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas Reflector}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause [the law] is so broad it can be applied arbitrarily and discriminatory,\u8221\'20\'1D Davis Hammet, the director of Loud Light, a youth voter registration group, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kansascity.com/news/politics-government/election/article252500853.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Kansas City Star}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThese are people who would be registering voters and they\u8217\'20\'19d have to take a very real risk that they\u8217\'20\'19d lose their right to vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The groups have filed a lawsuit against the new law and have asked a judge for a temporary injunction to block implementation of the law until the case is resolved.\par \par \uc2 enltrHeads up: The League of Women Voters of Kansas and other nonprofits are suspending voter registration drives in the state for fear of criminal prosecution under a new Republican-backed state law. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/y5CdnD4qH9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/y5CdnD4qH9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Griffin (@kylegriffin1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kylegriffin1/status/1411036956209815553?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.25am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Anti-white mania\u8217\'20\'19 and comparisons to Nazis: right-wing rhetoric intensifies\par \par \uc2 The extremist rhetoric from rightwing news networks and some elected Republicans is \u8220\'20\'1Cintensifying\u8221\'20\'1D, experts have warned, after a Republican congressman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/y3dn3m/gop-rep-compares-democrats-to-nazis-says-they-want-to-destroy-the-country"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compared}}}\uc2  Democrats to Nazis and a hard-right news host {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/qanon-executions-oann-presenter-traitors-election-1603678"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggested}}}\uc2  tens of thousands of Americans should be executed.\par \par \uc2 On his Fox News show on 24 June, \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , seated in front of a screen blaring the words \u8220\'20\'1Canti-white mania\u8221\'20\'1D, raged that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/fox-news/tucker-carlson-critical-race-theory-will-lead-genocide-white-americans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the US could \u8220\'20\'1Cbecome Rwanda\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , apparently referencing the 1994 genocide in the country, when hundreds of thousands of Tutsi people were slaughtered.\par \par \uc2 enltr"The Fox base prefers propagandistic opinion shows [rather] than any semblance of news. People want to be lied to, and it's above my head to know what to do about that. What do we do about that, when millions of people want to be lied to every day?" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WwL8XqbkKy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/WwL8XqbkKy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hardeep Matharu (@Hardeep_Matharu) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Hardeep_Matharu/status/1410891794955517957?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Brian Stelter, CNN\u8217\'20\'19s chief media correspondent, whose newly released book {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/Hoax/Brian-Stelter/9781982142452"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hoax}}}\uc2  explores how Fox News covered Trump, told an interviewer in June that the US had entered an environment \u8220\'20\'1Cwhere the Fox base\u8221\'20\'1D prefers \u8220\'20\'1Cpropagandistic opinion shows [rather] than any semblance of news\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople want to be lied to, and it\u8217\'20\'19s above my head to know what to do about that,\u8221\'20\'1D Stelter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/washington-post-live/2021/06/24/transcript-brian-stelter-author-hoax-donald-trump-fox-news-dangerous-distortion-truth/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Washington Post}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWhat do we do about that, when millions of people want to be lied to every day?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/02/rightwing-media-fox-news-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Extremist rhetoric from rightwing media and officials is \u8216\'20\'18intensifying\u8217\'20\'19, experts say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Is Breyer retiring? Legal experts watched law clerk ranks for clues\par \par \uc2 In mid-June, my colleague David Smith reported, a group of 18 legal academics issued an extraordinary joint letter urging the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  justice \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2  to retire so that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  can name his successor.\par \par \uc2 The pressure on Breyer to retire was the result of a blunt warning from \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Republican minority leader in the Senate, that Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/jun/14/mitch-mcconnell-supreme-court-stephen-breyer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would not get a supreme court nominee}}}\uc2  confirmed in 2024 if Republicans regain control of the chamber.\par \par \uc2 One proxy for what might be on Breyer\u8217\'20\'19s mind\u8212\'20\'14his staffing choices\u8212\'20\'14suggests he\u8217\'20\'19s not going anywhere immediately.\par \par \uc2 enltrJustice Breyer has hired full complement of four law clerks for fall term, Supreme Court confirms. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DavidLat?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DavidLat}}}\uc2  reported earlier. Suggests but doesn't guarantee Breyer is sticking around.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Stohr (@GregStohr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GregStohr/status/1411025687486533637?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Relief and anxiety as crowds of people plan to gather to celebrate Independence Day\par \par \uc2 Americans enjoying newfound liberty are expected to travel and gather for cookouts, fireworks, concerts and beach outings over the Fourth of July weekend in numbers not seen since pre-pandemic days, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-fourth-of-july-coronavirus-pandemic-lifestyle-business-d829b1f82c7e7c0c51522f67a599538b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There are fears that the mixing of large numbers of vaccinated and unvaccinated Americans at a time when the highly contagious delta variant is spreading rapidly could undo some of the progress made against the scourge.\par \par \uc2 But experts said outdoor events did not pose a lot of risk: \u8220\'20\'1COutdoor stuff remains, I think, pretty safe for unvaccinated or vaccinated people,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Dr. Ashish Jha\uc2 , dean of Brown University\u8217\'20\'19s School of Public Health. \u8220\'20\'1CProbably a packed outdoor concert is not ideal, but short of that, outdoor activity is safe for people. Watching fireworks is fine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We need you to stop the counting\u8217\'20\'19: new details on White House interference in Arizona\par \par \uc2 During the 2020 election, Clint Hickman, a 56-year-old lifelong Republican, was the chair of the Maricopa County Board of Supervisors, which oversees elections in the most populous county in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of the election, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/news/politics/elections/2021/07/02/records-show-trump-allies-kelli-ward-rudy-giuliani-pressured-county-officials-over-election-results/7813304002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona Republic reports}}}\uc2 , he twice let calls from the White House trying to connect him with the president go to his voicemail, as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies tried a range of tactics to try to influence the local elections process in Arizona and other swing states.\par \par \uc2 One of the voicemails to the Arizona Republican official came the very same night that news broke about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s call to Georgia Secretary of State \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , in which Trump asked the Georgia elections official to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/03/trump-georgia-raffensperger-call-biden-washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D enough votes there}}}\uc2  to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s win in the state. The call was recorded, and the Washington Post published the full audio.\par \par \uc2 Hickman, the Arizona official, said he was appalled by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to interfere in Georgia, and that he did not want to be the target of similar interference or record his own conversation with Trump, so he did not return the White House voicemail.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to tape a president, so I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to talk to a president,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING NEWS WITH AUDIO: 'We need you to stop the counting': Records detail intense efforts by Trump allies to pressure Maricopa County supervisors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dYr5XuQ1Vt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/dYr5XuQ1Vt}}}\uc2  via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/azcentral?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @azcentral}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kathytulumello?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @kathytulumello}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WendellK?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WendellK}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dannowicki?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @dannowicki}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 YvonneWingettSanchez ?? (@yvonnewingett) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/yvonnewingett/status/1411041555398332417?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The local Republican official\u8217\'20\'19s defense of the legitimate election process came at a cost: Hickman received death threats, there were protesters outside of his house, and his wife received a phone call threatening sexual violence, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/news/politics/elections/2021/07/02/records-show-trump-allies-kelli-ward-rudy-giuliani-pressured-county-officials-over-election-results/7813304002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona Republic reported}}}\uc2 , noting the threats were serious enough that sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s deputies were dispatched to his home to protect him and his family.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden praises teachers\u8217\'20\'19 sacrifices in address to the \uc2 National Education Association\par \par \uc2 Addressing the nation\u8217\'20\'19s largest union of teachers and other school staff, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  praised teachers\u8217\'20\'19 dedication during the coronavirus pandemic and told them that they deserved a raise. He quipped that American parents who had to educate their kids at home this past year now truly understand why teachers should be paid more, and also made an awkward sex joke about the Lincoln Bedroom.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden, in remarks to the \uc2 National Education Association\uc2 , which counts FLOTUS among its members, jokes "If I didn\u8217\'20\'19t support the NEA, I\u8217\'20\'19d be sleeping in the Lincoln Bedroom alone-and that\u8217\'20\'19s not where we sleep. We don\u8217\'20\'19t sleep in the Lincoln Bedroom, I\u8217\'20\'19d be sent down to it" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/RrWfjveHQx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/RrWfjveHQx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 DJ Judd (@DJJudd) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DJJudd/status/1411074625921073157?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 On the latest episode of \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Politics Weekly Extra podcast, Jonathan Freedland speaks to Yasmeen Abutaleb, author of a new book that details just how serious \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s condition was when he contracted Covid-19 last October:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two-thirds of Americans believe democracy is under threat, polls finds\par \par \uc2 This is Lois Beckett, picking up our live US politics coverage from Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 At the start of this holiday weekend, it\u8217\'20\'19s worth remembering that this country\u8217\'20\'19s national anthem is less a celebration than a question: is the star-spangled banner still waving? Can this embattled democracy endure?\par \par \uc2 This Fourth of July, a lot of Americans are worried about that question: a new poll found that two-thirds of them believe that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/2-out-of-3-americans-believe-u-s-democracy-is-under-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 democracy in the United States is under threat}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The new poll results make an interesting contrast with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/05/us-threat-democracy-russia-china-global-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previous poll of 50,000 people from 53 countries}}}\uc2  around the world, which found that nearly half of respondents believed the United States itself threatened democracy in their home countries. The poll found that the US was seen as a greater threat to democracy than Russia or China.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Two-thirds of U.S. adults believe that American democracy is under threat according to the latest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NewsHour?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NewsHour}}}\uc2  / {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NPR?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NPR}}}\uc2  / {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maristpoll?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @maristpoll}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TnYS66pXqA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/TnYS66pXqA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 PBS NewsHour (@NewsHour) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NewsHour/status/1410886929323810816?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Lois Beckett, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2  warned that regional disparities in coronavirus vaccination rates could create \u8220\'20\'1Ctwo types of America\u8221\'20\'1D. Asked about whether he is concerned the delta variant of coronavirus could cause outbreaks in the US, Fauci said, \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think you\u8217\'20\'19re going to be seeing anything nationwide. Because fortunately, we have a substantial proportion of the population vaccinated. So it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be regional.... We\u8217\'20\'19re going to see, and I\u8217\'20\'19ve said, almost two types of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The US jobs report showed the economy added 850,000 jobs last month. In remarks celebrating the jobs report this morning, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the latest numbers represented \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric progress\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CPut simply: our economy is on the move, and we have Covid-19 on the run,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 * Biden and defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  announced support for a bill to remove the review of military sexual assault cases from the chain of command. Democratic senator Kirsten Gillibrand has been pushing the legislation for several years. Biden said in a statement, \u8220\'20\'1CWe need concrete actions that fundamentally change the way we handle military sexual assault and that make it clear that these crimes will not be minimized or dismissed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The US military will complete the withdrawal of troops from Afghanistan by the end of next month, the White House press secretary told reporters. Biden said earlier today that the operation was \u8220\'20\'1Con track\u8221\'20\'1D with his plans to withdraw all troops by September 11, denying reports that the withdrawal would wrap up in the next few days.\par \par \uc2 * The death toll from the Surfside condo building collapse increased to 20. The seven-year-old daughter of a Miami firefighter was among the victims whose bodies were recovered from the Florida site. As of now, 128 people remain unaccounted for.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 The Trump Organization\uc2  may face even more legal troubles in the months to come, as New York prosecutors have indicated their investigation is continuing. Prosecutors filed tax crime charges against the company and its chief financial officer, Allen Weisselberg, yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Lois will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Maanvi Singh reports on how the delta variant is affecting Americans who lack the protection of a vaccine:\par \par \uc2 Just as the troubling Delta variant was spreading through the US, Charis Hill got a worrying call from their doctor.\par \par \uc2 The medications Hill takes to treat their spondylitis affect their immune system, and they knew the Covid-19 vaccine might not work as well for them as it does for others. So weeks after their second shot, they got a test.\par \par \uc2 The results were shocking: \u8220\'20\'1CNo antibodies were detected in my system,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hill, who lives in California. As the rest of their state celebrated a grand reopening, a jubilant lifting of social distancing rules and mask mandates, Hill went back into isolation.\par \par \uc2 Across the country, coronavirus death rates have plummeted as more and more Americans who are eligible for the vaccine get inoculated. And research from the UK indicates that the current vaccines are effective against new variants.\par \par \uc2 But even in states like California, which has one of the highest rates of per capita vaccination in the world, those who don\u8217\'20\'19t want to get vaccinated, those who can\u8217\'20\'19t, and those like Hill \u8211\'20\'13 for whom the vaccines don\u8217\'20\'19t provide adequate protection \u8211\'20\'13 remain unprotected against Delta, which researchers believe to be the most infectious variant yet.\par \par \uc2 Scientists are also studying whether the variant is deadlier than others, and causes more severe infections. Epidemiologists and other public health experts worry that state and federal policies are leaving the most vulnerable behind.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/01/delta-variant-us-coronavirus-us-vulnerable"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Threat to vulnerable Americans rises as Delta variant spreads }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  voiced similar concerns about the delta variant of coronavirus earlier today, while taking reporters\u8217\'20\'19 questions after delivering prepared remarks on the June jobs report.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the possibility of additional outbreaks in the US because of the delta variant, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CI am concerned that people who have not gotten vaccinated have the capacity to catch the variant and spread the variant to other people who have not been vaccinated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added, \u8220\'20\'1CI am not concerned there is going to be a major outbreak -- in other words, that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have another epidemic nationwide, but I am concerned lives will be lost.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Senior health officials have been going on television this week to spread the message that the delta variant does not pose a threat to vaccinated individuals. They have also encouraged all eligible unvaccinated people to get their shot as quickly as possible.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Regional disparities in vaccination rates could create 'two types of America,' Fauci says\par \par \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s chief medical adviser, warned that regional disparities in coronavirus vaccination rates could create \u8220\'20\'1Ctwo types of America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In an interview airing fully this Sunday, NBC News anchor Chuck Todd asked Fauci whether he believed the delta variant of coronavirus could cause another surge in cases in the US.\par \par \uc2 enltrWATCH: Dr. Fauci says Covid-19 vaccination rate disparities could create 'two types of America' {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/MTP?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #MTP}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jFHF2L9OBC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jFHF2L9OBC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Meet the Press (@MeetThePress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MeetThePress/status/1411012054195056654?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think you\u8217\'20\'19re going to be seeing anything nationwide. Because fortunately, we have a substantial proportion of the population vaccinated. So it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be regional,\u8221\'20\'1D the infectious disease expert told Todd.\par \par \uc2 Fauci added, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to see, and I\u8217\'20\'19ve said, almost two types of America. You know, those regions of America which are highly vaccinated and we have a low level of dynamics of infection. And in some places, some states, some cities, some areas, where the level of vaccination is low and the level of virus dissemination is high. That\u8217\'20\'19s where you\u8217\'20\'19re going to see the spikes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , issued a similar warning yesterday, noting that the delta variant now accounts for about a quarter of new coronavirus cases in the US.\par \par \uc2 According to Walensky, there are about 1,000 US counties where less than 30% of the community is vaccinated. In those regions, the risk of the delta variant spreading is particularly high.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Miami firefighter\u8217\'20\'19s daughter found dead in condo rubble as toll rises to 20\par \par \uc2 Richard Luscombe and Amanda Holpuch report:\par \par \uc2 The seven-year-old daughter of a Miami firefighter was found dead in the rubble of a collapsed condominium, officials said on Friday as they announced the official death toll in Miami had risen to 20 people.\par \par \uc2 The Miami-Dade county mayor, \uc2 Daniella Levine Cava\uc2 , said the rescue mission overnight was difficult as operations stretched into their ninth day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt goes without saying that every night has been immensely difficult for everybody and particularly the families who have been impacted,\u8221\'20\'1D Levine Cava said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut last night was uniquely different. It was truly different and more difficult for our first responders.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese men and women are paying an enormous human toll each and every day, and I ask that all of you please keep all of them in your thoughts and prayers,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Two bodies were recovered overnight, including the young girl. Levine Cava said that the number of unaccounted for stood at 128, down from the previous figure of 145.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the detectives were able to reach and verify the safety of a person in question, we discovered that there were several family members who could have been potentially in the building and now we can mark them as safe,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is very, very good news. That\u8217\'20\'19s 188 people accounted for,\u8221\'20\'1D Levine Cava said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/02/miami-condo-collapse-victims-firefighter-daughter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Miami firefighter\u8217\'20\'19s daughter found dead in condo rubble as toll rises to 20 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Before concluding the naturalization ceremony, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  recognized Sandra Lindsay with an \u8220\'20\'1COutstanding American by Choice\u8221\'20\'1D award, which celebrates noteworthy contributions from naturalized US citizens.\par \par \uc2 Biden recounted how Lindsay, who was the first person in America to get fully vaccinated against coronavirus outside of the clinical trials, immigrated to Queens, New York, from Jamaica when she was 18 years old.\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden recognized Sandra Lindsay as an \u8220\'20\'1COutstanding American by Choice,\u8221\'20\'1D a program that recognizes citizens who have been naturalized. The director of nursing for critical care in Queens, NY is the the first American to be vaccinated against COVID-19 outside of a clinical trial. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xQUtfFwpMc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xQUtfFwpMc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Patsy Widakuswara (@pwidakuswara) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/pwidakuswara/status/1411042717153513481?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 She later got multiple advanced degrees in nursing and now serves as the director of nursing for critical care at a Long Island hospital, where she dedicated herself to helping coronavirus victims during the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Biden noted that Lindsay lost an aunt and an uncle to coronavirus. \u8220\'20\'1CIn her pain, she didn\u8217\'20\'19t lose hope,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The scrubs and badge that Lindsay wore when she received her coronavirus vaccination will be included in the Smithsonian\u8217\'20\'19s national exhibit on Covid-19, Biden added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  noted that six of the 21 immigrants who became citizens at the White House today have served in the US military.\par \par \uc2 The president asked those six new citizens to stand up and be recognized for their military service.\par \par \uc2 Biden then led the room in applauding the six service members.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 After homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas issued the oath of citizenship, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  delivered remarks to congratulate the 21 immigrants present at the White House.\par \par \uc2 Biden noted the new citizens represented many different backgrounds and nationalities. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is one trait you all share in common: courage,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president praised the new citizens, saying they reflected what was best about America. Biden recounted how he once told Chinese President \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  that America is defined by one word: \u8220\'20\'1Cpossibilities\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what America\u8217\'20\'19s built on,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnything is possible in America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president then expressed gratitude to the group for choosing to become citizens, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CThank you for choosing the United States of America, believing that America is worthy of your aspirations, worthy of your dreams.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden participates in naturalization ceremony ahead of July 4 holiday\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now participating in a naturalization ceremony at the White House to welcome new citizens to the US ahead of Independence Day on July 4.\par \par \uc2 enltrHomeland Security Secretary Mayorkas, himself an immigrant from Cuba, delivers the oath of allegiance at a naturalization ceremony in the East Room of the White House, with President Biden looking on. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NkDoARL5G4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NkDoARL5G4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jennifer Epstein (@jeneps) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeneps/status/1411037006252187653?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas, who is the first immigrant to hold his post, issued the oath of citizenship.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, our nation is better than it was yesterday. It is better today in part because we have in you new citizens of it,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayorkas said.\par \par \uc2 The ceremony comes as the Biden administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/02/trump-organization-charges-politics-joe-biden-washington-live?page=with:block-60df57f08f08e77b0abf3c26#block-60df57f08f08e77b0abf3c26"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launches a new effort}}}\uc2  to encourage eligible immigrant to apply for US citizenship.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 During the White House press briefing, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  was asked about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/06/30/kamala-harris-office-dissent-497290"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Politico report}}}\uc2  that some staffers in \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 office are complaining of an \u8220\'20\'1Cabusive\u8221\'20\'1D work environment there.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI try not to speak to or engage on anonymous reports or anonymous sources,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said. \u8220\'20\'1CI will say that the vice-president is an incredibly important partner to the president of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some White House reporters criticized Psaki\u8217\'20\'19s response, noting that the administration often makes senior officials available \u8220\'20\'1Con background\u8221\'20\'1D (meaning they cannot be quoted by name) to explain new policies being enacted.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CI try not to speak to or engage on anonymous reports or anonymous sources,\u8221\'20\'1D says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec}}}\uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , whose team regularly organizes anonymous briefings on topics in the news. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wmPMxEp5ps"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/wmPMxEp5ps}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jennifer Jacobs (@JenniferJJacobs) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JenniferJJacobs/status/1411026223841611779?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Psaki bristled against that criticism, saying on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CI think everyone knows the difference between attacking someone as an anonymous source and providing details on a policy announcement to reporters in an effort to provide information and answer media questions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI think everyone knows the difference between attacking someone as an anonymous source and providing details on a policy announcement to reporters in an effort to provide information and answer media questions\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1411028684044185601?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will soon participate in a naturalization ceremony at the White House to welcome new citizens to the US ahead of the July 4 holiday.\par \par \uc2 The ceremony comes as the Biden administration launches an effort to encourage eligible immigrants to apply for US citizenship.\par \par \uc2 CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/07/02/politics/biden-us-citizenship/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The effort stems from one of President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s early executive orders that called on federal agencies to develop \u8216\'20\'18welcoming strategies that promote integration, inclusion, and citizenship.\u8217\'20\'19...\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The idea is to find a whole-of-government way to reach out to people who are able to naturalize,\u8217\'20\'19 [a] Citizenship and Immigration Services official said, adding that there are 9 million people in the US who are lawful permanent residents who may be eligible to apply for citizenship.\par \par \uc2 That includes, for example, holding naturalization ceremonies at national parks to raise awareness, partnering with the \uc2 US Postal Service\uc2  to display promotional posters at Postal Service facilities about becoming a US citizen, and engaging with the Department of Veterans Affairs and veteran service organizations to find ways to educate service members and veterans on citizenship, according to the strategy, titled \u8216\'20\'18Interagency Strategy for Promoting Naturalization.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 US troops to complete Afghanistan withdrawal by end of August, White House says\par \par \uc2 The US military will complete the withdrawal of all troops from Afghanistan by the end of next month, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had set a goal of withdrawing all troops by September 11, and he said this morning that the military was \u8220\'20\'1Con track\u8221\'20\'1D with those plans.\par \par \uc2 The president denied reports that the withdrawal will be completed within the next few days and then deflected further questions about the operation, instead redirecting focus to the July 4 holiday in the US.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s comments came as US troops departed Bagram, the crucial airbase north of Kabul that has served as the heart of the American military operation in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/02/us-troops-leave-afghanistans-bagram-air-base-after-nearly-20-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US troops leave Afghanistan\u8217\'20\'19s Bagram airbase after nearly 20 years}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  also announced that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will deliver remarks on Sunday evening, at 7.30 pm ET, to commemorate Independence Day and the country\u8217\'20\'19s independence from coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 The July 4 holiday comes as the US is falling short of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s goal to get 70% of American adults at least partially vaccinated by Independence Day.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said of the missed goal, \u8220\'20\'1COur job is not done. The work continues even on July 5.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Taking the podium at the White House press briefing, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  announced that the US will send 1.5 million doses of the Moderna coronavirus vaccine to El Salvador this Sunday.\par \par \uc2 The US has already allocated 80 million coronavirus vaccine doses to countries around the world, as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  promised to do by the end of June.\par \par \uc2 The White House pandemic response team director, \uc2 Jeff Zients\uc2 , also said yesterday that the US will distribute millions more vaccine doses over the next couple of months.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust as our work to vaccinate Americans does not stop on July 4th, our work to help vaccinate the world does not stop at these 80 million doses,\u8221\'20\'1D Zients said at the pandemic response team\u8217\'20\'19s press briefing yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will continue to share tens of millions more US doses over the summer months as we help lead the fight to end the pandemic across the globe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , is now holding her daily briefing, and she is joined by the White House director of the National Economic Council, Brian Deese.\par \par \uc2 The NEC director celebrated this morning\u8217\'20\'19s jobs report, which showed the US economy added 850,000 jobs last month, outpacing expectations.\par \par \uc2 Deese credited \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s economic strategy with accelerating the country\u8217\'20\'19s economic recovery. He also noted that wages have been on the rise in recent months, benefitting American workers.\par \par \uc2 On another note, Deese announced that the president will direct the department of transportation to take steps to protect airline passengers.\par \par \uc2 For example, one proposal is to require airlines to refund checked bag fees if the bag does not arrive in a passenger\u8217\'20\'19s destination city on time.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden welcomes Dodgers to White House to celebrate World Series win\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  welcomed the \uc2 Los Angeles Dodgers\uc2  to the White House today to celebrate their 2020 World Series championship.\par \par \uc2 The team presented Biden and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , a former California senator, with custom Dodgers jerseys to thank them for the invitation.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s jersey was printed with the number 46, and Harris\u8217\'20\'19 had the number 49 stitched on the back, representing Biden being the 46th president and Harris being the 49th vice-president.\par \par \uc2 enltrDODGERS AT WHITE HOUSE: President Biden and Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  receive custom \uc2 LA Dodgers\uc2  jerseys from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/WorldSeries?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #WorldSeries}}}\uc2  champions. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VZvgqzKIGd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VZvgqzKIGd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Forbes (@Forbes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Forbes/status/1411000292473294849?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Congratulating the team on their victory, Biden said the Dodgers\u8217\'20\'19 win had demonstrated how much the country benefits from the joy that sports bring.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the season began, it was easy to feel like we had bigger things to worry about than just sports. And of course we did and we still do,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I think what we discovered is, we need sports more than we ever realized.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president also thanked the team for allowing Dodgers Stadium to be a mass vaccination site this year. The site closed down in late May, but while in operation, it vaccinated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbclosangeles.com/news/sports/get-vaccinated-at-dodger-stadium-ahead-of-reopening-day/2615727/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 12,000 people}}}\uc2  per day.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden, Defense Sec back shifting jurisdiction on military sexual assault cases from armed forces\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his defense secretary, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , took a huge step, long and fiercely debated, today when they both announced their backing for a fundamental change to the military justice system that would remove decisions on prosecuting sexual assault cases from military commanders.\par \par \uc2 US Secretary of Defense \uc2 Lloyd Austin III\uc2  greets German Minister of Defense Annegret Kramp-Karrenbauer at the Pentagon earlier this week. Photograph: DoD/ZUMA Press Wire Service/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 The US president backed the move earlier today and Austin put out a statement and took to \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrWe must do more as a Department to counter the scourge of sexual assault and sexual harassment in our military.\par \par \uc2 Today, I'm directing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DeptofDefense?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DeptofDefense}}}\uc2  to move forward on several reforms on this front. Among them, working with Congress to directly amend the UCMJ by: (1/5)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Secretary of Defense \uc2 Lloyd J. Austin III\uc2  (@SecDef) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecDef/status/1410981473327452168?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Austin earlier had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/pentagon-chief-supports-removing-chain-command-sexual-assault/story?id=78430459"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signaled}}}\uc2  he will work with Congress to remove the prosecution of sexual assault and domestic violence cases from the military chain of command.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Defense Secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  will direct the Pentagon to remove the prosecution of sexual assault, domestic violence, child abuse and retaliation from the military chain of command -- a seismic shift in how the military will handle such crimes. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/A70Hj06xIN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/A70Hj06xIN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mark Satter (@marksatter) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/marksatter/status/1410980606591307786?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 This will stand as one of the biggest overhauls of the military justice system in recent history.\par \par \uc2 Biden is stopping short of backing a congressional effort to strip commanders of oversight of all major crimes, however.\par \par \uc2 The president said he \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongly\u8221\'20\'1D supported the initiative.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSexual assault is an abuse of power and an affront to our shared humanity,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSexual assault in the military is doubly damaging because it also shreds the unity and cohesion that is essential to the functioning of the US military and to our national defense.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press adds:\par \par \uc2 The president formally approved more than two dozen recommendations made by an independent review commission on sexual assault in the military. The changes include a call to shift prosecution decisions on sexual assault cases to special victims\u8217\'20\'19 prosecutors outside of the chain of command and to remove the military\u8217\'20\'19s sexual assault response coordinators and victims advocates from the command structure system.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI look forward to working with Congress to implement these necessary reforms and promote a work environment that is free from sexual assault and harassment for every one of our brave service members,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement endorsing the recommendations by the commission.\par \par \uc2 New York Democratic Senator Kirsten Gillibrand, had the support of 66 senators for a bill that would have independent prosecutors handle felonies that call for more than a year in prison. But other key lawmakers and leaders of the military services have balked at including all major crimes.\par \par \uc2 Biden hailed Gillibrand\u8217\'20\'19s work on the issue.\par \par \uc2 Austin, for the first time, voiced support for taking those sexual assault and related crimes away from the chain of command and letting independent military lawyers handle them.\par \par \uc2 United States Senator Kirsten Gillibrand offers remarks during a press conference to introduce the Vanessa Guill\u233\'00\'E9n Military Justice Improvement and Increasing Prevention Act, earlier this month. Photograph: REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively morning in US politics news out of Washington, DC. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The US jobs report showed the economy added 850,000 jobs last month. In remarks celebrating the jobs report this morning, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the latest numbers represented \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric progress\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CPut simply: our economy is on the move, and we have Covid-19 on the run,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 * Biden addressed concerns that the Delta variant of coronavirus could spread at July 4th celebrations this weekend. \u8220\'20\'1CI am concerned that people who have not gotten vaccinated have the capacity to catch the variant and spread the variant to other people who have not been vaccinated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/useconomy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy}}}\uc2  was boosted by this mornings job report. American companies continue to take on staff as demand picks up. The 850K gains were more than the 700,000 increase which Wall Street expected, and the stock market rose as a result.\par \par \uc2 * More legal troubles likely ahead for \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  after tax crime charges. Manhattan prosecutors filed tax crime charges against the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  and its chief financial officer, Allen Weisselberg, yesterday. In a 15-count indictment, prosecutors charged Weisselberg and his associates with engaging in a 15-year-long scheme to receive company perks without paying proper taxes on them. The charges marked a new chapter in the long-running investigation into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s family business and New York state attorney general Letitia James said this is just the beginning.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden concerned about Covid variant among unvaccinated\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  also addressed concerns that the delta variant of coronavirus could spread at July 4th celebrations this weekend.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am concerned that people who have not gotten vaccinated have the capacity to catch the variant and spread the variant to other people who have not been vaccinated,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am not concerned there\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a major outbreak, in other words that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have another epidemic nationwide. But I am concerned lives will be lost.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr"I am concerned lives will be lost": President Biden says he's not worried about another "major outbreak" of COVID-19, but he fears that people who aren't vaccinated will catch and spread the Delta variant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Nj065CIsxp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Nj065CIsxp}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/crwoM9N24p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/crwoM9N24p}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1410978902076428300?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments come a day after the director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention warned that the delta variant now accounts for nearly a quarter of all new coronavirus cases in the US.\par \par \uc2 The CDC director, \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , noted there are about 1,000 US counties where less than 30% of the community is vaccinated. The variant poses a particularly serious threat to those areas with lower vaccination rates.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration had set a goal of getting 70% of American adults at least partially vaccinated by July 4, but the country has fallen slightly short of that objective.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another reporter asked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  whether he was \u8220\'20\'1Cconfident\u8221\'20\'1D that Congress would enact his American Jobs Plan and American Families Plan.\par \par \uc2 The question prompted a laugh from the president, who asked the reporters, \u8220\'20\'1CWho wants to put money on anything that Congress is going to do? Look, folks, this is a process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden on whether he thinks Congress will enact his plans: "Have you ever been confident about anything with guarantee? Who wants to put money on anything that Congress is going to do? Look, folks \u8212\'20\'14 this is a process." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Nj065CIsxp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Nj065CIsxp}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MJXJM8CpzW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MJXJM8CpzW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1410980607547609089?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden said he was going to \u8220\'20\'1Ctry to be as persuasive as I can\u8221\'20\'1D to convince lawmakers that his plans will help the nation\u8217\'20\'19s economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s comments come as Congress considers action on both the bipartisan infrastructure framework and a Democratic reconciliation bill.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took a few questions from reporters after concluding his prepared remarks on the June jobs report.\par \par \uc2 The first couple of questions focused on the withdrawal of US troops from Afghanistan, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/02/us-troops-leave-afghanistans-bagram-air-base-after-nearly-20-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 service members leave}}}\uc2  the crucial airbase of Bagram north of Kabul after 20 years.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether the withdrawal of troops would be complete in the next few days, Biden said no but noted the US is \u8220\'20\'1Con track\u8221\'20\'1D with their plans to leave Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 The president pushed back against concerns that the Afghan government will fail once the US leaves, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe were in that war for 20 years.\u8221\'20\'1D He added, \u8220\'20\'1CI think they have the capacity to be able to sustain the government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When a reporter asked another question about Afghanistan, Biden tried to brush it aside. \u8220\'20\'1CI want to talk about happy things, man,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  argued the strong June jobs report is a \u8220\'20\'1Cdirect result\u8221\'20\'1D of his $1.9 trillion coronavirus relief package.\par \par \uc2 However, the president emphasized that more work still needs to be done, urging Congress to pass his American Jobs Plan and American Families Plan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow\u8217\'20\'19s the time to accelerate the progress we\u8217\'20\'19ve been making,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s comments come as Democratic congressional leaders work to advance the bipartisan infrastructure framework, as well as a separate reconciliation bill to cover other infrastructure proposals.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 'This is historic progress': Biden celebrates strong jobs report\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now delivering remarks on this morning\u8217\'20\'19s jobs report, which showed the US economy added 850,000 jobs last month.\par \par \uc2 The president said the report \u8220\'20\'1Cbrought us something else to celebrate\u8221\'20\'1D in addition to Independence Day, which will occur on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Biden noted that more than 3 million jobs have been created since he took office, which is the most of any president in the first five months of his term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is historic progress, pulling our economy out of the worst crisis in 100 years,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CPut simply: our economy is on the move, and we have Covid-19 on the run.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 On Wall Street, stocks have hit a new record high as investors welcome today\u8217\'20\'19s employment report.\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500, which covers a broad swathe of the US market, is up 13 points or 0.3% at 4,333 points in early trading.\par \par \uc2 The tech-focused \uc2 Nasdaq\uc2  also hit a new high, currently up 54 points or 0.35% at 14,576.\par \par \uc2 The Dow is slightly higher at 34,661.58 with tech stocks leading the way: \uc2 Intel\uc2 , Apple and \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  are all up around 1.2%, while aerospace manufacturer \uc2 Boeing\uc2  and pharmaceuticals group Walgreens Boots Allianc e are both down around 1.8%.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2021/jul/02/markets-us-jobs-report-opec-ftse-sterling-reopening-inflation-business-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street at record high after jobs report \u8211\'20\'13 business live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will soon deliver remarks on the strong June jobs report, and it seems likely the president will take a victory lap about the economy adding 850,000 jobs last month.\par \par \uc2 Biden and his aides have been tweeting out messages like this since the report came out, citing the numbers as evidence of how the president\u8217\'20\'19s economic strategy is proving effective:\par \par \uc2 enltr3 million jobs since we took office.\par \par \uc2 Our economic plan is working.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1410960025829453831?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s senior advisers have also made a point to compare Biden\u8217\'20\'19s jobs record so far to that of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . From Biden\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump's first year jobs record: 1.8 million new jobs.\par \par \uc2 Biden's first FIVE months: 3 million new jobs. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bEH1fFpFec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/bEH1fFpFec}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ronald Klain\uc2  (@WHCOS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WHCOS/status/1410957873857847298?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Washington Post\u8217\'20\'19s Heather Long said the latest US jobs report demonstrates how raising wages is an effective strategy for attracting workers.\par \par \uc2 The leisure and hospitality industry, where pay has increased by 3.6% in the past three months, accounted for 40% of the 850,000 jobs added last month.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe key jobs day takeaway: Higher wages work.\par \par \uc2 Leisure & hospitality pay jumped 3.6% in past 3 months\par \par \uc2 Leisure and hospitality accounted 40% of the job gains\par \par \uc2 Pay is up ~$1.30 above pre-pandemic rate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZAu0P4ZzbF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ZAu0P4ZzbF}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3UCjXQUpox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3UCjXQUpox}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Heather Long (@byHeatherLong) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/byHeatherLong/status/1410948479686483968?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 US economy added 850,000 jobs last month, latest jobs report shows\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/useconomy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy}}}\uc2  added 850,000 jobs in June, as American companies continue to take on staff as demand picks up.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s more than the 700,000 increase which Wall Street expected.\par \par \uc2 May\u8217\'20\'19s non-farm payroll has been revised up too, to show 583,000 new hires (up from 559,000).\par \par \uc2 But the unemployment rate has risen, to 5.9% from 5.8%, suggesting more people are looking for work.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s business live blog has more details and analysis of the report, so follow along there:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2021/jul/02/markets-us-jobs-report-opec-ftse-sterling-reopening-inflation-business-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy added 850,000 jobs in June as recovery continues \u8211\'20\'13 business live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the face of increasing legal scrutiny on his company, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has remained defiant, attacking the New York investigation as politically motivated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo people see the Radical Left prosecutors, and what they are trying to do to 75M+++ Voters and Patriots, for what it is?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement yesterday.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s attacks on New York prosecutors may energize his loyal supporters, but it won\u8217\'20\'19t stop the investigation from continuing or protect his family business from legal exposure.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 On the surface, the charges against Allen Weisselberg did seem like \u8220\'20\'1Csmaller fish\u8221\'20\'1D. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/06/28/trump-lawyer-manhattan-da-wont-charge-496768"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with Politico,}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer Ronald Fischetti said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like the Shakespeare play Much Ado About Nothing. This is so small that I can\u8217\'20\'19t believe I\u8217\'20\'19m going to have to try a case like this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But surfaces can be deceptive.\par \par \uc2 After three years of subpoenas, supreme court hearings and existential legal rows about the legality of charging a president of the United States with wrongdoing, New York\u8217\'20\'19s fearsome prosecutorial team have charged a little-known 73-year-old accountant with defrauding taxpayers of $1.7m over 15 years. That is big money for most people, but not an amount that would worry Trump, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/profile/donald-trump/?sh=231fa23947bd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Forbes calculates}}}\uc2  is worth $2.4bn.\par \par \uc2 Downplaying the significance of this week\u8217\'20\'19s indictment would, however, be a mistake. Alongside Weisselberg, Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Cyrus Vance\uc2 , and the New York state attorney general Letitia James also charged the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  with tax fraud, the start of a process that could crack the secretive Trump empire wide open.\par \par \uc2 The salvo in the long-brewing legal battle will, at the very least, wrap up Trump for years in legal woes, and at worst could destroy his family business and put not just Weisselberg but the Trump family members who run his business and Trump himself in the dock.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/02/trump-organization-tax-charges-prosecutors-allen-weisselberg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump exposed as prosecutors make first move in high-stakes chess game}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 More legal troubles likely ahead for \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  after tax crime charges\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Manhattan prosecutors filed tax crime charges against the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  and its chief financial officer, Allen Weisselberg, yesterday.\par \par \uc2 In a 15-count indictment, prosecutors charged Weisselberg and his associates with engaging in a 15-year-long scheme to receive company perks without paying proper taxes on them.\par \par \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  finance chief Allen Weisselberg leaves a New York court after surrendering to authorities. Photograph: Spencer Platt/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The charges marked a new chapter in the long-running investigation into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s family business, and more trouble may lie ahead for the company.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/07/01/nyregion/allen-weisselberg-charged-trump-organization.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 In the next phase of the broader investigation into Mr. Trump and his company, the prosecutors are expected to continue scrutinizing whether the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  manipulated property values to obtain loans and tax benefits, among other potential financial crimes, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 New York Attorney General Letitia James indicated there may be more charges to come, saying in a statement yesterday, \u8220\'20\'1CThis investigation will continue, and we will follow the facts and the law wherever they may lead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210702eh720025t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
