\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  boss tells US staff to be back in office in September\b0\par\par\uc2 Kalyeena Makortoff Banking correspondent \par \uc2 520 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 June 2021\par 17:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Chief executive sends \u8216\'20\'18very strong\u8217\'20\'19 message to US staff where many workers are vaccinated against Covid\par \par \uc2 The chief executive of Morgan Stanley has become the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/feb/25/goldman-sachs-boss-wants-bankers-back-to-their-desks-asap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest US banking boss }}}\uc2  to call for an end to remote working, telling his New York staff that anyone who feels safe going out to a restaurant should return to the office.\par \par \uc2 James Gorman\uc2  admitted that the bank would take a different approach in countries such as India or the UK \u8211\'20\'13 where fewer than 25% of its 5,000 London staff have been going to work in person \u8211\'20\'13 due to stricter Covid restrictions.\par \par \uc2 However, in the US, where nearly 90% of staff in its New York headquarters had been vaccinated, the chief executive said he was issuing a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery strong\u8221\'20\'1D message to staff to get back to their desks by Labor Day on 6 September.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you can go to a restaurant in New York City, you can come into the office. And we want you in the office,\u8221\'20\'1D Gorman said during a financial services conference organised by the bank on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake about it: we do our work inside \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  offices. And that\u8217\'20\'19s where we teach, that\u8217\'20\'19s where our interns learn, that\u8217\'20\'19s how we develop people,\u8221\'20\'1D the chief executive added. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s where you build all the soft cues that go with having a successful career that aren\u8217\'20\'19t just about Zoom presentations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also said bankers could not expect large paycheques if they worked away from Wall Street. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you want to get paid New York rates, you work in New York. None of this: \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m in Colorado \u8230\'20\'26 and getting paid like I\u8217\'20\'19m sitting in New York City.\u8217\'20\'19 Sorry, that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The executive claimed he was not \u8220\'20\'1Cdictating\u8221\'20\'1D a return to office, in contrast to \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 , which required US staff to return to their desks on Monday. \u8220\'20\'1CBut [on] Labor Day, I\u8217\'20\'19ll be very disappointed if people haven\u8217\'20\'19t found their way into the office,\u8221\'20\'1D Gorman said. \u8220\'20\'1CThen we\u8217\'20\'19ll have a different kind of conversation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Morgan Stanley\u8217\'20\'19s chief executive is the latest US banking boss to hit out at remote working, which has left white-collar workers running some of the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest businesses from their kitchen tables.\par \par \uc2 The Goldman Sachs chief executive, \uc2 David Solomon\uc2 , made waves after he called remote working an \u8220\'20\'1Caberration\u8221\'20\'1D, while \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s boss, \uc2 Jamie Dimon\uc2 , said it was poor practice for new and younger staff, as well as employees who wanted \u8220\'20\'1Cto hustle\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 suggesting promotions might be harder to clinch for staff who worked from home.\par \par \uc2 A number of European banks, including UK lenders that are more focused on high-street banking, have offered more flexible arrangements for staff. \uc2 NatWest Group\uc2  has said it expects {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/jun/01/natwest-preparing-for-just-13-of-staff-to-work-in-office-full-time"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just 13% of its 64,000 employees}}}\uc2  to work from the office full-time. Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/apr/07/thousands-of-hsbc-and-jp-morgan-staff-to-work-at-home-regularly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HSBC is planning for thousands}}}\uc2  of its staff to work remotely long-term and expects to cut its global office footprint by 40% as a result.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210615eh6f002jv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
