\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Striking coalminers in Alabama energize support across the south\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 906 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 June 2021\par 07:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 United Mine Workers of America\uc2  members are fighting for better wages and benefits and have filed unfair labor practice charges against \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\par \par \uc2 About 1,100 coalminers represented by the \uc2 United Mine Workers of America\uc2  in Brookwood, Alabama, have been on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.al.com/news/2021/04/as-alabama-coal-miners-strike-company-implements-contingency-plan.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike }}}\uc2  since the start of April against \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  amid new union contract negotiations.\par \par \uc2 As the strike heads into its third month, workers are fighting for improvements to wages and benefits after they say several concessions were made by workers under the previous contract in 2016 when \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  took control of the mines in the wake of a bankruptcy filing by \uc2 Walter Energy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The strike has energized support across the state and other parts of the south, in an area that has traditionally been hostile to labor disputes.\par \par \uc2 Last month supporters held a concert to raise money for striking miners that included Mike Cooley of the Drive-By Truckers and comedian Drew Morgan. Labor leaders from around the US, including the AFA-CWA president, Sara Nelson, and the AFL-CIO secretary treasurer, Liz Shuler, have visited the striking miners to lend their support.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWarrior Met still refuses to engage in meaningful negotiations with the UMWA at the bargaining table,\u8221\'20\'1D the UMWA international president, \uc2 Cecil E Roberts\uc2 , said in a recent press release. \u8220\'20\'1CBut they are clearly on the wrong side of history. Community support for the strikers is growing, and now their struggle is gaining nationwide attention.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Strikers say they are suffering the impacts from the lost income, which makes it difficult to make ends meet and afford basic necessities like food and rent or home payments. They have also carried out acts of civil disobedience outside the company\u8217\'20\'19s main offices.\par \par \uc2 James Traweek has worked at \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  for four years at the No 7 mine in Brookwood. He explained miners accepted a $6-an-hour pay cut and reduction in health insurance and retirement benefits during the bankruptcy process five years ago, while adhering to a strict attendance policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were required to work six, sometimes seven days a week, for 12 hours a day. We worked on a four-strike system, which meant missing four days in a year resulted in termination,\u8221\'20\'1D said Traweek. \u8220\'20\'1CThe only thing that was accepted as an excuse was a death in the immediate family. We had to work sick with the flu and many other illnesses in fear of losing our jobs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He noted the workers were just seeking to be compensated what they were worth in wages and benefits comparable to other unionized mines. \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  have brought in replacement workers as part of their continuity plan, the use of which Traweek characterized as \u8220\'20\'1Cgut-wrenching\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re fighting for our families and every other member of the organized labor community across the world. We can\u8217\'20\'19t allow corporate greed to rob us of our dignity and worth,\u8221\'20\'1D added Traweek. \u8220\'20\'1CAfter bringing a company from bankruptcy to record breaking production, we feel we deserve more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the strike, the UMWA filed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/search/case/warrior%20met%20coal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 several unfair labor practice charges}}}\uc2  against \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2 , including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/10-CA-273269"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allegations}}}\uc2  the company threatened bankruptcy and layoffs. Shortly after the strike began, \uc2 Warrior Met Coal{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tuscaloosathread.com/umwa-unity-rally-miners-strike/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained}}}\uc2  a court injunction limiting the number of striking workers on the picket lines on site at the mines and local residents {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://earther.gizmodo.com/alabama-coal-mine-seems-to-be-leaking-pollution-while-i-1846841323"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2  complaints of visible pollution in two creeks from runoff at the mine sites a few weeks into the strike.\par \par \uc2 The company recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/06/warrior-met-coal-inc-hcc-q1-2021-earnings-call-tra/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assured }}}\uc2  investors in an earnings call that customer production volume commitments would be met through 2021, despite the strike\u8217\'20\'19s impact on production at mines in Alabama.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe mining industry is an important part of the community in Brookwood, Alabama. This has been the way of life here for a long time. The wealthy conglomeration in New York that took over the bankrupt \uc2 Walter Energy\uc2  does not care about the men and women that work in the coalmines or their families,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rily Hughett, a coalminer at \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  in Brookwood for 13 years, who worked through the bankruptcy transition in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Hughett explained coalminers face multiple dangers working on the job, including the risk of roof falls, methane gas buildups, low oxygen levels, working with heavy equipment and the pressure on workers to cut corners on safety for the sake of production. Coalmining is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.industriall-union.org/special-report-why-is-mining-still-so-dangerous"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historically}}}\uc2  one of the most dangerous job professions.\par \par \uc2 Though \uc2 Warrior Met Coal{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marketwatch.com/investing/stock/hcc/financials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experienced}}}\uc2  a drop in revenue during the coronavirus pandemic as the coal and steel industries {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/steel-orders-jump-after-covid-19-slowdown-11607947200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slowed down}}}\uc2  production, the company has made millions of dollars in profits since the bankruptcy. They {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tuscaloosanews.com/story/news/local/2021/04/09/union-coal-miners-continue-strike-reject-deal-warrior-met-coal/7167336002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported}}}\uc2  a loss of about $35m in 2020 compared with net income of $302m in 2019.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe only want a fair wage and good insurance for our families, but while they make hundreds of millions of dollars, they should show a little respect for the men and women that brought this company from bankruptcy to a thriving company,\u8221\'20\'1D Hughett added.\par \par \uc2 Workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://umwa.org/news-media/press/strike-continues-for-umwa-members-at-warrior-met-mines/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  rejected}}}\uc2  a tentative agreement offered by the company on 9 April, opting to continue the strike, as they were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jacobinmag.com/2021/05/conservatives-coal-miners-strike-alabama-unfair-labor-practices-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offered}}}\uc2  just a $1.50-an-hour raise over five years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey lowballed it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Marcus Vance, another coalminer on strike at \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI think they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to starve everybody out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210601eh61000un\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
