\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden plans to beef up \uc2 IRS\uc2  to claim up to $700bn in tax from richest Americans\b0\par\par\uc2 Edward Helmore in New York \par \uc2 534 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 April 2021\par 14:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President set to give US tax agency an extra $80bn in resourcesBiden to order federal contractors to pay $15m minimum wage\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans to give tax collectors an extra $80bn to seek as much as $700bn in new revenue from high earners and large corporations, as part of the \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican Families Plan\u8221\'20\'1D set to be unveiled this week.\par \par \uc2 Separately, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2021/04/27/fact-sheet-biden-harris-administration-issues-an-executive-order-to-raise-the-minimum-wage-to-15-for-federal-contractors/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the White House announced}}}\uc2  overnight that Biden will issue an executive order requiring federal contractors to pay a $15 minimum wage to workers on federal contracts.\par \par \uc2 Enhanced tax enforcement by the \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2  (\uc2 IRS\uc2 ), coupled with new disclosure rules, could raise $700bn over the next decade from wealthy people and privately-owned businesses, according to unidentified administration officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/27/business/economy/biden-american-families-plan.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  speaking to the New York Times.}}}\par \par \uc2 The additional funding represents an increase of two-thirds over the agency\u8217\'20\'19s entire funding levels for the past decade.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the administration said the new federal wage floor \u8220\'20\'1Cwill promote economy and efficiency in federal contracting, providing value for taxpayers by enhancing worker {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://scholar.harvard.edu/files/nataliaemanuel/files/emanuel_jmp.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 productivity}}}\uc2  and generating higher-quality work by boosting workers\u8217\'20\'19 health, morale, and effort\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe executive order ensures that hundreds of thousands of workers no longer have to work full time and still live in poverty. It will improve the economic security of families and make progress toward reversing decades of income inequality,\u8221\'20\'1D it said.\par \par \uc2 The measures come ahead of a major policy speech before a joint session of congress on Wednesday in which Biden is expected to frame raising taxes on wealthy Americans employing sophisticated schemes to lower tax exposure and closing corporate loopholes as a way of leveling the tax burden between middle and lower earning Americans and the wealthy.\par \par \uc2 As part of the new tax structure, the administration plans to raise the top income tax rate to 39.6% from 37% and raising capital gains tax rates on those who earn more than $1m a year. Tax rates will also be raised on income for people earning more than $1m per year through stock dividends.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, IRS commissioner \uc2 Charles Rettig{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/13/business/irs-tax-gap.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told a Senate committee}}}\uc2  that tax cheats cost the government as much as $1tn a year and the agency lacked the resources to enforce the tax code. Biden, it is widely reported, plans to use additional money raised by a crackdown to help pay for his \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican Families Plan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But higher taxes face a pushback from Silicon Valley and Wall Street. Administration sources {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/1ad9b56b-671c-47d4-bee1-130ae55a3e14"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told the Financial Times}}}\uc2  that capital gains tax rise will hit only the richest 0.3% \u8211\'20\'13 a \u8220\'20\'1Csliver\u8221\'20\'1D of the US population.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, the White House has said that raising the minimum wage for hundreds of thousands of workers on federal contracts is \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical\u8221\'20\'1D to the functioning of the federal government \u8220\'20\'1Cfor cleaning professionals and maintenance workers who ensure federal employees have safe and clean places to work, to nursing assistants who care for the nation\u8217\'20\'19s veterans, to cafeteria and other food service workers who ensure military members have healthy and nutritious food to eat, to laborers who build and repair federal infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210427eh4r001xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
