\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Virginia police officer fired after donating to Kyle Rittenhouse fundraiser\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 496 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 April 2021\par 08:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  reported lieutenant donated $25 to teenager accused of killing two people during police brutality protest last August\par \par \uc2 The Virginia city of Norfolk has fired a police lieutenant after \uc2 the Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/16/us-police-officers-public-officials-crowdfunding-website-data-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that he donated to and expressed support for Kyle Rittenhouse, the teenager accused of killing two people during a police brutality protest in Wisconsin last summer.\par \par \uc2 City officials announced on Tuesday that police Lt William Kelly had been \u8220\'20\'1Crelieved of duty\u8221\'20\'1D after an internal investigation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHis egregious comments erode the trust between the Norfolk police department and those they are sworn to serve. The city of Norfolk has a standard of behavior for all employees, and we will hold staff accountable,\u8221\'20\'1D the city manager, Chip Filer, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The development came after it was revealed that they had obtained data from a Christian crowdfunding website that was hacked, apparently showing an initially anonymous $25 donation to Rittenhouse\u8217\'20\'19s legal defense fund was linked to Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s work email address.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 , the donation carried the comment: \u8220\'20\'1CGod bless. Thank you for your courage. Keep your head up. You\u8217\'20\'19ve done nothing wrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It went on to say: \u8220\'20\'1CEvery rank and file police officer supports you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to prosecutors, Rittenhouse, who is white, came to Kenosha, Wisconsin, last August as the city was in the throes of chaotic protests after a white police officer shot a Black man, Jacob Blake, in the back during a domestic disturbance. Rittenhouse was 17 at the time.\par \par \uc2 Rittenhouse is accused of opening fire on protesters with an AR-15-style rifle. Two were killed and one was wounded.\par \par \uc2 He has argued he fired in self-defense after the protesters attacked him, and his case became a rallying cry for some conservatives who helped raise money for his bail in November. Others have cast him as a trigger-happy domestic terrorist.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, Rittenhouse was captured on video at a bar wearing a T-shirt that read \u8220\'20\'1CFree as (expletive)\u8221\'20\'1D and flashing white supremacist signs, according to prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 Kelly was initially put on administrative duty Friday, the city said. He can appeal the firing.\par \par \uc2 It was not immediately clear if Kelly had an attorney representing him who could comment on his behalf.\par \par \uc2 Clay Messick, the president of the local police union, told the Pilot that the decision to fire Kelly, not a union member, was \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pilotonline.com/government/local/vp-nw-norfolk-rittenhouse-kelly-20210420-gtfbxgk2ojcxvgjlrlty2bgfky-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disappointing}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were hoping for a full, transparent investigation,\u8221\'20\'1D he told the newspaper. \u8220\'20\'1CBut after 72 hours, I do not believe that is what we got.\u8221\'20\'1D\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The Norfolk police chief, Larry Boone, said in a statement he hoped the \u8220\'20\'1Cperceptions\u8221\'20\'1D of an individual officer wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t undermine community relations with the department.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA police department cannot do its job when the public loses trust with those whose duty is to serve and protect them,\u8221\'20\'1D Boone said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contributed to this report\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210425eh4p0025x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
