\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Amazon workers in Alabama vote against forming company\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 first union\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 896 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2021\par 16:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers at Bessemer warehouse reject joining RWDSULegal challenge looks inevitable due to many contested ballots\par \par \uc2 Amazon has won a victory in its hard-fought campaign to stop workers at an Alabama warehouse forming the company\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 first union\uc2 , in a tough blow for the US labor movement.\par \par \uc2 Workers at the Bessemer, Alabama, plant have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2021/04/09/business/stock-market-today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted }}}\uc2  1,798 to 738 to reject the Retail, Wholesale and Department Store Union. Counting concluded on Friday morning, and attention will now focus on some 505 challenged ballots , but the margin of victory was too greatto change the outcome.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CChallenges are not sufficient in number to affect the results of the election,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The union immediately said it would launch a legal challenge to the result, which is likely to look at the high number of contested ballots and union allegations of unfair tactics during the campaign. Amazon shares rose 0.8% on Friday, adding to earlier gains.\par \par \uc2 The fight to form a union in the warehouse in Bessemer, a suburb north of Birmingham, we eagerly watched by America\u8217\'20\'19s labor movement as one of its most important battles in recent history. Some 5,800 workers were eligible to vote on whether to join the Retail, Wholesale and Department Store Union (RWDSU) as the first unionized Amazon warehouse in the US.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the RWDSU president, \uc2 Stuart Appelbaum\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe won\u8217\'20\'19t let Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s lies, deception and illegal activities go unchallenged, which is why we are formally filing charges against all of the egregious and blatantly illegal actions taken by Amazon during the union vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmazon knew full well that unless they did everything they possibly could, even illegal activity, their workers would have continued supporting the union.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union\u8217\'20\'19s struggle has attracted the support of a range of leftwing politicians and some Republicans eager to court working-class voters. But Amazon had fiercely resisted the effort.\par \par \uc2 Amazon is the US\u8217\'20\'19s second largest private employer after \uc2 Walmart\uc2 , with 950,000 employees, the majority of whom work in its massive warehouses, which have been the subject of numerous reports of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gizmodo.com/exclusive-amazons-own-numbers-reveal-staggering-injury-1840025032"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hazardous }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2020/feb/05/amazon-workers-protest-unsafe-grueling-conditions-warehouse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 grueling}}}\uc2  working conditions.\par \par \uc2 The union drive was the biggest unionization push at the company since it was founded in 1995, and workers faced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/feb/03/amazon-intensifies-severe-effort-discourage-first-warehouse-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fierce lobbying }}}\uc2  from both sides ahead of the vote.\par \par \uc2 Labor organisers hope the publicity surrounding the vote \u8211\'20\'13 even in defeat \u8211\'20\'13 will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/apr/03/amazon-bessemer-union-leaders-labor-movement-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spur other unionization }}}\uc2  attempts, especially in the south, which has been long been a hostile place for unions.\par \par \uc2 Some 3,215 total ballots were received by the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 . A simple majority of votes determined the winner.\par \par \uc2 However, the eligibility of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-amazon-com-union-ballots-exclusive-idINKBN2BW084"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 500 ballots }}}\uc2  was challenged, mostly by Amazon, according to the RWDSU. Union organizers are already making noises about fighting the election, alleging that Amazon has fought the union drive unfairly and intimidated its workers to prevent them making a fair and free choice.\par \par \uc2 Brandon Magner, a labor lawyer and author of the Labor Law Lite newsletter, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThese objections, if sustained by the regional office, could set aside the election result and cause the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  to order another election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Post-election hearings are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/news-publications/publications/fact-sheets/nlrb-representation-case-procedures-fact-sheet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held}}}\uc2  21 days after ballots are tallied.\par \par \uc2 Amazon strongly and publicly opposed the union, from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/jan/27/amazon-seeks-to-block-workers-from-voting-by-mail-in-landmark-union-drive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeking}}}\uc2  to delay the election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/jan/27/amazon-seeks-to-block-workers-from-voting-by-mail-in-landmark-union-drive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing}}}\uc2  for in-person voting, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthout.org/articles/amazon-is-paying-consultants-nearly-10000-a-day-to-obstruct-union-drive/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hiring}}}\uc2  expensive union avoidance consultants, forcing workers to participate in captive audience meetings, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/feb/03/amazon-intensifies-severe-effort-discourage-first-warehouse-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flooding}}}\uc2  workers with anti-union messaging and encouraging them to vote against it, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bhamnow.com/2021/02/25/see-how-amazons-bhm1-employees-make-a-difference/?fbclid=IwAR1mT8DitlGjBoEOvxQsdxCwGhqpayikk2ftYRxwKFlVS1pCQEXGSTwBtlE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sponsoring local media content}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2021/03/29/amazons-pr-campaign-ahead-of-union-vote-shows-how-worried-it-is.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 waging}}}\uc2  PR fights against critics.\par \par \uc2 The union drive has come as Amazon has emerged as one of the biggest winners of the Covid-19 pandemic. The company\u8217\'20\'19s profits have soared amid pandemic lockdowns, as has its share price. \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 , Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s founder, was listed as the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/06/donald-trump-billionaire-rankings-forbes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Forbes magazine }}}\uc2  last week for the fourth consecutive year, with a personal fortune of $177bn.\par \par \uc2 Before the election, Amazon successfully {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/amazon-aims-to-blunt-union-drive-at-alabama-warehouse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed to expand}}}\uc2  the bargaining unit for the election from 1,500 employees proposed by the RWDSU to over 5,800 employees. The union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/news/us-journal/the-alabama-workers-trying-to-unionize-an-amazon-fulfillment-center"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained more than 3,000 union authorization cards}}}\uc2  to warrant the election in late 2020, but it is unclear how many of those employees remained employed with Amazon to be eligible to participate in the election.\par \par \uc2 An unnamed person {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/10-CA-272644"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.al.com/business/2021/02/amazon-accused-of-anti-union-activities-through-website.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unfair labor practice charge}}}\uc2  in February against Amazon in regards to the anti-union website.\par \par \uc2 Mike Foster, the lead organizer for the Bessemer effort, said the union organizing drive offered thanks to the expressions of support they had received from around the world for their effort.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy no means is this the end. Failure isn\u8217\'20\'19t in my category, I don\u8217\'20\'19t even know what that means. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to fight and continue to fight,\u8221\'20\'1D said Foster. \u8220\'20\'1CThis battle has just begun. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know how to do nothing but fight.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Emmitt Ashford, an Amazon worker, expressed frustration and anger over the result, but offered hope and encouragement moving forward.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is just the spark that has started a fire across the United States. The labor movement is alive,\u8221\'20\'1D said Emmitt \u8220\'20\'1COur time will come around again and next time we will win, but at the same time, we\u8217\'20\'19ve done so much, inspired so many people, and gained so much support.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210409eh490020d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
