\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US Capitol: police officer and suspect dead after vehicle rams barrier \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Gabrielle Canon in San Francisco (now) and Joan E Greve in Washington (earlier) \par \uc2 10,049 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 April 2021\par 00:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Officer killed in attack identified as William \u8216\'20\'18Billy\u8217\'20\'19 EvansFull report: one officer and suspect dead after car rams into barrierCapitol police lifts lockdown two hours after vehicle attackVaccinated Americans can travel, CDC saysEconomy adds 916,000 jobs as vaccine rollout fuels hiring boomSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Thanks for reading along today. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of what we\u8217\'20\'19ve covered:\par \par \uc2 * The White House flags are at half-staff following the death of a US Capitol police officer following a violent attack. President Biden shared his condolences while acknowledging the \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat a difficult time this has been for the Capitol everyone who works there, and those who protect it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Questions are now being raised about whether security measures around the Capitol need to be increased.\par \par \uc2 * Law enforcement officials identified 25-year-old Noah Green as the now-deceased suspect in the attack. His motive is still under investigation.\par \par \uc2 * A new policy enacted by the Biden administration will grant an additional $1 billion a month in food assistance with the aim to help $25 million low-income Americans.\par \par \uc2 * The head of the Minneapolis homicide department testified against Derek Chauvin, calling the actions that led to the death of \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally unnecessary\u8221\'20\'1D use of deadly force.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/02/derek-chauvin-murder-trial-george-floyd-knee-neck-deadly-force"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Detective says Chauvin knee on neck a 'totally unnecessary' use of deadly force}}}\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it for me tonight! Hope you all have a great night.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.46am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Lt Richard Zimmerman, who leads the Minneapolis homicide department, testified today in the trial of Derek Chauvin in the murder of \uc2 George Floyd\uc2 , telling the court that Chauvin\u8217\'20\'19s actions were \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally unnecessary\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Chris McGreal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/02/derek-chauvin-murder-trial-george-floyd-knee-neck-deadly-force"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had the story, }}}\uc2  reporting that Zimmerman \u8212\'20\'14 a 4-decade veteran and the longest serving officer on the force \u8212\'20\'14 said he hadn\u8217\'20\'19t ever been trained that placing a knee on the neck was a strategy for restraint during an arrest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf your knee is on a person\u8217\'20\'19s neck, that can kill them,\u8221\'20\'1D Zimmerman said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/02/derek-chauvin-murder-trial-george-floyd-knee-neck-deadly-force"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Detective says Chauvin knee on neck a 'totally unnecessary' use of deadly force}}}\par \par \uc2 Chauvin, who is facing charges of second and third-degree murder, and manslaughter, and possibly up to 40 years in prison, pleaded not guilty on the grounds that his actions were in-line with police protocol.\par \par \uc2 But Floyd, who died after being pinned to the ground for over nine minutes with Chauvin\u8217\'20\'19s knee on his neck, was already in handcuffs, which Zimmerman said should have been enough to safely restrain him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnce you secure or handcuff a person, you need to get them out of the prone position as soon as possible because it restricts their breathing,\u8221\'20\'1D Zimmerman said.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/02/derek-chauvin-murder-trial-george-floyd-knee-neck-deadly-force"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Roughly 25 million Americans could soon see an increase in food assistance as part of a new policy enacted by the Biden Administration, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-us-news-coronavirus-pandemic-california-united-states-e84a9273605a89df32765e4faea2dcc4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 USDA\uc2  estimates show that the new program will send out roughly $1 billion monthly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a real increase in people\u8217\'20\'19s benefits that\u8217\'20\'19s going to make it a little easier to keep food on the table,\u8221\'20\'1D Lindsay Nako, director of litigation and training at the Impact Fund, which represented the California plaintiffs alongside the Western Center on Law & Poverty, told AP.\par \par \uc2 The move marks a shift from former President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to food assistance. Lawsuits filed in Pennsylvania and California against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agriculture secretary, Sonny Perdue, were settled last week by Tom Vilsack, who filled his seat under the Biden administration, the Washington Post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2021/04/02/biden-usda-snap-relief/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 California, the state with the largest population, stands to gain the most from the change, with an increase of nearly $120 million a month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe emergency Snap increases authorized by Congress last year were not being distributed equitably, and the poorest households \u8212\'20\'14 who have the least ability to absorb the economic shocks brought about by Covid \u8212\'20\'14 received little to no emergency benefit increases,\u8221\'20\'1D Vilsack said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CAs part of President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to deliver economic relief and ensure every family can afford to put food on the table, today\u8217\'20\'19s actions will provide much-needed support for those who need it most.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has issued a statement, saying that Officer William Evans, who was killed in the line of duty today, \u8220\'20\'1Cmade the ultimate sacrifice\u8221\'20\'1D on behalf of the American people.\par \par \uc2 enltrStatement by VP Harris on today's attack outside the Capitol honoring Officer Evans, who lost his life, and all Capitol Police and National Guard who responded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/W22ydAaFX5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/W22ydAaFX5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sara Cook (@saraecook) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/saraecook/status/1378112049797079040?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Officer Evans served on the force for 18 years.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Law enforcement officials have identified Noah Green as the deceased suspect responsible for the death of a US Capitol Police officer in today\u8217\'20\'19s violent attack, but an investigation is still underway and authorities have not yet confirmed a motive.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reports that Green, a 25-year-old from Indiana, was a self-described follower of \uc2 Louis Farrakhan\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 who spent decades {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.adl.org/education/resources/reports/nation-of-islam-farrakhan-in-his-own-words"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spreading antisemitic views}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14and his Black nationalist movement, the Nation of Islam.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW from me + {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BrandyZadrozny?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BrandyZadrozny}}}\uc2  : Statement from \uc2 Facebook\uc2  on the Capitol attack suspect Noah Green's purported page.\par \par \uc2 The page praised Nation of Islam and repeatedly warned of a nearing "end times." Story coming shortly. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VUEAe3JAJX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VUEAe3JAJX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Collins (@oneunderscore__) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/oneunderscore__/status/1378097022973177859?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Green\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Facebook\uc2  account, which was taken down on Friday, showed the young man struggled through the past year, and also posted about the \u8220\'20\'1Cend times\u8221\'20\'1D and the anti-Christ.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo be honest, these past few years have been tough, and these past few months have been tougher,\u8221\'20\'1D Green reportedly wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CI have been tried with some of the biggest, unimaginable tests in my life. I am currently now unemployed, after I left my job, partly due to afflictions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Green also shared on social media his belief that the federal government was trying to control his mind.\par \par \uc2 In the hours before he rammed his car into US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  officers, killing one and injuring the other, Green posted \uc2 Instagram\uc2  stories linking to videos of Farrakhan, and a caption that read, \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 U.S. Government\uc2  is the #1 enemy of Black people!\u8221\'20\'1D CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/live-news/capitol-security-threat-04-02-21/h_ffa25ab3eab707b711515c0c863c887a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In March, he credited the Nation of Islam leader with saving him from \u8220\'20\'1Cthe terrible afflictions I have suffered presumably by the CIA and \uc2 FBI\uc2 , government agencies of the United States of America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 From CNN:\par \par \uc2 In his \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post, Green wrote that he had been \u8220\'20\'1Cunknowingly\u8221\'20\'1D taking a drug and suffering from side effects.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Minister is here to save me and the rest of humanity, even if it means facing death,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote, appearing to reference Farrakhan. \u8220\'20\'1CBe willing to deny yourself and follow him, pick up your cross\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 The second officer, who was struck by the car used in today\u8217\'20\'19s attack at the US Capitol is in stable condition, the USCP shared in a tweet.\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE: The other USCP officer who was struck by the car is in stable and non-threatening condition.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2  (@CapitolPolice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CapitolPolice/status/1378105541755539456?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The officer\u8217\'20\'19s name has not been released.\par \par \uc2 According to CNN, retired Lt Gen Russel Honor\u233\'00\'E9, who reported on the need for more security at the Capitol after 6 January, said that today, the system did what it was supposed to.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe security system that worked today was the readiness of the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  out front challenging the car and then the barriers, buffers that went in after 9/11,\u8221\'20\'1D Honor\u233\'00\'E9 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/04/02/politics/us-capitol-incident/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Wolf Blitzer. \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, we lost Officer Evans today, but by and large that system worked. The \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  responded, they stopped him. The system worked.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rep. Matt Gaetz\u8217\'20\'19 communications manager has resigned, leaving the Florida Republican to navigate a federal investigation into whether he sexually trafficked an underage girl, without a spokesperson.\par \par \uc2 Luke Ball, who worked with Gaetz for all three of the Congressman\u8217\'20\'19s terms, is known as one of his closest and longest-serving aides, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , reports.\par \par \uc2 enltrLuke Ball, the communications director for Rep. Matt Gaetz, has resigned, according to a person familiar.\par \par \uc2 Ball quit out of principle, according to the person. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LACaldwellDC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LACaldwellDC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Jansing (@ChrisJansing) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisJansing/status/1378000645026877443?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Gaetz, who gained national attention as a highly vocal Trump-ally, has denied that he paid for sex or that he engaged sexually with a 17-year-old girl. The 38-year-old Congressman has claimed the allegations came from a extortion plot worth $25 million.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reported last week that the Justice Department has linked Gaetz to Joel Greenberg, a former Florida tax collector, who was indicted last year on sex trafficking charges.\par \par \uc2 From the NYT:\par \par \uc2 The Times has reviewed receipts from Cash App, a mobile payments app, and Apple Pay that show payments from Mr. Gaetz and Mr. Greenberg to one of the women, and a payment from Mr. Greenberg to a second woman. The women told their friends that the payments were for sex with the two men, according to two people familiar with the conversations.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, Ron DeSantis, issued an executive order today, banning businesses and government agencies from requiring proof that a person has been vaccinated, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/02/us/florida-vaccine-passport-desantis.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to the New York times.\par \par \uc2 Alleging that the requirement of such proof would \u8220\'20\'1Creduce individual freedom\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Charm patient privacy,\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ccreate two classes of citizens based on vaccination\u8221\'20\'1D the order states that \u8220\'20\'1Cit is necessary to protect the fundamental rights and privacies of Floridians and the free flow of commerce within the state\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Businesses that don\u8217\'20\'19t comply could become ineligible for state funding.\par \par \uc2 So-called \u8220\'20\'1Cvaccine passports\u8221\'20\'1D have become yet another politically divisive issue, and Republican governors have begun rallying against them as government overreach even though the Biden administration has no plans to require them or issue them.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden and the Democrats want to force Americans to present a \u8220\'20\'1Cvaccine passport\u8221\'20\'1D upon demand, yet they oppose presenting an ID to cast a vote.\par \par \uc2 Vaccine passports will have no place in South Carolina. The very idea is un-American to its core.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Gov. Henry McMaster (@henrymcmaster) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/henrymcmaster/status/1377689071523397632?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrA vaccine passport is 100% hypocritical coming from those who oppose voter ID. But it\u8217\'20\'19s entirely predictable after the overreach that we saw this past year.\par \par \uc2 When leaders overstep their authority in a time of crisis, that\u8217\'20\'19s how they break our country.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor Kristi Noem (@govkristinoem) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/govkristinoem/status/1377613266491469837?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Several other countries have already embraced the idea. Israel was the first to roll out their program and with other European countries are considering their own versions, including the UK.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alejandro Mayorkas, the secretary of the homeland security, has released a statement in response to the attack at the Capitol this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy thoughts and prayers go out to the family, friends, and colleagues of the US Capitol police officer who lost his life today protecting the very symbol of our democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayorkas said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is still much to be determined about this attack and DHS offers its full support to Capitol police and DC Mayor Bowser.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 USCP has identified the officer killed in the attack as William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans, an 18-year veteran of the force.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 After two deadly attacks on the US Capitol mere months apart, questions are being raised about whether security measures, which were enhanced after 6 January, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/2021/4/2/22364516/capitol-attack-car-barrier-fence-security-police"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are extensive enough, Vox reports. }}}\par \par \uc2 A review of the security released last month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/context/read-the-report-task-force-1-6-capitol-security-review/91993776-3301-4d92-bb97-658d65c864dc/?itid=lk_inline_manual_4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  that the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  are \u8220\'20\'1Cunderstaffed, insufficiently equipped and inadequately trained\u8221\'20\'1D to defend the nation\u8217\'20\'19s seat of government from future attacks.\par \par \uc2 In a 15-page draft report, commissioned by the House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , retired army L. Gen Russel Honor\u233\'00\'E9 called for adding 854 officers, including 424 to specialize in intelligence, dignitary protection and operational planning.\par \par \uc2 He also recommended additional fencing, specifically barriers that are \u8220\'20\'1Ceasily erected and deconstructed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrMore of my interview with former {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FBI?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FBI}}}\uc2  agent Brad Garrett about today's attack at the U.S. Capitol. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BradInvestigate?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BradInvestigate}}}\uc2  tells me the current threat is too high not to add more security at the Capitol. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/7NewsDC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @7NewsDC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xQSQFoW56n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xQSQFoW56n}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Scott Taylor 7 News I-Team (@ScottTaylorTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ScottTaylorTV/status/1378098861122723844?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Roughly four miles of 7ft-high \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-scalable\u8221\'20\'1D metal fencing was set up around the Capitol complex following the 6 January riot but it was taken down in March, according to Vox.\par \par \uc2 Representative Tim Ryan told reporters today that new permanent additions to security are being considered by lawmakers. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll be reviewing everything, at this point, including the fencing,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, emphasizing that there are still many unknowns about today\u8217\'20\'19s incident\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t get too far ahead of ourselves without knowing that we have the ability to protect the Capitol, to harden the Capitol,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden orders White House flags at half-staff\par \par \uc2 Gabrielle Canon here, signing in from the west coast to take you through the Friday afternoon news.\par \par \uc2 President Biden has issued a statement on today\u8217\'20\'19s violent attack at the US Capitol that resulted in the death of Officer William Evans and left another US Capitol police officer injured.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know what a difficult time this has been for the Capitol, everyone who works there, and those who protect it,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in the statement, after expressing his condolences to Evans\u8217\'20\'19 family. His death is the second line-of-duty death this year for the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2 , who also lost an officer during the 6 January attack, and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/car-rams-capitol-barricade-add0fea76244f1755344aa856ee64ecd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seventh in the agency\u8217\'20\'19s history}}}\uc2 , according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Here is Biden\u8217\'20\'19s full statement:\par \par \uc2 Jill and I were heartbroken to learn of the violent attack at a security checkpoint on the U.S. Capitol grounds, which killed Officer William Evans of the \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2 , and left a fellow officer fighting for his life. We send our heartfelt condolences to Officer Evans\u8217\'20\'19 family, and everyone grieving his loss. We know what a difficult time this has been for the Capitol, everyone who works there, and those who protect it.\par \par \uc2 I have been receiving ongoing briefings from my Homeland Security Advisor, and will be getting further updates as the investigation proceeds.\par \par \uc2 I want to express the nation\u8217\'20\'19s gratitude to the Capitol Police, the National Guard Immediate Response Force, and others who quickly responded to this attack. As we mourn the loss of yet another courageous Capitol Police officer, I have ordered that the White House flags be lowered to half-mast.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me on this sad day in Washington. My west coast colleague Gabrielle Canon will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * US Capitol police officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans was killed after a car rammed through a security barrier at the Capitol this afternoon. The acting USCP chief, Yogananda Pittman, said a suspect attempted to drive through the barrier and then exited his car wielding a knife. The suspect lunged at the two officers present, and at least one of the officers opened fire on the man, who later died of his injuries.\par \par \uc2 * The Capitol attack did not appear to be terrorism-related, the acting chief of the Metropolitan police department of DC said. At an afternoon press conference, the acting MPD chief, Robert Contee, said it did not appear the Capitol was under active threat. The lockdown at the Capitol was lifted soon afterwards.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  mourned Evans as \u8220\'20\'1Ca martyr for our democracy\u8221\'20\'1D. The House speaker said in a statement: \u8220\'20\'1CToday, once again, these heroes risked their lives to protect our Capitol and our country, with the same extraordinary selflessness and spirit of service seen on January 6. On behalf of the entire House, we are profoundly grateful.\u8221\'20\'1D A spokesperson for Pelosi also said the Capitol flags will be lowered to half-staff in honor of Evans.\par \par \uc2 * The Major League Baseball All-Star Game is being moved out of Georgia over the state\u8217\'20\'19s new voting law. The law, which Republican Governor Brian Kemp signed late last month, restricts access to voting, and it has been widely criticized by Democrats and voting rights activists.\par \par \uc2 * Fully vaccinated Americans can travel without quarantining, the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  said. According to the CDC\u8217\'20\'19s newest guidelines, vaccinated individuals can travel without getting tested for coronavirus or quarantining after their return. The agency said such travel is low-risk for those who have been vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 Gabrielle will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Major League Baseball pulls All-Star Game from Georgia over voting law\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine reports:\par \par \uc2 Major League {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/baseball"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Baseball}}}\uc2  will not hold the annual All-Star Game in Atlanta this year after Georgia passed a new law that makes it significantly harder to vote.\par \par \uc2 The announcement is perhaps the most consequential action taken since Georgia governor Brian Kemp, a Republican, signed the measure into law. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/31/delta-georgia-voting-restrictions-statement-coca-cola"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Delta Airlines and Coca-Cola spoke out against the bill}}}\uc2  this week, but faced criticism for not doing so earlier, when their influence could have had a significant impact on the legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have decided that the best way to demonstrate our values as a sport is by relocating this year\u8217\'20\'19s All-Star Game and MLB draft,\u8221\'20\'1D Rob Manfred, the league\u8217\'20\'19s commissioner, said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CMajor League Baseball fundamentally supports voting rights for all Americans and opposes restrictions to the ballot box.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Georgia law implements new requirements for mail-in voting, a process voters in the state used in record numbers without evidence of fraud in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/02/mlb-baseball-all-star-game-georgia-voting-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Major League Baseball pulls All-Star Game from Georgia over voting law}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi mourns killed USCP officer as 'a martyr for our democracy'\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has released a statement mourning the loss of US Capitol police officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans in this afternoon\u8217\'20\'19s attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, America\u8217\'20\'19s heart has been broken by the tragic and heroic death of one of our Capitol Police heroes: Officer William Evans. He is a martyr for our democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic speaker said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMembers of Congress, staff and Capitol workers, and indeed all Americans are united in appreciation for the courage of the \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2 . Today, once again, these heroes risked their lives to protect our Capitol and our country, with the same extraordinary selflessness and spirit of service seen on January 6. On behalf of the entire House, we are profoundly grateful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pelosi pledged that Congress was ready to \u8220\'20\'1Cassist law enforcement with a swift and comprehensive investigation into this heinous attack\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMay we always remember the heroism of those who have given their lives to defend our democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D the speaker said. \u8220\'20\'1CMay it be a comfort to the family of Officer Evans that so many mourn with them and pray for them at this sad time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 USCP identifies killed officer as William 'Billy' Evans\par \par \uc2 The US capitol police has identified the officer who was killed in the attack this afternoon as William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is with profound sadness that I share the news of the passing of Officer William \u8216\'20\'18Billy\u8217\'20\'19 Evans this afternoon from injuries he sustained following an attack at the North Barricade by a lone assailant,\u8221\'20\'1D the USCP acting chief, Yogananda Pittman, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 enltrStatement on the Loss of USCP Colleague Officer William "Billy" Evans: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JMAEbTcbAp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/JMAEbTcbAp}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DPvkAv5ptO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DPvkAv5ptO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2  (@CapitolPolice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CapitolPolice/status/1378078115495301120?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Pittman noted Evans, who succumbed to his injuries after being struck by a car that rammed through a security barrier, had been a member of the USCP force for 18 years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe began his USCP service on March 7, 2003, and was a member of the Capitol division\u8217\'20\'19s first responder\u8217\'20\'19s unit,\u8221\'20\'1D Pittman said. \u8220\'20\'1CPlease keep Officer Evans and his family in your thoughts and prayers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Brian Schatz\uc2 , a Democrat of Hawaii, offered his thoughts to the US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2 , after an officer died in the attack this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBeing a Capitol police officer has never been more difficult or more stressful. All the love and comfort in the world to them and their family members,\u8221\'20\'1D Schatz said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrBeing a Capitol Police officer has never been more difficult or more stressful. All the love and comfort in the world to them and their family members.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Brian Schatz\uc2  (@brianschatz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brianschatz/status/1378061165914284032?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 This is the second line-of-duty death for the USCP since January, when Officer Brian Sicknick succumbed to his injuries from the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Prior to 2021, a total of four USCP officers had died in the line of duty in the entire history of the force, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uscp.gov/media-center/uscp-fast-facts#:~:text=Four%20USCP%20law%20enforcement%20officers,Gibson%2C%20and%20Sergeant%20Clinton%20J."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the USCP website}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House and Senate are not in session but some elected officials and staff were in the building on Friday, as a car rammed a security barrier on the grounds.\par \par \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2 , a Democratic representative from California, spoke to CNN from his car, where he said officers had told him to go after he came back to the Capitol from going out for lunch.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really sad,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1COnce the barriers were removed we were moving back to some sense of normalcy, but this just shows the level of risk there still is.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t imagine saying that going to the United States Capitol to represent your constituents is actually a dangerous thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/02/us-capitol-lockdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Capitol lockdown: one officer and suspect dead after car rams into barrier}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Noah Green, a 25-year-old man from Indiana, is the suspect who rammed through a Capitol security checkpoint in his car this afternoon, according to NBC News.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING / NBC News: Multiple senior law enforcement officials briefed on the investigation say Noah Green, 25 year old male, from Indiana is the person who attacked the Capitol today.\par \par \uc2 Reported by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PeteWilliamsNBC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PeteWilliamsNBC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jonathan4ny?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @jonathan4ny}}}\uc2  and myself.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tom Winter (@Tom_Winter) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Tom_Winter/status/1378070336441176066?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  has said the suspect exited the vehicle wielding a knife and was then shot by at least one of the officers present. He later succumbed to his injuries and died.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  has provided the latest information on the attack that occurred this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 According to USCP, a man in a blue sedan charged a security barrier at the Capitol, striking two officers. The man then exited the vehicle with a knife and ran toward the officers.\par \par \uc2 At least one of the officers drew their weapon and shot the suspect, who succumbed to his injuries about 30 minutes later. One of the USCP officers who was hit by the car also died of his injuries.\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE: Here is the latest information. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GOVaMv8EXk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GOVaMv8EXk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2  (@CapitolPolice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CapitolPolice/status/1378066966691340288?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate majority leader, Chuck Schumer, said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbroken\u8221\'20\'1D for the US Capitol Police officer who was killed today, after a car rammed through a security barrier.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m praying for the officer injured and his family. We\u8217\'20\'19re in their debt,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic leader said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe thank the Capitol Police, National Guard, & first responders for all they do to protect the Capitol and those inside.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m heartbroken for the officer killed today defending our Capitol and for his family. I\u8217\'20\'19m praying for the officer injured and his family.\par \par \uc2 We're in their debt\par \par \uc2 We thank the Capitol Police, National Guard, & first responders for all they do to protect the Capitol and those inside\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chuck Schumer (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1378067037776449540?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 USCP lifts Capitol lockdown after car attack\par \par \uc2 The US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  has lifted the lockdown on the Capitol grounds, about two hours after a car rammed a security barrier and injured two USCP officers, killing one of them.\par \par \uc2 But the police force noted the area immediately surrounding the attack site is still under restricted access as officials continue to process the scene.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe USCP has cleared the external security threat incident located at all of the U.S. Capitol Campus buildings, however the area around the crime scene will continue to be restricted and individuals should follow police direction. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6SXr5WJmcE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6SXr5WJmcE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2  (@CapitolPolice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CapitolPolice/status/1378063372130848774?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman Mikie Sherrill, a Democrat of New Jersey, expressed profound sadness over the death of another US Capitol Police officer so shortly after the 6 January insurrection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo see these \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  who\u8217\'20\'19ve been traumatized already by what happened, so many members of Congress \u8211\'20\'13 myself included \u8211\'20\'13 feel we owe them a huge debt that we can never repay for their bravery on January 6,\u8221\'20\'1D Sherrill told MNSBC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd to see the ongoing attacks against them, my heart is going out to all of their families, to all of their loved ones.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Mikie Sherrill (D-NJ): \u8220\'20\'1CTo see these Capitol Police who\u8217\'20\'19ve been traumatized already \u8230\'20\'26 so many members of Congress \u8212\'20\'14 myself included \u8212\'20\'14 feel we owe them a huge debt that we can never repay for their bravery on January 6th.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EukFTY36C9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EukFTY36C9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1378061337515859969?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has ordered the flags at the Capitol to be flown at half-staff after a US Capitol police officer died in an attack this afternoon, a spokesperson for the House speaker said.\par \par \uc2 enltrSpeaker Pelosi has ordered the flags at the U.S. Capitol to be flown at half-staff due to the death of a U.S. Capitol Police Officer in the of duty today. The process of lowering the flags may take longer than usual because of the Capitol\u8217\'20\'19s current lockdown status.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Drew Hammill (@Drew_Hammill) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Drew_Hammill/status/1378058113803255811?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The fatal attack on two US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  officers today comes less than three months after the deadly insurrection at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 One USCP officer, Brian Sicknick, died of his injuries from the 6 January insurrection, and a second USCP officer, Howard Liebengood, died by suicide days later.\par \par \uc2 Now, another USCP officer has died today, after an attacker rammed his car through a security barrier and then exited the vehicle wielding a knife.\par \par \uc2 The tragedy deals another blow to a police force that was already mourning.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Police: 'It does not appear to be terrorism related'\par \par \uc2 Robert Contee of the Washington DC, Metropolitan police department has just said at the briefing outside the US Capitol that the attack by a man driving a car at \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  officers \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not appear to be terrorism related\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Acting chief of the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2 , Yogananda Pittman, just described the now-deceased suspect in the attack as having got out of the vehicle after ramming her officers and crashing into a barrier and then he \u8220\'20\'1Cran aggressively\u8221\'20\'1D at them, brandishing a knife.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s understood the suspect was then shot dead by police.\par \par \uc2 Pittman moments earlier said that of the two \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  officers taken to hospital after being rammed \u8220\'20\'1Cone has succumbed\u8221\'20\'1D to their injuries\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Names have not been released yet as next of kin are being notified.\par \par \uc2 Members of the police and national guard block a street near the US Capitol today. Photograph: Eric Baradat/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 According to the USCP acting chief, Yogananda Pittman, the suspect tried to ram through a Capitol security barrier with his car at approximately 1.02pm ET.\par \par \uc2 The suspect then exited the vehicle with a knife in hand and tried to \u8220\'20\'1Clunge\u8221\'20\'1D toward the two USCP officers present.\par \par \uc2 After the suspect did not respond to vocal commands from the officer, the officers opened fire. The suspect and one of the USCP officers have now died.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 US Capitol officer dead after car attack\par \par \uc2 Yogananda Pittman, the acting chief of US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2 , is now holding a briefing on the car attack that occurred near the Capitol this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Pittman announced that sadly, one of the officers involved in the attack has succumbed to his injuries and died. Pittman did not identify him because the USCP is still trying to locate his next of kin.\par \par \uc2 Pittman also confirmed that the suspect in the attack has died.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Capitol attack suspect has died \u8211\'20\'13 reports\par \par \uc2 We continue to await confirmation from the authorities but there are more reports now that the suspect was shot dead after driving a car into two police officers.\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BREAKING?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BREAKING}}}\uc2  : Man shot by Capitol Police after driving into barricade dies from injuries, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PeteWilliamsNBC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PeteWilliamsNBC}}}\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Michael Pegram (@MichaelNBC12) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MichaelNBC12/status/1378047332487421953?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mid-afternoon summary\par \par \uc2 US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  plan to brief the media in about 20 minutes. So do stay tuned. It\u8217\'20\'19s been a busy morning in US political news. Here are the main items so far:\par \par \uc2 * The US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  has confirmed that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/02/joe-biden-us-politics-economy-jobs-report-covid-latest-news?page=with:block-606755078f08611d06d8a489#block-606755078f08611d06d8a489"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two officers have been injured}}}\uc2  after a car attempted to run through a security checkpoint outside the \uc2 US Congress\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Just around an hour ago, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/02/joe-biden-us-politics-economy-jobs-report-covid-latest-news?page=with:block-606751d58f087a7cbd51e300#block-606751d58f087a7cbd51e300"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Capitol Hill staffers received a text message}}}\uc2  informing them of an \u8220\'20\'1Cexternal security threat\u8221\'20\'1D and asking them to \u8220\'20\'1Cseek cover\u8221\'20\'1D if outside. Shortly after, the US Capitol was put on lockdown.\par \par \uc2 * Fully vaccinated Americans can now travel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/02/joe-biden-us-politics-economy-jobs-report-covid-latest-news?page=with:block-606736d48f083302090e2e1f#block-606736d48f083302090e2e1f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 without self-quarantining}}}\uc2 , the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/coronavirus/2019-ncov/travelers/travel-during-covid19.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced today}}}\uc2 . Vaccinated people also do not need to take a coronavirus test before traveling. But wear a mask!\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  encouraged Americans to \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/02/joe-biden-us-politics-economy-jobs-report-covid-latest-news?page=with:block-606739fe8f083302090e2e66#block-606739fe8f083302090e2e66"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 buckle down}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D as coronavirus cases rise. The US president emphasized that there is still a lot of work left to be done to rebuild the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/useconomy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy}}}\uc2  after the many setbacks caused by the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 * Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/02/joe-biden-us-politics-economy-jobs-report-covid-latest-news?page=with:block-606737a38f087a7cbd51e124#block-606737a38f087a7cbd51e124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 celebrated}}}\uc2  the latest jobs report, which showed the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/useconomy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy}}}\uc2  added 916,000 jobs last month.The president credited the resiliency of the American people and his administration\u8217\'20\'19s new economic vision for helping the economy to rebound one year after the start of the coronavirus pandemic. \u8220\'20\'1COpportunity is coming,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 We are watching and listening closely for any confirmation that the suspect in the lone attack on the US Capitol this afternoon has died after being shot by police. We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you more details on this as soon as they emerge.\par \par \uc2 There is little information at this stage on the identity of the suspect, who was driving a passenger car and rammed two US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  officers before crashing into a giant concrete barrier.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dozens and dozens of National Guard troops are now walking through the corridors of the US Capitol kitted out with riot shields, batons and plastic visors on the front of their helmets. They don\u8217\'20\'19t appear to be wearing body armor, they are in ordinary camouflage uniform.\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE: Law enforcement officials have said a driver has been shot by Capitol Police after a car rammed into a barricade outside the US Capitol building and injured two police officers. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alexrossiSKY?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @alexrossiSKY}}}\uc2  says the \uc2 FBI\uc2  has responded to the incident.\par \par \uc2 Read more: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Frg2acoW0y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Frg2acoW0y}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0WD3ZwdafR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0WD3ZwdafR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sky News (@SkyNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SkyNews/status/1378047046582734853?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 National Guard are also already lined up outside.\par \par \uc2 enltrNational Guard has now been deployed around US Capitol. Officers are fully equipped with riot shields ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lf1s7pUozI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/lf1s7pUozI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kieran Bradley (@KieranKBradley) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KieranKBradley/status/1378047880276144132?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Latest reports, which have not been officially confirmed, are that after ramming the two police officers the driver of the car got out of the vehicle brandishing a knife.\par \par \uc2 Two Capitol Police officers are injured. This is what congressional sources are telling reporters on Capitol Hill. There are no details about the identity or even the gender of the driver of the blue passenger sedan.\par \par \uc2 Two law enforcement officials have now told The Associated Press that the driver was then shot by police, and is in critical condition in the hospital.\par \par \uc2 At least one officer is in serious condition.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe suspect who rammed into two \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  Officers exited his vehicle brandishing a knife and was shot. The suspect and two officers were transported to the hospital. Footage via Fox News: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/10TAUW6UNz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/10TAUW6UNz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 RealTimBlack (@RealTimBlack) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RealTimBlack/status/1378046309974818818?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The AP adds:\par \par \uc2 One of the officers who was injured was taken by police car to the hospital; the other was being transported by emergency medical crews, the officials said.\par \par \uc2 The incident occurred about 100 yards from the entrance of the building on the Senate side of the Capitol. Fencing that prevented vehicular traffic near that area was recently removed as the Capitol has started to open up after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/09/us-capitol-insurrection-white-supremacist-terror"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 riots}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 The security checkpoint is typically used by senators and staff on weekdays. Congress is currently on recess.\par \par \uc2 Video posted online showed a dark colored sedan crashed against a vehicle barrier and a police K9 inspecting the vehicle.\par \par \uc2 Law enforcement and paramedics could be seen caring for at least one unidentified individual.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had just departed the White House for Camp David when the incident occurred. As is customary, he was traveling with a member of the National Security Council Staff who was expected to brief him on the incident.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s Good Friday and Passover and the US Capitol was pretty empty today when this incident occurred.\par \par \uc2 Both chambers of the \uc2 US Congress\uc2 , the House of Representatives and the Senate, are out of session and those working inside have said there are very few staff around when a blue car rammed into a barrier close to the east front of the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 No matter the quietness of business today, \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  were of course on duty and two officers have been injured. US Parks Police are on duty, ditto District of Columbia police and more law enforcement are arriving on the scene.\par \par \uc2 National Guard troops have been seen lining up in the vicinity. It\u8217\'20\'19s less than three months since the January 6 deadly insurrection at the US Capitol when extremist fans of former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  stormed Congress in a failed attempt to stop the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the November election.\par \par \uc2 Several dozen National Guard just marched into position outside the Capitol, securing the wider perimeter, and federal investigators are on the scene.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s only been a few days since someone was arrested with weapons outside the residence of the US vice president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  issued a correction that the incident occurred at Constitution Avenue, not Independence Avenue.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 USCP confirms two officers injured after car rams security checkpoint\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  has confirmed that two officers have been injured after a car attempted to run through a security checkpoint.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUSCP is responding to the North Barricade vehicle access point along Independence Avenue for reports someone rammed a vehicle into two USCP officers,\u8221\'20\'1D the agency said in a statement on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA suspect is in custody. Both officers are injured. All three have been transported to the hospital.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There had been previous reports that gunshots were fired at the security checkpoint, but the USCP statement does not mention anything about that.\par \par \uc2 enltrCRITICAL INCIDENT: USCP is responding to the North Barricade vehicle access point along Independence Avenue for reports someone rammed a vehicle into two USCP officers. A suspect is in custody. Both officers are injured. All three have been transported to the hospital. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4TXIdulJc6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4TXIdulJc6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2  (@CapitolPolice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CapitolPolice/status/1378036076175110145?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  about the situation at the Capitol before she concluded her briefing.\par \par \uc2 Asked who is traveling with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to Camp David this weekend and may be able to keep him briefed on the situation, Psaki said the president \u8220\'20\'1Calways travels with a national security rep\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrWH Press Sec. Psaki is asked about the reports of gunfire at the U.S. Capitol and how Biden is alerted while off campus. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JOlHl90RD1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JOlHl90RD1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1378036773729804294?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 According to NBC News, a car that was trying to get through a Capitol security checkpoint would not stop, and shots were fired.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW -- via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PeteWilliamsNBC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PeteWilliamsNBC}}}\uc2  on the Capitol: "A car was trying to get through a checkpoint and wouldn't stop"\par \par \uc2 "We've been told that shots were fired," says officers shot at the car.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 j.d. durkin (@jiveDurkey) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jiveDurkey/status/1378035632023474185?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Punchbowl News reporter shared a video of a helicopter landing on the east front of the Capitol, after reports of a car driving into a security barrier near the grounds.\par \par \uc2 enltr????A helicopter just landed on the east front of the Capitol. I\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen anything like this before. ever. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LxV0mywRSe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LxV0mywRSe}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1378033434082344972?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Asked about the security situation on Capitol Hill, White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said she was not aware of it because it started while she was briefing reporters.\par \par \uc2 She indicated she may offer further details to the press as her team learns more about what happened.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Capitol in lockdown following reports of a car crashing into security barrier\par \par \uc2 Capitol Hill staffers have received a text message informing them of an \u8220\'20\'1Cexternal security threat\u8221\'20\'1D and asking them to \u8220\'20\'1Cseek cover\u8221\'20\'1D if outside, according to Punchbowl News.\par \par \uc2 enltr????Capitol staff just got this text message\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m in the Capitol and will keep everyone posted here. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ydQGyCJcof"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ydQGyCJcof}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1378031234589278208?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 A video by a Fox News reporter appeared to indicate a car had smashed into a security barrier near the Capitol. She spotted two people on stretchers.\par \par \uc2 enltrAppears that a car smashed into the barrier. Two people are on stretchers. Can\u8217\'20\'19t see whether it\u8217\'20\'19s an officer or civilian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ud5WYGyKFu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Ud5WYGyKFu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jacqui Heinrich (@JacquiHeinrich) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JacquiHeinrich/status/1378033471495475204?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  sidestepped questions about Republican congressman Matt Gaetz, who is reportedly under investigation for alleged sex trafficking.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said she did not want to comment on the allegations, instead referring reporters to the local authorities.\par \par \uc2 Asked if Gaetz should step down from the House judiciary committee, Psaki said, \u8220\'20\'1CThose are decisions we\u8217\'20\'19ll let leaders in Congress make.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/02/matt-gaetz-republican-congressman-doj-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DoJ reportedly investigating whether Matt Gaetz paid women for sex}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Japanese prime minister to visit White House this month\par \par \uc2 Japanese Prime Minister \uc2 Yoshihide Suga\uc2  will visit the White House later this month, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  just announced.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary said Suga will come to Washington to meet with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on April 16.\par \par \uc2 The trip will make Suga the first foreign leader to make an in-person visit to the White House since Biden became president.\par \par \uc2 Biden has held virtual meetings with several foreign leaders in recent weeks, but the White House has been very cautious about holding in-person meetings due to the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , is now holding her daily briefing with reporters.\par \par \uc2 Psaki was joined by Labor Secretary \uc2 Marty Walsh\uc2 , who addressed the latest jobs report released this morning.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecMartyWalsh?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SecMartyWalsh}}}\uc2  joins {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec}}}\uc2  today to talk {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/JobsReport?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #JobsReport}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/AmericanJobsPlan?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #AmericanJobsPlan}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/djdo7JqhhD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/djdo7JqhhD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Karine Jean-Pierre (@KJP46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KJP46/status/1378024412566458368?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The report showed the US economy added 916,000 jobs last month, but Walsh emphasized he wanted to do a closer analysis of the numbers with his advisers to better understand where the economic recovery is lagging.\par \par \uc2 Despite the promising news, Walsh emphasized it was still urgent that Congress pass \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s $2tn infrastructure plan to create jobs.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Echoing comments from his coronavirus response team, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  expressed similar concerns about the recent rise in coronavirus cases while delivering a speech on the March jobs report this morning.\par \par \uc2 enltrBIDEN: "Too many Americans are acting as if this fight is over. It is not... If the American people continue to do their part, mask up, practice social distancing, we could have a more normal July 4th. But this is still April, not July." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tGGlftjAnO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tGGlftjAnO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Daily Caller (@DailyCaller) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DailyCaller/status/1378008700196167684?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The president celebrated the news that 20 million vaccination doses were administered over the past week, but he warned, \u8220\'20\'1CToo many Americans are acting as if this fight is over. It is not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden added, \u8220\'20\'1CIf the American people continue to do their part, mask up, practice social distancing, we could have a more normal July 4th. But this is still April, not July. We aren\u8217\'20\'19t there yet. And so cases are going up again. The virus is spreading more rapidly in many places.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president pleaded with Americans to \u8220\'20\'1Cbuckle down and keep their guard up in this home stretch\u8221\'20\'1D by continuing to wear masks and practice social distancing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2  whether the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  is formally warning against non-essential travel at this point.\par \par \uc2 The reporter noted that the CDC director had made several comments during the briefing warning against non-essential travel. However, the agency\u8217\'20\'19s official guidance makes no such distinction between essential and non-essential travel for vaccinated individuals.\par \par \uc2 Walensky said the new guidance is meant to provide fully vaccinated Americans with information on the relative risk of traveling, which is low. But she reiterated she would not recommend non-essential travel at this point, due to the climbing number of coronavirus cases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would advocate against general travel overall,\u8221\'20\'1D Walensky said. \u8220\'20\'1COur guidance speaks to the safety of doing so. If you are vaccinated, it is lower risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House coronavirus response team\u8217\'20\'19s briefing has now concluded.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2  reiterated that she is still not recommending non-essential travel, as coronavirus cases rise in dozens of US states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not recommending travel at this time, especially for unvaccinated individuals,\u8221\'20\'1D the CDC director said at the White House coronavirus response team\u8217\'20\'19s briefing.\par \par \uc2 Walensky said moments later that there is still much work left to be done to get the virus under control, especially with only about 20% of American adults fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  emphasized that fully vaccinated Americans should still take precautions while traveling, despite the relatively low risk to themselves.\par \par \uc2 The agency asked vaccinated Americans to continue wearing masks, socially distancing and regularly washing their hands during their travels.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House coronavirus response team is now holding its briefing, and the director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention addressed her agency\u8217\'20\'19s new travel guidance.\par \par \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2  summarized the new CDC guidelines, which indicate that Americans do not need to quarantine after domestic or international travel.\par \par \uc2 However, Walensky emphasized the CDC is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot recommending travel at this time due to the rising number of cases\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 About half of US states have reported increases in new coronavirus cases over the past week, even as public health experts urge Americans to remain vigilant about limiting the spread of the virus.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  said fully vaccinated Americans can also travel internationally, although the guidelines are a bit stricter.\par \par \uc2 While vaccinated people do not need to quarantine after international travel, the CDC still recommends getting tested for coronavirus three to five days after arriving back in the US.\par \par \uc2 International travelers do not need to get tested before their trip, unless their destination country requires it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fully vaccinated Americans can travel without quarantining, CDC says\par \par \uc2 Fully vaccinated Americans can now travel without self-quarantining, the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/coronavirus/2019-ncov/travelers/travel-during-covid19.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced today}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Vaccinated people also do not need to take a coronavirus test before traveling, although the CDC has asked those traveling to still wear masks.\par \par \uc2 The updated guidance comes about a month after the CDC announced its initial guidelines for vaccinated individuals.\par \par \uc2 At that time, the agency asked vaccinated Americans to continue to avoid travel, due to fears that it could cause a surge in infections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery time there\u8217\'20\'19s a surge in travel, we have a surge of cases in this country,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , the CDC director, said last month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re hopeful that our next set of guidance will have more science around what vaccinated people can do, perhaps travel being among them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden encourages Americans to 'buckle down' as coronavirus cases rise\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  emphasized that there is still a lot of work left to be done to rebuild the US economy after the many setbacks caused by the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The president encouraged Americans to continue working to limit the spread of coronavirus in order to allow states to safely reopen.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToo many Americans are acting as if this fight is over. It is not,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t give back the progress we\u8217\'20\'19ve all so fought so hard to achieve. We need to finish this job. We need every American to buckle down and keep their guard up in this home stretch.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s comments come as about half of US states have reported increases in new coronavirus cases over the past week, despite a steady rise in vaccinations.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the White House, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  touted the positive impact that his coronavirus relief package has had on the US economy.\par \par \uc2 But Biden emphasized that the relief bill brought only temporary change to the economy, while his proposed infrastructure plan would bring longer-lasting reform to allow the US to \u8220\'20\'1Cbuild back better\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The president encouraged lawmakers to negotiate over his proposal in the weeks to come, as congressional Republicans have signaled they will not support the plan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongress should debate my plan,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut Congress should act.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 'Opportunity is coming,' Biden says after promising jobs report\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  celebrated the latest jobs report, which showed the US economy added 916,000 jobs last month.\par \par \uc2 The president credited the resiliency of the American people and his administration\u8217\'20\'19s new economic vision for helping the economy to rebound one year after the start of the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHelp is here. Opportunity is coming. And at long last, there is hope for so many families,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president argued the positive economic news reflected the impact of his coronavirus relief package and the steady increase in vaccinations across the country.\par \par \uc2 Biden reiterated, \u8220\'20\'1CThere is nothing the American people cannot do if you give them a chance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 CDC to say vaccinated people can travel without quarantining - reports\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  is reportedly updating its travel guidance for vaccinated people.\par \par \uc2 According to multiple reports, the CDC will say vaccinated people can travel domestically and internationally without taking a coronavirus test or quarantining as long as they wear masks.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: CDC is updating its guidelines for vaccinated individuals, saying they can travel domestically and internationally without a Covid-19 test as long as they wear a mask in public. Individuals who travel do not need to self-quarantine.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Erin Banco (@ErinBanco) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ErinBanco/status/1378000488663224320?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The White House coronavirus response team\u8217\'20\'19s briefing will start at any moment now, and the senior health officials will likely address this change.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  celebrated the March jobs report released this morning in a new statement, saying the data is \u8220\'20\'1Cresounding evidence that, under Congressional Democrats and President Biden, Help Is Here\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 However, the Democratic speaker noted millions of Americans, particularly women and people of color, have not regained the jobs they lost at the start of the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is imperative that, as we deliver the benefits of the American Rescue Plan as urgently and equitably as possible, we advance President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s American Jobs Act: a visionary, once-in-a-century investment in America\u8217\'20\'19s workers and future, which will Build our economy Back Better from this crisis by revitalizing our nation\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said.\par \par \uc2 The president will likely deliver a similar message when he speaks about the jobs report in a few minutes.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/apr/02/us-economy-jobs-hiring-vaccine-rollout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy adds 916,000 March jobs as vaccine rollout fuels hiring boom}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate parliamentarian is expected to soon issue a ruling on whether Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer can attempt to pass another bill via reconciliation during this fiscal year, according to CBS News.\par \par \uc2 CBS{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/infrastructure-bill-second-budget-reconciliation-senate-schumer-parliamentarian/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 D emocrats used a budget resolution for the current fiscal year to lay the groundwork for passing the American Rescue Plan. Although typically budget reconciliation is used only once per fiscal year, the majority leader asked the Senate parliamentarian whether he can revise the current budget resolution to allow for another reconciliation process to pass the infrastructure package.\par \par \uc2 Parliamentarian \uc2 Elizabeth MacDonough\uc2  could rule as early as Friday on whether to allow for another budget reconciliation bill this year, a Senate aide told CBS News.\par \par \uc2 Top Schumer aides have asked MacDonough about using Section 304 of the Congressional Budget Act of 1974 to allow for a second reconciliation process this fiscal year. The parliamentarian is an expert on the obscure procedures of the Senate, and can determine whether certain actions are permitted under Senate rules.\par \par \uc2 MacDonough\u8217\'20\'19s ruling will have major implications for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure plan, which almost certainly cannot pass the Senate unless reconciliation is used.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have already signaled opposition to the plan, mainly due to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s proposals to roll back Trump-era tax cuts to help pay for the proposal.\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  said yesterday that he plans to fight Biden\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure plan \u8220\'20\'1Cevery step of the way\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chauvin trial resumes, with police chief's testimony expected\par \par \uc2 The fifth day of Derek Chauvin \u8217\'20\'19s trial is now underway in Minneapolis, where the former police officer faces murder charges over the killing of \uc2 George Floyd\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Minneapolis police chief {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/02/george-floyd-derek-chauvin-trial-police-chief-testimony"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Medaria Arradondo}}}\uc2  is expected to testify against Chauvin, which criminal justice experts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/02/george-floyd-derek-chauvin-trial-police-chief-testimony"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have described}}}\uc2  as a remarkable and potentially unprecedented move.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Joanna Walters is running a separate live blog on Chauvin\u8217\'20\'19s trial, so follow along there to get the latest news on the court proceedings:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/02/derek-chauvin-trial-george-floyd-death-latest-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Derek Chauvin trial: senior police expected to testify over George Floyd death \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton reports:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration}}}\uc2  plans to invest $5bn toward gun violence prevention in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most hard-hit areas as part of a key infrastructure package announced this week.\par \par \uc2 This investment marks an important step in acknowledging the disparate impact of gun violence and is the first time the government has set aside this much money at one time to address community violence holistically over a multi-year period.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHistorically, the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s approach, particularly when faced with surges in gun homicides, is to fund strategies that over-police,\u8221\'20\'1D said Paul Carillo, community violence initiative director for the Giffords Law Center to Prevent Gun Violence, in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Biden administration demonstrated a commitment to addressing the root causes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The proposal comes as America has witnessed a significant increase in gun violence during the pandemic. Los Angeles has recorded an 11-year high in homicides. Philadelphia is seeing one of the highest annual gun violence rates in half a century.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has long been a firm advocate for gun control and has called for bans on assault weapons and universal background checks. He has reiterated his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/03/23/politics/biden-gun-control-colorado-atlanta/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resolve}}}\uc2  after the first high-profile mass shootings of his tenure in the White House.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/02/biden-administration-infrastructure-gun-violence-prevention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration plans historic $5bn investment to combat gun violence in hard-hit areas}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  is expected to release new travel guidelines for vaccinated people later today, according to CNN.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew travel guidelines for vaccinated people are expected from the CDC today, officials say, after a lengthy deliberation process. More details expected at briefing later this morning.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin Liptak (@Kevinliptakcnn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Kevinliptakcnn/status/1377975735365873670?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The members of the White House coronavirus response team will likely discuss the new guidelines at their briefing this morning.\par \par \uc2 When the CDC released its initial guidelines for vaccinated Americans, the agency still discouraged everyone from traveling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery time there\u8217\'20\'19s a surge in travel, we have a surge of cases in this country,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , the CDC director, said last month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re hopeful that our next set of guidance will have more science around what vaccinated people can do, perhaps travel being among them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House coronavirus response team will also hold a briefing this morning to provide an update on vaccine distribution and case numbers.\par \par \uc2 The data on vaccine distribution in the US has been very encouraging, with 30% of Americans now having received at least one vaccine dose, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/graphics/covid-vaccine-tracker-global-distribution/?sref=6flipp83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But vaccinations are ramping up as case numbers increase across the country, intensifying fears of a \u8220\'20\'1Cfourth wave\u8221\'20\'1D of infections.\par \par \uc2 Cases are rising as state and local officials continue relaxing coronavirus-related restrictions, despite public health experts\u8217\'20\'19 urgent warnings to remain vigilant about limiting the spread of the virus.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/29/us-covid-cases-cdc-walensky-doom-scared-biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky}}}\uc2 , the \uc2 federal Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) director, said Monday, \u8220\'20\'1CWe have so much to look forward to, so much promise and potential of where we are, and so much reason for hope. But right now I\u8217\'20\'19m scared.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/01/us-fourth-wave-covid-coronavirus-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US may be in early stages of fourth wave as Covid cases rise, reports say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chauvin trial: police chief to testify against former officer in 'remarkable move'\par \par \uc2 As the prosecutor Jerry Blackwell addressed the jury {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/29/george-floyd-killing-focus-derek-chauvin-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for the first time}}}\uc2  in the murder trial of Derek Chauvin last week, he reeled off a list of witnesses expected to testify: from eyewitnesses who watched as the former officer held his knee on \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s neck for nine minutes and 29 seconds, to forensic pathologists, use of force experts and members of the Minneapolis police department.\par \par \uc2 Among the most significant on this long list was the most senior member of that department, Chief Medaria Arradondo.\par \par \uc2 It is, of course, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2015/dec/31/ties-that-bind-conflicts-of-interest-police-killings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rare for an officer-involved death to make it to criminal trial}}}\uc2 , but it is rarer still \u8211\'20\'13 perhaps unprecedented, experts say \u8211\'20\'13 for a police chief to testify against one of their own former officers.\par \par \uc2 Arradondo\u8217\'20\'19s testimony is likely to be a powerful weapon in the prosecution\u8217\'20\'19s case as the defense will attempt to argue that Derek Chauvin\u8217\'20\'19s protracted use of a knee-to-neck restraint was in line with use of force guidance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a pretty remarkable move on the part of the prosecution,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Cedric Alexander, the former police chief and public safety director of DeKalb county, Georgia.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very rare that you\u8217\'20\'19re going to see a chief either appear for the defense or the prosecution. But each one of these kinds of events brings its own set of circumstances. And in this particular case, where you have a knee to the neck and it\u8217\'20\'19s being questioned \u8216\'20\'18was that trained technique?\u8217\'20\'19 To be able to have the chief of police\u8230\'20\'26 to under oath testify is clearly going to be of importance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/02/george-floyd-derek-chauvin-trial-police-chief-testimony"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Derek Chauvin trial: police chief to testify against former officer in 'remarkable move'}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to deliver remarks on promising jobs report\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will soon deliver remarks on the promising March jobs report, which was released this morning.\par \par \uc2 The report showed the US economy added 916,000 jobs last month, bringing the unemployment rate down to 6%.\par \par \uc2 Biden will likely credit the distribution of coronavirus vaccines and the passage of his $1.9tn relief bill for helping strengthen the economy, but the full picture is a bit more complicated.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Dominic Rushe reports:\par \par \uc2 In March, consumer confidence hit its highest level since the start of the pandemic, according to the latest poll by the \uc2 Conference Board\uc2 , and US stock markets have been setting new highs....\par \par \uc2 Unemployment remains high and has hit low-wage workers, people of color and women the hardest. The latest gains suggest that the worst of the pandemic-related jobs slump may be over \u8211\'20\'13 but big issues remain.\par \par \uc2 Last week, 719,000 people filed claims for unemployment benefits, the labor department announced on Thursday. The figure was up from 658,000 the week before. Although the number of claims is trending down from record highs, it is still more than three times as high as it was before the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Biden will likely argue his newly announced infrastructure plan will help tackle some of these issues, but it remains unclear whether that proposal can make it through Congress.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s speech is coming up later this morning, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/apr/02/us-economy-jobs-hiring-vaccine-rollout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy adds 916,000 March jobs as vaccine rollout fuels hiring boom}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210402eh42001ml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
