\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Amazon union vote count set to start for Alabama warehouse workers\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 807 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 March 2021\par 06:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Campaign viewed as one of the biggest and most consequential unionization drives in recent America history\par \par \uc2 Vote counting is set to begin in an election to determine whether Amazon warehouse workers in Bessemer, Alabama, will form a union in what is viewed as one of the biggest and most consequential unionization drives in recent America history.\par \par \uc2 The contest has pitted America\u8217\'20\'19s labor movement \u8211\'20\'13 backed by a slew of Democrat politicians and some Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 against one of the most powerful companies in the world.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) will start to tally the votes to see if the Bessemer workers will form a union with the Retail Wholesale and Department Store Union (RWDSU). If successful, the warehouse would be the \uc2 first union\uc2  at Amazon in the US, as many Amazon workers in Europe are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2021/03/25/amazon-alabama-europe-unions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  already unionized.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis campaign has already been a victory in many ways. Even though we don\u8217\'20\'19t know how the vote will turn out, we believe we have opened the door to more organizing around the country, and we have exposed the lengths to which employers will go to crush their employees trying to gain a union voice,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Stuart Appelbaum\uc2 , president of RWDSU. \u8220\'20\'1CThis campaign has become the prime example for why we need labor law reform in this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Around 5,800 employees were eligible to vote in the election, with a majority of those who voted to determine the outcome.\par \par \uc2 The results could take a while to be finally counted and the process could be legally fraught. The \uc2 NLRB\uc2  said it will not have an estimate for how long the vote count will take until counting begins. The union estimated it will take about a week for results.\par \par \uc2 During the vote count, the union and Amazon will have the opportunity to challenge the veracity of ballots and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/news-outreach/fact-sheets/nlrb-representation-case-procedures-fact-sheet/main-steps-representation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 file}}}\uc2  objections within five business days of the vote count.\par \par \uc2 The results could also be delayed if enough ballots are challenged to affect the outcome of the election, at which point a hearing officer with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  will determine whether a challenged ballot will be counted.\par \par \uc2 Amazon aggressively {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/feb/03/amazon-intensifies-severe-effort-discourage-first-warehouse-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposed}}}\uc2  the union organizing efforts at the Bessemer warehouse, encouraging workers to vote \u8220\'20\'1Cno\u8221\'20\'1D in the election through posters, signs, mailings, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.doitwithoutdues.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 website}}}\uc2 , texts, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/amazon-anti-union-ads-removed-by-twitch-alabama-warehouse-2021-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ads}}}\uc2 , captive audience meetings, and hired union avoidance consultants at nearly $10,000 per day ahead of the election. Under the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/pro-act-problem-solution-chart/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pro Act}}}\uc2 , a labor law reform bill supported by Democrats and labor unions around the US, employers would be prohibited from forcing workers into captive audience meetings, and fines would significantly be increased for labor law violations.\par \par \uc2 The union drive has received {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://southernworker.org/amazon/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support}}}\uc2  from unions and organizations in the Bessemer area and around the US. Several congress members {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2021/03/05/lawmakers-show-solidarity-for-amazon-union-vote-in-alabama.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visited}}}\uc2  the union organizing site over the past few weeks to show their support for the workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis election is important because it\u8217\'20\'19s the start to addressing inadequate working conditions,\u8221\'20\'1D said Eric Hall, founder of the Black Lives Matter chapter in Birmingham, Alabama, which has supported the union organizing efforts and participated in rallies to garner community support for the workers.\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/29/technology/amazon-union-vote.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated 85%}}}\uc2  of the Amazon warehouse workers in Bessemer are Black.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBirmingham is a city known for its strong stance for civil rights. Its people led a rebellion against racism and Jim Crow, and in this present day movement it\u8217\'20\'19s the grand and great grandchildren fighting against today\u8217\'20\'19s injustices, fighting against the rich and powerful, fighting systemic racism, fighting economic and social injustice,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hall.\par \par \uc2 According to the RWDSU, hundreds of Amazon workers around the US have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-03-19/amazon-workers-inspired-by-alabama-weigh-union-drives-elsewhere"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reached out}}}\uc2  to the union during the Alabama organizing effort with interests to start union organizing within their workplaces.\par \par \uc2 As the union election in Alabama concluded, Amazon executives increasingly attacked their critics, with recent spars on social media from Amazon CEO \uc2 Dave Clark\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/amazonnews/status/1375529101931520007"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s communications team}}}\uc2  against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/davehclark/status/1375045409542823939"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Senator Bernie Sanders}}}\uc2 , Senator Elizabeth Warren and Congressman Mark Pocan.\par \par \uc2 According to Recode, the tweets came after Amazon founder \uc2 Jeff Bezos{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/recode/2021/3/28/22354604/amazon-twitter-bernie-sanders-jeff-bezos-union-alabama-elizabeth-warren"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed }}}\uc2  dismay that executives weren\u8217\'20\'19t pushing back enough on criticism toward the company.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s PR account claimed reports workers urinate in bottles due to their inability to take bathroom breaks during shifts are false, The Intercept {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theintercept.com/2021/03/25/amazon-drivers-pee-bottles-union/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2  on leaked emails and memos where Amazon management discussed problems with delivery drivers urinating in plastic bottles and defecating in plastic bags.\par \par \uc2 An Amazon spokesperson said in an email: \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t believe the RWDSU represents the majority of our employees\u8217\'20\'19 views. Our employees choose to work at Amazon because we offer some of the best jobs available everywhere we hire, and we encourage anyone to compare our total compensation package, health benefits, and workplace environment to any other company with similar jobs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210330eh3u000uq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
