\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18You will not have your seat again\u8217\'20\'19: how the Fight for $15 movement gained new momentum\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Aratani \par \uc2 1,366 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 March 2021\par 14:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Congress\u8217\'20\'19s failure to raise the federal minimum wage last month dealt a blow, but advocates are pressuring lawmakers to bring the issue back\par \par \uc2 For Terrence Wise, a \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  employee from Kansas City, Missouri, the battle for a raise in the federal minimum wage is far from over.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden campaigned on a raise, the first since 2009, and the majority of Americans of both parties support an increase. And yet, last month, Congress blocked an increase from the paltry $7.25 an hour where it has been stuck since 2009. Now there are signs of new momentum for change.\par \par \uc2 If Washington can\u8217\'20\'19t find a solution, Wise had a warning for politicians of both sides. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re not going to make $15 a reality for workers, if you\u8217\'20\'19re not going to create an environment for workers to join a union and make that possible, you will not be re-elected. You will not have your seat again,\u8221\'20\'1D Wise said, a leader with the Fight for $15 movement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not continue to choose representatives who are truly not representing us or who are out of tune with the working class.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe say don\u8217\'20\'19t take it as a threat \u8211\'20\'13 take it as a promise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/13/fight-for-15-minimum-wage-workers-labor-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 High hopes}}}\uc2  that the federal minimum wage would be lifted for the first time in over 10 years came with the introduction of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s $1.9tn stimulus package. The wage hike, which Biden tucked into his original stimulus plan, would have been the largest victory for the Fight for $15 movement since it started to mobilize fast-food workers in 2012.\par \par \uc2 But when the bill hit the Senate, the wage increase faced two major hurdles: moderate Democrats who said that $15 was just too high and a ruling from the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s parliamentarian on whether including an increase in the spending bill would break Senate rules.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, both factors stopped the increase from going into law.\par \par \uc2 While Congress\u8217\'20\'19s failure to raise the minimum wage dealt a blow to the Fight for $15 movement, advocates say there is still enough momentum behind the issue to build pressure on lawmakers in DC to bring a $15 minimum wage back to the table. Activists also say the Democratic party risks losing the support of some of its base if a new minimum wage fails to pass.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s such a core priority for so many organizations, for so many people, so many of the voters that put a lot of these elected officials into office,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tsedeye Gebreselassie, director of work quality at the National Employment Law Project. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the top economic policy priority this year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Multiple polls have shown there is broad support for a $15 minimum wage. One \uc2 Pew Research{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2019/07/30/two-thirds-of-americans-favor-raising-federal-minimum-wage-to-15-an-hour/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  from 2019 found that 67% of Americans support a minimum wage increase. An Amazon/Ipsos {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipsos.com/en-us/news-polls/minimum-wage-thought-leadership-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  released this month found approximately the same percentage of support.\par \par \uc2 With inaction from Congress, 29 states have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2021/03/12/when-it-comes-to-raising-the-minimum-wage-most-of-the-action-is-in-cities-and-states-not-congress/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased}}}\uc2  their own minimum wage above the federal rate. Seven states have passed legislation increasing their minimum wage to $15 gradually, Florida being the most recent state to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/23/fight-for-15-minimum-wage-florida-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pass}}}\uc2  the measure by a ballot initiative. A few companies have also taken things into their own hands, with \uc2 Costco\uc2 , Amazon and Target increasing their minimum wage to at least $15 in recent years.\par \par \uc2 The increase in positive public opinion and the adoption of a $15 minimum wage by states and companies are hard-fought achievements for the Fight for $15, but federal legislation would force states and companies who refuse to increase their minimum wage to adapt.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, the White House and Democrats in Congress have said they will continue to push the issue forward, though how the party plans to get legislation through the Senate remains unclear. Ron Klain, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/mehdi-on-msnbc/watch/wh-chief-of-staff-ron-klain-on-biden-s-next-legislative-priorities-106880581923"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MSNBC}}}\uc2  on 14 March \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re in the fight for $15\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going back at it to try to find a legislative strategy to get the votes together to pass the minimum wage,\u8221\'20\'1D Klain said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to talk to our allies on Capitol Hill, our allies in the broader Fight for $15, and try to figure out how we get the votes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/03/23/democrats-moderates-minimum-wage-477651"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reports}}}\uc2  have indicated that Democratic senators who pushed for the $15 minimum wage are meeting with their colleagues who voted against it to talk about next steps to increase the minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 All Republicans and eight Democrats voted against the inclusion of the wage increase in the stimulus bill. Most of the Democratic senators who voted against it voiced concerns over the rushed way the raise was being passed and its potential impact on small businesses and restaurants, but indicated they were open to some kind of increase.\par \par \uc2 One Democratic senator, \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , who is considered the most conservative Senate Democrat, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/22/us-15-dollar-minimum-wage-joe-manchin-west-virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the star holdout }}}\uc2  during the minimum wage debate. Manchin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/22/us-15-dollar-minimum-wage-joe-manchin-west-virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that he supports an increase that is \u8220\'20\'1Cresponsible and reasonable\u8221\'20\'1D, citing an $11 figure as something he would support.\par \par \uc2 In addition to getting all party senators on the same page, Democrats will either have to overrule the Senate parliamentarian, who in February ruled that a wage increase cannot be included in a bill passed with a simple majority, or get support from at least 10 Republican senators to pass the bill.\par \par \uc2 Support to overrule the parliamentarian as the stimulus bill went through Congress was weak, with Biden saying that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cdisappointed\u8221\'20\'1D in the decision but that he would \u8220\'20\'1Crespect\u8221\'20\'1D it.\par \par \uc2 Another way to bypass the parliamentarian\u8217\'20\'19s ruling would be if Democrats agree to do away with the filibuster, which would allow them to pass legislation with a simple majority. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/22/filibuster-us-senate-democrats-republicans-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Legislation}}}\uc2  protecting voting rights has recently shed a more prominent spotlight on the debate over the filibuster, though some Democrats have voiced hesitancy over getting rid of the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, some moderate Republicans have come out with minimum wage increase plans of their own, showing that there is some support for an increase as the party tries to appeal to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2020/nov/06/democrats-republicans-working-class-party-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more working-class voters}}}\uc2 , though they are scaled back compared to what progressive Democrats want.\par \par \uc2 One {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.romney.senate.gov/sites/default/files/2021-02/higher%20wages%20for%20american%20workers%20act_one%20pager.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plan}}}\uc2 , created by Republican senators \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  and Tom Cotton, would increase the minimum wage to $10 an hour by 2025 and include a crackdown on employers hiring undocumented workers. Another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hawley.senate.gov/hawley-announces-legislation-require-15-minimum-wage-billion-dollar-corporations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plan}}}\uc2 , from Republican senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , would increase the minimum wage to $15 for corporations who make more than $1bn a year.\par \par \uc2 Though it appears compromise could be made on an increased minimum wage that is lower than $15, progressive Democrats and advocates for a $15 minimum wage are refusing to budge to anything below that.\par \par \uc2 Progressive House Democrats, in an attempt to pressure their colleagues in the Senate to take on a $15 wage, have started to renew demands for legislation. On a recent call with the press, a dozen House Democrats, labor leaders and activists demanded that a $15 wage increase be passed by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Representative \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2 , who organized the call, said that Democrats can include the increase in must-pass legislation, such as the annual defense spending bill. Khanna, along with other progressive Democrats, have also advocated for overturning the parliamentarian to raise the minimum wage to $15 if it comes to it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[We\u8217\'20\'19re] making the case now that we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to be prepared to overturn the parliamentarian if it comes to that, and that we have to get it done,\u8221\'20\'1D Khanna said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis time we realized that we have to mobilize to make this clear months in advance, so it\u8217\'20\'19s not like we\u8217\'20\'19re doing this a week before the parliamentarian decision or right when the parliamentarian rules.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Khanna said the number of groups on the call demonstrates the widespread support for a $15 minimum wage in the Democratic party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere could be real disappointment if we don\u8217\'20\'19t get it this time,\u8221\'20\'1D Khanna said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Democratic party is unified around this in the House, among groups and, candidly, [among] the people who helped us win the election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210328eh3s000rt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
